1
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,083
- The food was delicious, sir.
- Thank you, sir.

2
00:01:25,291 --> 00:01:27,333
Mom, please wake Jeeva up.

3
00:01:27,916 --> 00:01:31,000
- He's getting late for school.
- Oh, so you're Tamilians?

4
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:33,791
Where are you from? Chennai?

5
00:01:34,916 --> 00:01:35,833
We're not from Chennai.

6
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:37,750
A town near Madurai.

7
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:40,250
You wouldn't know.

8
00:01:41,375 --> 00:01:43,083
Oh, you're from Madurai!

9
00:01:44,791 --> 00:01:48,500
Sir, isn't this one of Madurai's
most popular hotel chains?

10
00:01:48,791 --> 00:01:49,708
This is not the same.

11
00:01:51,041 --> 00:01:51,916
That's my name.

12
00:01:52,791 --> 00:01:54,166
I just added "Hotel" to my name.

13
00:01:54,916 --> 00:01:57,833
Oh, now I get it.
You dropped the "H" from "Hotel."

14
00:02:02,208 --> 00:02:05,500
Sir, is this your family?

15
00:02:09,125 --> 00:02:10,000
Yes.

16
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,083
This is my wife.

17
00:02:13,208 --> 00:02:15,458
Jeeva, you're getting late.
Hurry up and get ready.

18
00:02:23,041 --> 00:02:25,416
- Ma'am, do you have chutney?
- I'll get it.

19
00:02:26,458 --> 00:02:27,500
This is my brother-in-law.

20
00:02:27,583 --> 00:02:29,750
As in your wife's brother?

21
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:32,625
Yeah.

22
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:47,333
This is my mother-in-law.

23
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,333
Your son is very cute.

24
00:02:54,583 --> 00:02:55,458
What's his name?

25
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,875
Jeeva.

26
00:03:06,583 --> 00:03:08,583
But your son
did not take after his mother.

27
00:03:09,416 --> 00:03:10,583
He takes after you.

28
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:19,666
Instead of minding your own business
and having breakfast,

29
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:22,250
why would you cause chaos
early in the morning?

30
00:03:22,541 --> 00:03:24,791
Sir, why would you make such a remark?

31
00:03:25,708 --> 00:03:27,291
We already have too many problems
in the family.

32
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:29,541
- Please leave, Sir.
- Sorry, Sir!

33
00:03:29,833 --> 00:03:31,166
Okay, Sir, see you!

34
00:03:35,083 --> 00:03:37,875
<i>Bro! My dear, Bro!</i>

35
00:03:39,208 --> 00:03:42,000
<i>Bro! My dear, Bro!</i>

36
00:03:43,083 --> 00:03:47,125
<i>Even the victorious have fallen</i>

37
00:03:47,208 --> 00:03:51,083
<i>Many who failed still prevailed</i>

38
00:03:51,166 --> 00:03:54,000
<i>Bro! My dear, Bro!</i>

39
00:03:54,166 --> 00:03:56,291
Jeeva, whom do you like the most?
Mom or Dad?

40
00:03:57,875 --> 00:03:58,958
I like Mom!

41
00:04:01,958 --> 00:04:04,291
But I like my Dad more than her.

42
00:04:05,041 --> 00:04:06,666
Please don't rat me out to my Mom.

43
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:08,916
Because Mom and Dad are having problems.

44
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:09,875
I get it!

45
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:13,833
<i>Beyond winning and losing
Lies a single truth</i>

46
00:04:14,416 --> 00:04:16,458
- Bye, Grandma.
- Bye.

47
00:04:17,708 --> 00:04:19,125
- Dad!
- Yeah!

48
00:04:19,208 --> 00:04:22,916
Yesterday in school,
they conducted a running race.

49
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,416
- Yeah?
- My friend Prakash won the race.

50
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:29,291
The entire school cheered for him.

51
00:04:29,375 --> 00:04:30,666
Is that so? That's great!

52
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:33,458
When will I be able to participate
in a running race, Dad?

53
00:04:35,375 --> 00:04:36,333
Next year, my dear.

54
00:04:36,416 --> 00:04:37,833
Yay! Jolly!

55
00:04:39,833 --> 00:04:43,500
<i>What Bro? Why Bro?
That's how life rolls, Bro</i>

56
00:04:43,791 --> 00:04:47,333
<i>Me Bro, You Bro, Everybody Bro!</i>

57
00:04:47,416 --> 00:04:48,541
<i>My dear, Bro!</i>

58
00:05:01,833 --> 00:05:03,250
Jeeva, do well, okay!

59
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:04,416
All the best!

60
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:06,416
- Bye!
- Bye, Dad!

61
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:10,500
<i>Upon life's stage, all are actors</i>

62
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:13,000
<i>And must perform</i>

63
00:05:13,083 --> 00:05:14,291
<i>My dear, Bro!</i>

64
00:05:14,375 --> 00:05:18,166
<i>The creator of the stage
Reigns in imagination</i>

65
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,875
<i>At his command, all must yield</i>

66
00:05:20,958 --> 00:05:22,291
<i>My dear, Bro!</i>

67
00:05:22,375 --> 00:05:26,333
<i>Life is theater
Understand the script</i>

68
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:30,083
<i>Be perceptive,
And no role is beyond you</i>

69
00:05:30,458 --> 00:05:33,291
<i>Bro! My dear, Bro!</i>

70
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:37,291
<i>Bro! My dear, Bro!</i>

71
00:05:38,375 --> 00:05:42,125
<i>What Bro? Why Bro?
That's how life rolls, Bro</i>

72
00:05:42,375 --> 00:05:45,916
<i>Me Bro, You Bro, Everybody Bro!</i>

73
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,083
<i>My dear, Bro!</i>

74
00:05:48,541 --> 00:05:49,833
Brother, could you look after my shop?

75
00:05:49,916 --> 00:05:51,791
- I'll be back soon.
- Sure, make it fast.

76
00:05:54,958 --> 00:05:56,625
I reckon your father is late today, too.

77
00:05:56,708 --> 00:05:59,791
When he comes to get me, neither
am I going to talk to him nor go home.

78
00:05:59,875 --> 00:06:02,500
<i>Bro! My dear, Bro!</i>

79
00:06:03,875 --> 00:06:06,625
<i>Bro! My dear, Bro!</i>

80
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:14,750
Hello, is it happening?

81
00:06:16,583 --> 00:06:18,500
Hey, I'm not coming. You carry on.

82
00:06:19,541 --> 00:06:21,500
Hello, Sir. Late as usual.

83
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,333
Someone already took away Jeeva.

84
00:06:24,083 --> 00:06:25,083
Who took him away?

85
00:06:25,333 --> 00:06:27,625
- I just arrived.
- Yes, Sir. But you're late.

86
00:06:27,791 --> 00:06:29,791
So, his uncle came to pick him up.

87
00:06:30,208 --> 00:06:31,166
Which Uncle?

88
00:06:35,875 --> 00:06:37,083
How are you related to the boy?

89
00:06:37,291 --> 00:06:38,375
- I'm his father.
- Mother.

90
00:06:38,458 --> 00:06:39,625
- Grandma.
- Uncle.

91
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:41,750
- You guys are Tamil, are you?
- Yes, Sir!

92
00:06:41,833 --> 00:06:43,416
How could you be so irresponsible?

93
00:06:44,208 --> 00:06:46,416
Why would you arrive late
to pick up your son each day?

94
00:06:47,416 --> 00:06:48,291
Sorry, Sir!

95
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,541
It's my fault I was late.

96
00:06:52,416 --> 00:06:53,458
Fine, don't be afraid.

97
00:06:53,583 --> 00:06:56,375
We'll check the CCTV camera
and find out who took him.

98
00:07:03,833 --> 00:07:04,708
Sir,

99
00:07:05,333 --> 00:07:06,208
that's Jeeva.

100
00:07:07,416 --> 00:07:08,500
Sir, please fast forward.

101
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,625
Sir, you could spot his face in this clip.

102
00:07:12,208 --> 00:07:13,500
He took away your son.

103
00:07:47,958 --> 00:07:49,333
<i>- How dare you lie?
- Where is the money?</i>

104
00:07:49,416 --> 00:07:51,291
- How dare you con people?
- Would you repeat it?

105
00:07:51,375 --> 00:07:52,958
- Confess, damn it!
- I ought to!

106
00:07:53,041 --> 00:07:55,333
- How dare you mess in our locality?
- I'll skin you if you don't 'fess up.

107
00:07:55,416 --> 00:07:57,625
- I won't spare you!
- Don't you dare attempt this again.

108
00:07:57,708 --> 00:07:59,208
{\an8}I ought to!

109
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,750
{\an8}- Open your mouth, and confess!
- Oh no!

110
00:08:02,916 --> 00:08:04,208
- I said, confess!
- More beatings will make him talk.

111
00:08:04,375 --> 00:08:05,291
Bloody arrogant people.

112
00:08:05,375 --> 00:08:06,458
Who are these people?

113
00:08:07,041 --> 00:08:10,333
This couple conned people
out of their money in Laxmi Nagar.

114
00:08:10,416 --> 00:08:12,708
- They got caught.
- Why did you guys get caught?

115
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
What happened to you guys?

116
00:08:25,875 --> 00:08:27,041
Why do you have casts on?

117
00:08:27,125 --> 00:08:29,458
Last night I slipped and fell
in the bathroom.

118
00:08:29,541 --> 00:08:31,791
- That's why I'm in a cast.
- What happened to you?

119
00:08:32,375 --> 00:08:33,833
Did you both go to the bathroom together?

120
00:08:37,875 --> 00:08:39,666
{\an8}COUPLE ARRESTED FOR FRAUD
IN MANGALAPURAM, CHENNAI!

121
00:08:43,375 --> 00:08:44,791
SUDHA HOUSE

122
00:09:04,541 --> 00:09:06,083
How dare you reject my call?

123
00:09:06,416 --> 00:09:07,833
I'll teach you a lesson
when I get a hold of you.

124
00:09:24,208 --> 00:09:25,166
Chutti Anna, one Dosa, quick.

125
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:27,000
Saravana, the cook, has stepped out.

126
00:09:27,083 --> 00:09:28,041
Could you please wait for 15 minutes?

127
00:09:28,791 --> 00:09:29,666
5 minutes?

128
00:09:52,083 --> 00:09:53,083
Okay, sir.

129
00:09:53,583 --> 00:09:54,833
- Chutti Anna!
- Hi, Sadha.

130
00:09:54,916 --> 00:09:56,250
Please check how much I owe you.

131
00:09:57,250 --> 00:09:58,958
1,240 rupees.

132
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:01,666
- Here's 1,000. I'll pay the balance later.
- Sure!

133
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:04,416
How much?

134
00:10:07,708 --> 00:10:08,958
- Chutti Anna!
- Tell me.

135
00:10:09,041 --> 00:10:10,833
I have a plan called <i>Quick Money.</i>

136
00:10:11,166 --> 00:10:12,083
Would you like to invest in it?

137
00:10:12,416 --> 00:10:13,916
What is Quick Money?

138
00:10:14,291 --> 00:10:15,541
Aren't you aware of it?

139
00:10:15,625 --> 00:10:17,291
You start making a profit
the instant you invest in it.

140
00:10:17,375 --> 00:10:19,291
- That's Quick Money.
- Instant profit?

141
00:10:19,541 --> 00:10:22,666
- How does it work?
- Making a quick buck won't last.

142
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:24,416
Pay the bill and be on your way.

143
00:10:26,625 --> 00:10:27,500
Please leave, Sir.

144
00:10:28,333 --> 00:10:29,958
Hey, what does the board say?

145
00:10:31,541 --> 00:10:34,291
It says, "Do not discuss politics and
business here with the customers."

146
00:10:34,375 --> 00:10:35,250
Chutti Anna!

147
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:36,541
It says not to discuss with the customers.

148
00:10:36,625 --> 00:10:38,166
- Yes!
- But I'm speaking to the owner.

149
00:10:41,458 --> 00:10:43,125
- Hi!
- Hello!

150
00:10:43,208 --> 00:10:45,208
- Couldn't find a customer yet?
- No luck!

151
00:10:45,291 --> 00:10:48,166
At present, everyone has become smart.
So, it's tough.

152
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:50,583
Forget about me.
Did you settle your issues?

153
00:10:51,666 --> 00:10:53,541
Not yet. Problems still exist.

154
00:10:54,083 --> 00:10:55,208
Don't worry.
Everything will be fine.

155
00:10:55,916 --> 00:10:56,791
It should be fine.

156
00:10:58,041 --> 00:10:59,083
Or I should make it fine.

157
00:11:15,833 --> 00:11:16,708
Why are you troubling yourself?

158
00:11:16,791 --> 00:11:18,583
Please give me your card.
I'll pay and bring it back to your house.

159
00:11:18,666 --> 00:11:21,041
- Is the AC voltage in summer low?
- Yes, sir!

160
00:11:21,541 --> 00:11:23,625
- But it works well in the rainy season.
- Yes, sir.

161
00:11:23,708 --> 00:11:25,125
It doesn't work well when needed.

162
00:11:25,208 --> 00:11:26,416
When we don't need it,
it works well.

163
00:11:26,708 --> 00:11:28,750
{\an8}- Do you live on Lal Bahadur Street?
- Yes, sir.

164
00:11:28,833 --> 00:11:29,958
{\an8}I, too, live on the same street.

165
00:11:30,666 --> 00:11:32,000
{\an8}I am facing the same issue at home.

166
00:11:33,041 --> 00:11:35,166
Don't worry. We'll fix it.

167
00:11:35,541 --> 00:11:36,458
Have faith.

168
00:11:37,166 --> 00:11:38,041
Venkatachalam!

169
00:11:39,916 --> 00:11:40,791
Good morning, Sir.

170
00:11:42,750 --> 00:11:44,041
Hey, don't push me around.

171
00:11:44,375 --> 00:11:45,833
Step aside.
Don't step on my toes.

172
00:11:46,291 --> 00:11:47,166
I ought to!

173
00:11:47,791 --> 00:11:49,333
Hey! Hey! Move, woman!

174
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:52,500
Hey, it's the ladies' queue.
Move to the other queue.

175
00:11:52,583 --> 00:11:55,291
My question exactly.
What are you doing in the ladies' queue?

176
00:11:56,166 --> 00:11:57,500
Early drinker, you are.

177
00:11:57,583 --> 00:12:00,291
Don't piss me off.
I'll close the counter.

178
00:12:00,416 --> 00:12:03,000
- Hey, there's an emergency at home.
- I said to switch the queue.

179
00:12:03,416 --> 00:12:05,833
- Hi, sir. Good morning.
- Hi, Saravana.

180
00:12:06,375 --> 00:12:08,833
My wife has an appointment
with the doctor.

181
00:12:08,916 --> 00:12:10,625
Also, I have to
drop my car off for service.

182
00:12:10,708 --> 00:12:12,291
There's too much of a crowd for billing.

183
00:12:12,375 --> 00:12:14,500
Could you please open your counter?

184
00:12:14,583 --> 00:12:15,458
- Okay, sir.
- Great!

185
00:12:17,916 --> 00:12:20,333
Dear consumers, the other counter is open.

186
00:12:20,416 --> 00:12:21,416
- Switch to it.
- Hey, where are you going?

187
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,375
- I've been waiting for a long time.
- Hey, switch to the other counter.

188
00:12:55,250 --> 00:12:56,250
Are you able to hear the heartbeat?

189
00:12:58,125 --> 00:13:00,125
Only during the 3rd-month scan
would you get a clear picture.

190
00:13:00,375 --> 00:13:02,208
So, don't forget to come for a check-up.

191
00:13:02,708 --> 00:13:05,625
Also, have your food and tablets on time.

192
00:13:05,708 --> 00:13:09,166
During this period, you and the child
should be extra careful.

193
00:13:09,250 --> 00:13:10,125
Okay.

194
00:13:10,708 --> 00:13:11,791
Didn't your husband come with you?

195
00:13:35,583 --> 00:13:38,208
Hello! Who are you, people?
This is my house.

196
00:13:38,416 --> 00:13:39,875
Why are you bringing my stuff outside?

197
00:13:39,958 --> 00:13:40,916
We don't know anything.

198
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,291
The house owner is inside.
Speak to him.

199
00:13:43,791 --> 00:13:45,708
- Hurry up. Take everything outside.
- Hey, who are you?

200
00:13:46,166 --> 00:13:48,833
Finally, you made it.
I've been waiting for a long time.

201
00:13:48,916 --> 00:13:51,375
Hello, first, tell me who you are?
And how did you get in?

202
00:13:51,833 --> 00:13:53,250
Why did you break my lock?

203
00:13:53,333 --> 00:13:55,208
Listen, I'm the owner of this house.

204
00:13:55,750 --> 00:13:58,166
I reckon you rented this house
through <i>Right Choice Properties.</i>

205
00:13:58,250 --> 00:14:01,083
Sir, I leased the house
for three lakh rupees.

206
00:14:01,166 --> 00:14:03,041
What?
You paid three lakh rupees for the lease?

207
00:14:03,375 --> 00:14:05,375
They have swindled your money.

208
00:14:05,458 --> 00:14:06,958
That's a fraudulent company.

209
00:14:07,166 --> 00:14:08,583
They haven't paid me two months' rent yet.

210
00:14:08,958 --> 00:14:11,291
Find out where they are and
file a complaint with the Police.

211
00:14:11,791 --> 00:14:13,333
This is the <i>rental agreement</i> they gave me.

212
00:14:13,416 --> 00:14:15,458
How do you expect me to find them
or get them arrested?

213
00:14:16,375 --> 00:14:18,208
Hey, hurry up and remove things.

214
00:14:18,291 --> 00:14:19,416
- It's getting late.
- Yes.

215
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:21,416
Stop thinking
and find a way out of this.

216
00:14:32,750 --> 00:14:33,958
<i>It's a fraudulent company.</i>

217
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:36,208
<i>It's been two months since they closed.</i>

218
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:39,375
<i>They mentioned to the owners
that they're renting the house...</i>

219
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:42,291
And swindled money from people
like you and evaded the town.

220
00:14:43,916 --> 00:14:46,583
<i>I grew up in an Orphanage in Kerala.</i>

221
00:14:46,666 --> 00:14:48,875
<i>I am an orphan.</i>

222
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,541
<i>I don't have a stable income.</i>

223
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:54,750
<i>I thought leasing a house wouldn't mean
paying rent every month...</i>

224
00:14:54,833 --> 00:14:57,916
<i>So, I borrowed money, sold some jewels,</i>

225
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,166
<i>and took out a lease on that house.</i>

226
00:14:59,250 --> 00:15:02,375
<i>But I never expected they would con me.</i>

227
00:15:02,625 --> 00:15:04,708
If I could stay one day here...

228
00:15:05,458 --> 00:15:07,166
I hope it won't be a problem for you.

229
00:15:07,666 --> 00:15:09,750
If it's only for a day,

230
00:15:10,250 --> 00:15:11,666
we have no issues.

231
00:15:11,750 --> 00:15:13,750
Yes, only for a day.

232
00:15:14,291 --> 00:15:16,000
I'm already looking for a place to stay.

233
00:15:16,458 --> 00:15:17,500
I'll leave tomorrow.

234
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:20,458
Okay. Please make yourself comfortable.

235
00:15:20,708 --> 00:15:21,625
Thank you.

236
00:15:30,083 --> 00:15:31,958
<i>As per the scenario you mentioned,</i>

237
00:15:32,208 --> 00:15:34,291
it sounds very critical, Subramani.

238
00:15:34,416 --> 00:15:35,791
Yes, Doctor. I understand.

239
00:15:36,250 --> 00:15:37,250
I'll speak to them, Doctor.

240
00:15:38,666 --> 00:15:39,541
Sure, Doctor.

241
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:45,375
{\an8}Immediately, we must perform
a major surgery on her.

242
00:15:45,458 --> 00:15:46,916
Her health condition is very bad.

243
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,458
{\an8}This surgery is very critical.

244
00:15:48,875 --> 00:15:49,750
{\an8}It's impossible to perform.

245
00:15:50,083 --> 00:15:52,375
{\an8}But we have no choice but to perform.

246
00:15:52,458 --> 00:15:54,541
Sir, I don't understand.

247
00:15:55,291 --> 00:15:56,666
Is it possible
to perform the surgery or not?

248
00:15:56,750 --> 00:15:59,333
{\an8}Like I mentioned.
Her health condition is very bad.

249
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,583
This surgery is very critical.
It's impossible to perform.

250
00:16:01,708 --> 00:16:03,666
{\an8}But we have no choice but to perform.

251
00:16:03,833 --> 00:16:07,041
Hey, I don't understand what he's saying.

252
00:16:07,833 --> 00:16:09,416
There's nothing wrong with me.

253
00:16:09,541 --> 00:16:11,291
{\an8}I am doing well, though.
Let's go home.

254
00:16:11,375 --> 00:16:13,166
Mom, please shut up.

255
00:16:14,041 --> 00:16:15,916
Sir, please explain it clearly.

256
00:16:16,083 --> 00:16:17,583
There's a tumor on her lungs.

257
00:16:18,166 --> 00:16:19,625
It has crossed Stage 3 now.

258
00:16:19,708 --> 00:16:22,916
It's better for her
if we perform the surgery immediately.

259
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,416
It would cost you a lot of money.

260
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,000
Do you have insurance?

261
00:16:26,208 --> 00:16:28,208
How are you placed financially?

262
00:16:29,125 --> 00:16:30,416
We don't have any insurance.

263
00:16:31,625 --> 00:16:32,708
How much would the surgery cost?

264
00:16:33,708 --> 00:16:36,083
Approximately seven to eight lakhs.

265
00:16:38,083 --> 00:16:39,916
The sooner we perform the surgery,

266
00:16:40,208 --> 00:16:41,875
the greater the possibility of curing it.

267
00:16:41,958 --> 00:16:43,125
If you happen to delay it...

268
00:16:43,708 --> 00:16:45,541
I can't guarantee
how long she will be alive.

269
00:16:45,750 --> 00:16:47,500
Please take this
as a very serious warning.

270
00:16:55,625 --> 00:16:57,083
<i>I wish to become a Hero.</i>

271
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,250
<i>My mother used to say this all the time.</i>

272
00:16:59,333 --> 00:17:02,291
<i>So, what if no one produced your film?
We'll produce it ourselves.</i>

273
00:17:02,375 --> 00:17:05,666
{\an8}<i>Because his father, Rambo Selvaraj,
was a renowned stunt master in cinema.</i>

274
00:17:05,791 --> 00:17:08,083
<i>Moreover, he has done
a lot of good deeds during his time.</i>

275
00:17:08,416 --> 00:17:11,541
<i>My mother said that mentioning
his name is enough to raise funds.</i>

276
00:17:12,833 --> 00:17:15,583
You're asking at the wrong time.
But I'm ready to give my life, though.

277
00:17:15,666 --> 00:17:18,250
I need 8 lakh rupees to save my mother.

278
00:17:18,333 --> 00:17:19,250
I don't have any money.

279
00:17:19,333 --> 00:17:21,250
I'm already in a huge debt.

280
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:23,833
Jacky, your father allotted this place
under the trust.

281
00:17:23,916 --> 00:17:25,375
You can't sell or mortgage it.

282
00:17:25,458 --> 00:17:26,625
You can use it until it lasts.

283
00:17:26,916 --> 00:17:28,625
<i>Now, when I'm reaching out
to raise funds for Mom's surgery,</i>

284
00:17:28,791 --> 00:17:30,041
<i>no one's helping me out.</i>

285
00:17:31,333 --> 00:17:34,250
In this situation,
producing a film is not possible.

286
00:17:34,916 --> 00:17:37,291
You may use the same story
to direct another Hero.

287
00:17:37,375 --> 00:17:39,000
I wrote this script with you in mind.

288
00:17:39,166 --> 00:17:41,000
I cannot cast another Hero
to make this film.

289
00:17:41,083 --> 00:17:43,125
No matter how long it takes,
I'll wait for you.

290
00:17:43,791 --> 00:17:45,500
First, resolve your issues.

291
00:17:47,666 --> 00:17:51,291
I thought mentioning his name
would help raise funds to make a film.

292
00:17:52,625 --> 00:17:55,500
I told them you're going to die,
yet no one helped me out.

293
00:17:56,958 --> 00:18:00,708
In the name of doing good deeds,
he left us in peril.

294
00:18:00,833 --> 00:18:03,041
Not one soul did he help
is helping us now.

295
00:18:03,166 --> 00:18:05,250
People forget the help
they received recently.

296
00:18:05,375 --> 00:18:06,625
That's the way of life.

297
00:18:06,791 --> 00:18:08,041
Don't torment yourself.

298
00:18:08,125 --> 00:18:10,500
Nothing is wrong with me.
I'm doing well.

299
00:18:10,875 --> 00:18:12,000
When Dad was ill...

300
00:18:12,666 --> 00:18:15,333
he, too, kept saying
nothing was wrong with him,

301
00:18:15,916 --> 00:18:17,166
and in the end, he passed away.

302
00:18:18,250 --> 00:18:20,166
But this time I'm not giving up on you.

303
00:18:22,166 --> 00:18:24,166
If you're gone,
I don't have anyone else.

304
00:18:36,458 --> 00:18:39,083
Hey, why are you crying like a child?

305
00:18:39,166 --> 00:18:40,291
Don't worry. We'll overcome it.

306
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:48,208
Listen, no one can change fate.

307
00:19:03,041 --> 00:19:05,166
Nothing is wrong with me.
Let it go.

308
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:16,833
Hey, don't you see I'm rejecting the call?

309
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Why would you keep calling?

310
00:19:18,791 --> 00:19:20,541
Hey, Dad found out about our relationship.

311
00:19:21,166 --> 00:19:22,041
Are you serious?

312
00:19:24,708 --> 00:19:25,791
Who's this boy?

313
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:28,083
His name is Saravana.

314
00:19:29,250 --> 00:19:30,916
We've been in a relationship
since college.

315
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,375
He's in a secure government job,
and he owns a house.

316
00:19:33,708 --> 00:19:34,875
He's a very good boy.

317
00:19:36,083 --> 00:19:36,958
Are you sure?

318
00:19:38,833 --> 00:19:39,708
Okay!

319
00:19:40,083 --> 00:19:42,541
Latha, let's meet the boy.

320
00:19:43,708 --> 00:19:45,333
My Dad wants to meet you right away.

321
00:19:45,416 --> 00:19:46,916
We'll come to your house shortly.

322
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
I'm at the office.

323
00:19:48,583 --> 00:19:49,958
- So what?
- I mean...

324
00:19:51,041 --> 00:19:52,208
Some place near my office...

325
00:19:53,291 --> 00:19:54,458
Why don't we meet at a restaurant?

326
00:19:54,541 --> 00:19:56,125
It's a big deal that
he agreed to meet you.

327
00:19:56,208 --> 00:19:57,791
You'd better get home right away.

328
00:19:57,875 --> 00:19:59,625
For God's sake,
please keep the house clean.

329
00:20:01,125 --> 00:20:02,083
<i>"Keep the house clean."</i>

330
00:20:03,125 --> 00:20:04,000
<i>"Keep the house clean."</i>

331
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:17,291
<i>For God's sake,
please keep the house clean.</i>

332
00:21:26,666 --> 00:21:29,208
So, Saravanan,
what do you do for a living?

333
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:31,125
I work at the EB office, Uncle.

334
00:21:32,041 --> 00:21:33,916
Actually,
I'm not very interested in this job.

335
00:21:34,791 --> 00:21:37,708
After my mother's demise,
I had to take up a job.

336
00:21:37,833 --> 00:21:38,916
So, I am continuing it.

337
00:21:40,583 --> 00:21:42,375
Actually, I want to become
an entrepreneur, Uncle.

338
00:21:43,416 --> 00:21:44,500
I want to do something Big!

339
00:21:45,375 --> 00:21:46,708
Like, I want to launch my own brand.

340
00:21:47,916 --> 00:21:51,083
I want to launch a new product in
the market and make it successful.

341
00:21:51,541 --> 00:21:53,583
I want to become
a successful businessman like you.

342
00:21:55,666 --> 00:21:56,833
I will make it happen soon.

343
00:22:01,250 --> 00:22:02,125
One minute.

344
00:22:04,291 --> 00:22:06,458
Hey, why the heck
don't you answer my calls?

345
00:22:06,541 --> 00:22:08,541
- Sir!
- Do I look like a moron to you?

346
00:22:08,625 --> 00:22:10,416
Sir, I'm sorry.
Let's step outside and talk.

347
00:22:10,500 --> 00:22:11,375
I won't!

348
00:22:11,875 --> 00:22:14,166
Your house is always locked.
And you don't answer my calls.

349
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,041
You don't pay your EMI, either.

350
00:22:16,375 --> 00:22:18,291
Do you think
I won't reach you at your workplace?

351
00:22:18,375 --> 00:22:20,541
I called you many times.
But you never answered.

352
00:22:20,625 --> 00:22:21,666
I will stand right here and talk.

353
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:23,916
Sir! Sorry, Sir.

354
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,791
I've been paying EMIs
for the past five years.

355
00:22:27,416 --> 00:22:31,041
The loan principal has not come down,
and the interest is exorbitant.

356
00:22:31,125 --> 00:22:33,000
How would I even manage?
It's not fair.

357
00:22:33,083 --> 00:22:35,541
You should've thought about it before
taking out a loan from a private firm.

358
00:22:36,666 --> 00:22:39,416
Yeah! My mother made a mistake.

359
00:22:40,416 --> 00:22:41,666
I can't pay anymore.

360
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:44,125
I'll file a complaint with the Police.
You may leave.

361
00:22:44,208 --> 00:22:46,750
Oh, really?
Go ahead and file a complaint.

362
00:22:46,875 --> 00:22:48,583
They can't do anything to me.

363
00:22:48,666 --> 00:22:50,666
If you don't pay your EMI on time,

364
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:52,875
wait and watch what I do to you!

365
00:23:02,791 --> 00:23:03,708
Dad.

366
00:23:04,958 --> 00:23:05,875
He's a...

367
00:23:06,833 --> 00:23:07,708
...good guy, Dad.

368
00:23:07,791 --> 00:23:09,458
He cheated and lied to you.

369
00:23:11,125 --> 00:23:12,208
I did a background check.

370
00:23:13,583 --> 00:23:15,166
<i>He has borrowed money all over town.</i>

371
00:23:20,250 --> 00:23:21,125
<i>Saravana!</i>

372
00:23:23,291 --> 00:23:24,250
<i>Saravana!</i>

373
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:38,375
Mom!

374
00:23:39,375 --> 00:23:41,666
Why take a big loan to build this house?

375
00:23:45,166 --> 00:23:48,458
Do you think this is
an ordinary house that anyone can build?

376
00:23:52,250 --> 00:23:54,083
After your father's demise,

377
00:23:54,750 --> 00:23:58,666
we struggled for months
to find a roof over our heads.

378
00:24:01,708 --> 00:24:03,041
There was a time when we didn't
have a permanent address

379
00:24:05,083 --> 00:24:08,375
and paid rent and provided address proof
to live in strangers' houses.

380
00:24:10,791 --> 00:24:14,250
There was a period
when my only desire was

381
00:24:15,416 --> 00:24:17,458
to find a good house to rent.

382
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:21,125
But I never found one.

383
00:24:23,666 --> 00:24:25,166
Every day after I finish work...

384
00:24:26,416 --> 00:24:28,500
never have I slept peacefully.

385
00:24:31,541 --> 00:24:32,458
I had a wish, though.

386
00:24:33,500 --> 00:24:37,500
Something of our own,
scaling from earth to sky,

387
00:24:38,041 --> 00:24:39,958
I wish to build a house of our own.

388
00:24:41,458 --> 00:24:42,625
Finally, my wish came true.

389
00:24:45,625 --> 00:24:49,125
Saravana, I'm going to sleep
peacefully tonight.

390
00:25:05,041 --> 00:25:09,333
<i>We run and seek
Only to live</i>

391
00:25:10,208 --> 00:25:12,583
<i>Only to exist?</i>

392
00:25:13,083 --> 00:25:15,583
<i>We're all human, aren't we?</i>

393
00:25:17,250 --> 00:25:19,541
<i>Will it change one day?</i>

394
00:25:20,083 --> 00:25:22,666
<i>Will this ever change?</i>

395
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:26,166
<i>Will these scars ever heal?</i>

396
00:25:26,333 --> 00:25:29,833
<i>Will new paths emerge?</i>

397
00:25:30,458 --> 00:25:32,833
There's something called Ruby Coin.
Everything will be digital money.

398
00:25:32,916 --> 00:25:34,875
It's not the same
as chump change we carry.

399
00:25:34,958 --> 00:25:37,125
In the future,
physical currency won't exist.

400
00:25:37,208 --> 00:25:39,000
- Hey! Hey!
- It's red in color and...

401
00:25:40,458 --> 00:25:41,916
- I have a scheme called Quick Money.
- Quick Money?

402
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:43,333
- I have a scheme called Quick Money.
- Quick Money?

403
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:44,583
I have a scheme called Quick Money.

404
00:25:44,666 --> 00:25:46,000
Did you say, Rukmani?

405
00:25:46,791 --> 00:25:47,875
No, I meant Padmini.

406
00:25:47,958 --> 00:25:49,041
No use in explaining it to you.

407
00:25:49,958 --> 00:25:51,416
I don't understand a word.
Get lost!

408
00:26:10,125 --> 00:26:11,000
Saravana!

409
00:26:11,958 --> 00:26:14,250
Do you know why I like you very much?

410
00:26:14,333 --> 00:26:15,750
It's because of your mother.

411
00:26:15,833 --> 00:26:18,083
The respect you hold for your mother.

412
00:26:18,291 --> 00:26:20,958
I really miss her a lot.

413
00:26:21,041 --> 00:26:25,125
In my service,
I never came across such a woman.

414
00:26:29,666 --> 00:26:30,875
- Is it a photo or a video?
- Video.

415
00:26:30,958 --> 00:26:31,833
Okay, wait.

416
00:26:32,250 --> 00:26:33,125
- Go ahead!
- Record now.

417
00:26:33,208 --> 00:26:34,250
Watch, I'm going to expose you.

418
00:26:34,333 --> 00:26:35,625
Okay? Now, get out!

419
00:26:36,125 --> 00:26:37,833
Don't worry. We'll fix it.

420
00:26:38,333 --> 00:26:39,250
Have faith.

421
00:26:39,375 --> 00:26:40,250
Oh, super!

422
00:26:41,458 --> 00:26:42,875
Sir, I'm here to pay the electricity bill.

423
00:26:42,958 --> 00:26:45,458
Electricity is down.
Come back later.

424
00:26:45,541 --> 00:26:46,750
Is electricity down?

425
00:26:47,125 --> 00:26:48,166
Isn't this the Electricity Board?

426
00:26:48,250 --> 00:26:50,375
Hey, it's not like the EB office
runs on batteries.

427
00:26:50,458 --> 00:26:51,333
Get lost!

428
00:26:55,416 --> 00:26:57,000
{\an8}Don't you people have any sense?

429
00:26:57,083 --> 00:26:59,166
{\an8}The system is down.
Move to the next counter.

430
00:26:59,250 --> 00:27:00,541
{\an8}It's an old card. Get lost!

431
00:27:00,625 --> 00:27:02,375
{\an8}Do you know my experience in this field?

432
00:27:02,458 --> 00:27:04,125
{\an8}You weren't even born then.
Get out of here.

433
00:27:04,208 --> 00:27:05,083
{\an8}Closed!

434
00:27:05,166 --> 00:27:06,625
Udipi coffee!

435
00:27:07,416 --> 00:27:09,250
Amsavalli!

436
00:27:09,500 --> 00:27:11,208
{\an8}I think I'm getting a migraine.

437
00:27:11,291 --> 00:27:13,166
{\an8}I'll consult with a doctor and return.

438
00:27:13,500 --> 00:27:15,541
{\an8}Check what the hell the problem is.
I'm leaving!

439
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:18,375
{\an8}Sir, shall I give 10,000 to Saravanan,
as you mentioned over the call?

440
00:27:18,458 --> 00:27:19,625
When did I tell you?

441
00:27:19,708 --> 00:27:21,666
Just because no one lent him money.

442
00:27:21,750 --> 00:27:23,041
He mimicked your voice
and asked for the money.

443
00:27:23,125 --> 00:27:24,000
Oh!

444
00:27:24,083 --> 00:27:26,166
Saravana, is it true?

445
00:27:26,958 --> 00:27:27,833
Sorry, sir.

446
00:27:27,916 --> 00:27:29,041
I didn't hear you.
Come again.

447
00:27:29,291 --> 00:27:31,583
I didn't have another option, sir.

448
00:27:31,666 --> 00:27:33,291
You're not like your mother.

449
00:27:33,375 --> 00:27:34,791
I'm taking back my word.

450
00:27:34,875 --> 00:27:36,916
Just because I like you very much.

451
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:39,250
Don't do this.
It looks bad, man.

452
00:27:40,458 --> 00:27:41,791
But his voice was better than yours.

453
00:27:41,875 --> 00:27:43,500
Hey, get out of here!

454
00:27:43,916 --> 00:27:44,958
Idiot!

455
00:27:45,208 --> 00:27:51,125
<i>Who grants pain
And claims life in return?</i>

456
00:27:51,541 --> 00:27:57,875
<i>When the spectacle ends,
He seeks another</i>

457
00:27:58,291 --> 00:28:00,250
{\an8}<i>We run and seek...</i>

458
00:28:00,333 --> 00:28:02,500
No matter how educated you people are,
you're still stupid.

459
00:28:02,916 --> 00:28:04,583
It's easy to take a loan.

460
00:28:04,916 --> 00:28:08,291
But taking another loan is difficult.

461
00:28:08,458 --> 00:28:12,083
If you want to lease a property,
the property owner has to sign it.

462
00:28:12,166 --> 00:28:13,458
Instead of taking a loan
from the Government...

463
00:28:13,541 --> 00:28:16,458
he took a loan from a private firm
because the processing time was less.

464
00:28:16,541 --> 00:28:17,458
In my opinion...

465
00:28:17,958 --> 00:28:21,458
getting cheated is the biggest sin
than cheating.

466
00:28:22,250 --> 00:28:24,583
If we publish this in the media,
it'll backfire on you.

467
00:28:25,416 --> 00:28:27,291
They're private finance firms.

468
00:28:27,541 --> 00:28:30,500
Don't create any problems.
Handle them smoothly in another way.

469
00:28:30,583 --> 00:28:34,625
Buddy, I'd love to take on any work
to earn some extra income.

470
00:28:34,708 --> 00:28:35,833
You want to work for my father?

471
00:28:35,958 --> 00:28:38,291
Just because he was being nice
doesn't mean he's a good man.

472
00:28:38,500 --> 00:28:39,833
He's a cunning man!

473
00:28:40,125 --> 00:28:41,041
Hey, guys!

474
00:28:42,166 --> 00:28:45,333
- Hi, Rithi.
- I got beer, and everything is ready.

475
00:28:45,416 --> 00:28:47,625
We're heading straight to the drive-in
theater to watch the movie <i>Rockstar.</i>

476
00:28:47,958 --> 00:28:49,333
No, I'm not coming.

477
00:28:49,583 --> 00:28:52,208
- You guys carry on.
- Here, take this 25,000 rupees.

478
00:28:52,416 --> 00:28:54,583
Use it to pay this month's EMI.
We'll find a solution soon.

479
00:28:54,958 --> 00:28:56,291
Buddy, no thanks!

480
00:28:56,666 --> 00:28:58,125
You have been helping me every month.

481
00:28:59,458 --> 00:29:01,458
I'm feeling awkward about
taking more money from you.

482
00:29:02,750 --> 00:29:05,208
<i>Will it change one day?</i>

483
00:29:05,333 --> 00:29:08,875
<i>Will this ever change?</i>

484
00:29:08,958 --> 00:29:11,583
<i>Will these scars ever heal?</i>

485
00:29:11,666 --> 00:29:14,541
<i>Will new paths emerge?</i>

486
00:29:14,750 --> 00:29:17,416
<i>Will this phase never end?</i>

487
00:29:19,291 --> 00:29:21,625
{\an8}Following repeated allegations
of custodial brutality

488
00:29:21,708 --> 00:29:24,958
{\an8}against Inspector Kalyana Sundaram
of Mangalapuram Police Station...

489
00:29:25,166 --> 00:29:29,000
<i>So, the Human Rights Commission
has ordered an inquiry into him.</i>

490
00:29:29,083 --> 00:29:31,666
<i>Let's hear what the people of Mangalapuram
have to say about him.</i>

491
00:29:31,750 --> 00:29:34,666
{\an8}In our area, he's famously known
as Pulp-cane Kalyana Sundaram.

492
00:29:34,750 --> 00:29:37,416
He uses a huge cane
to beat the accused to a pulp.

493
00:29:37,500 --> 00:29:39,166
{\an8}He's beating only the people
who commit crimes.

494
00:29:39,250 --> 00:29:41,208
{\an8}There's a court to pass a verdict.

495
00:29:41,291 --> 00:29:42,416
{\an8}Who gave him the right to beat up people?

496
00:29:42,500 --> 00:29:45,166
{\an8}Only after he got posted here.
This is when this area is crime-free.

497
00:29:45,250 --> 00:29:48,208
{\an8}Even if we gather in groups to chatter,
he beats us to a pulp.

498
00:29:48,291 --> 00:29:52,250
{\an8}It's because of Kalyana Sundaram, Sir,
my son reformed and is going to work now.

499
00:29:52,333 --> 00:29:53,625
{\an8}I packed lunch and am heading to work.

500
00:29:53,708 --> 00:29:56,125
{\an8}In my opinion,
Kalyana Sundaram is a great man.

501
00:29:57,625 --> 00:29:58,916
I'm sure he was aware.

502
00:29:59,375 --> 00:30:02,083
{\an8}He knew that he was my brother-in-law,
yet he beat him up.

503
00:30:02,333 --> 00:30:04,416
I'm aware that he's your brother-in-law.
But he's new here.

504
00:30:04,500 --> 00:30:06,166
I'll make sure there are no conflicts
as we move forward.

505
00:30:06,250 --> 00:30:07,791
Let's set aside differences
and compromise.

506
00:30:16,958 --> 00:30:17,875
Saravana!

507
00:30:18,166 --> 00:30:22,166
Here is the money and the EB cards
of my 12 businesses.

508
00:30:22,333 --> 00:30:23,375
Please pay the electricity bill.

509
00:30:23,458 --> 00:30:25,958
There are still 20 days until
the due date. Why the hurry?

510
00:30:26,041 --> 00:30:28,166
On the due date,
most people run out of money.

511
00:30:28,250 --> 00:30:29,375
So, it's best to pay early.

512
00:30:29,458 --> 00:30:31,291
- Please pay the bill.
- Sure, I'll pay it.

513
00:30:38,333 --> 00:30:39,333
- Sir!
- Huh?

514
00:30:39,708 --> 00:30:41,541
My electricity bill is quite high, sir.

515
00:30:42,250 --> 00:30:43,583
Are you married?

516
00:30:44,208 --> 00:30:45,083
Yes, sir.

517
00:30:45,208 --> 00:30:47,125
Ask your wife.
She'll explain it to you.

518
00:30:47,208 --> 00:30:48,625
Sure, sir. I'll check with her.

519
00:30:48,708 --> 00:30:51,166
I like him. Very genuine guy.

520
00:30:51,250 --> 00:30:52,791
- Sir!
- Yeah.

521
00:30:53,250 --> 00:30:54,708
Sir, I'm not married.

522
00:30:54,958 --> 00:30:56,416
Still, my electricity bill is high.

523
00:30:56,791 --> 00:30:58,000
Holy shit!

524
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,291
Please come closer.

525
00:31:01,833 --> 00:31:05,416
If you don't mind,
shall I arrange a wife for you?

526
00:31:05,958 --> 00:31:06,916
Shameless creatures!

527
00:31:07,666 --> 00:31:11,083
{\an8}In my experience,
I've never seen such cheap people.

528
00:31:11,166 --> 00:31:12,041
{\an8}Closed!

529
00:31:24,541 --> 00:31:27,375
EMI payment?
Wait for five minutes, I'll be out.

530
00:31:31,041 --> 00:31:34,083
Sir, here is the money and EB cards
for five houses. Please pay the bill.

531
00:31:40,666 --> 00:31:43,250
<i>Here is the money and the EB cards
of my 12 businesses.</i>

532
00:31:43,416 --> 00:31:44,458
<i>Please pay the electricity bill.</i>

533
00:31:44,541 --> 00:31:47,000
<i>There are still 20 days until
the due date. Why the hurry?</i>

534
00:31:47,083 --> 00:31:49,166
<i>On the due date,
most people run out of money.</i>

535
00:31:49,250 --> 00:31:50,291
<i>So, it's best to pay early.</i>

536
00:31:50,375 --> 00:31:51,333
<i>Please pay the bill.</i>

537
00:31:54,333 --> 00:31:55,416
Sir, please wait for five minutes.
I'll be back.

538
00:32:04,458 --> 00:32:05,750
This is one month's EMI.

539
00:32:09,125 --> 00:32:10,458
Please adjust and get me an extension.

540
00:32:11,291 --> 00:32:12,750
I'll clear everything then.

541
00:32:20,916 --> 00:32:22,791
<i>If you don't pay your EMI in a day,</i>

542
00:32:22,875 --> 00:32:24,875
<i>wait and watch what I do to you.</i>

543
00:32:24,958 --> 00:32:27,291
<i>Ask him to pay the EMIs on time.</i>

544
00:32:27,375 --> 00:32:29,000
<i>He has borrowed money all over town.</i>

545
00:32:29,541 --> 00:32:30,750
<i>In my opinion...</i>

546
00:32:31,208 --> 00:32:34,416
{\an8}<i>getting cheated is the biggest sin
than cheating.</i>

547
00:32:58,208 --> 00:33:01,375
Sir, I saw that your 3BHK house
is up for rent in Mangalapuram.

548
00:33:01,458 --> 00:33:03,500
Yeah, that's my property.
Are you the tenant?

549
00:33:03,708 --> 00:33:04,958
No, sir, I'm Mithra.

550
00:33:05,291 --> 00:33:08,583
I run Standard Property, a property
management company in the same area.

551
00:33:09,666 --> 00:33:12,125
Here's my business card
and the company's address.

552
00:33:12,291 --> 00:33:14,541
Sir, we're managing
100+ premium properties.

553
00:33:14,625 --> 00:33:16,666
And we've been in this field
for more than 10 years.

554
00:33:16,750 --> 00:33:18,000
Fine, okay.

555
00:33:18,083 --> 00:33:19,666
The services that we provide

556
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:23,708
are to undertake
the client's rental properties

557
00:33:23,791 --> 00:33:27,458
and transfer the rent to the clients
on the said date.

558
00:33:27,708 --> 00:33:29,416
I see you reside in Adyar.

559
00:33:29,500 --> 00:33:31,166
But your property is in Mangalapuram.

560
00:33:31,250 --> 00:33:34,500
It'll be difficult for you to visit often
to check on the property.

561
00:33:34,708 --> 00:33:36,291
As we're situated in the same area,

562
00:33:36,375 --> 00:33:39,541
we'll regularly monitor
and hand you a month-wise report.

563
00:33:39,791 --> 00:33:42,291
Suppose the tenant is behind on rent,

564
00:33:42,375 --> 00:33:45,583
Standard Property
will pay you the rent on time.

565
00:33:46,291 --> 00:33:48,750
Our fee for this service is 10%.

566
00:33:48,916 --> 00:33:51,916
Also, I'll be collecting the same
from the tenant.

567
00:33:52,083 --> 00:33:54,666
You wouldn't have to worry
about your property anymore.

568
00:33:54,833 --> 00:33:57,458
Once you hire
Standard Property Management,

569
00:33:57,833 --> 00:33:59,166
we consider it as our own property.

570
00:34:02,666 --> 00:34:05,541
Sir, I reckon you have quoted 10,000
rupees as the rent for your property.

571
00:34:05,625 --> 00:34:08,750
But as per the market rate,
you can quote up to 15,000 rupees as rent.

572
00:34:09,208 --> 00:34:13,000
To be honest, your previous tenant
has cheated you all this time.

573
00:34:15,333 --> 00:34:16,208
Here's your agreement.

574
00:34:20,541 --> 00:34:22,250
Thank you, Sir.
Sir, here's your copy.

575
00:34:24,708 --> 00:34:26,250
Okay. Thank you.
Thank you, Sir.

576
00:34:28,916 --> 00:34:29,833
One minute.

577
00:34:34,375 --> 00:34:36,708
Since 1998, means...

578
00:34:37,125 --> 00:34:39,541
Is your main branch located in Chennai?

579
00:34:40,958 --> 00:34:43,416
No, Sir, our main branch
is located in Trichy.

580
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:44,875
Trichy!

581
00:34:46,958 --> 00:34:47,833
Okay!

582
00:34:49,041 --> 00:34:50,500
Okay? Okay!

583
00:35:10,250 --> 00:35:11,125
2,000.

584
00:35:12,833 --> 00:35:14,208
Credited... 4,000!

585
00:35:14,958 --> 00:35:15,833
8,000.

586
00:35:16,333 --> 00:35:17,208
Mom!

587
00:35:17,750 --> 00:35:18,625
Mom!

588
00:35:18,958 --> 00:35:20,708
I posted on Facebook

589
00:35:20,916 --> 00:35:22,791
through the Rambo Trust
to raise funds for your treatment.

590
00:35:22,875 --> 00:35:25,458
Many people have transferred money
to that account online.

591
00:35:25,625 --> 00:35:27,708
Until now, I have received 24,000 rupees.

592
00:35:27,791 --> 00:35:28,833
Are you serious?

593
00:35:29,416 --> 00:35:31,416
Is it from the Rambo Trust?

594
00:35:31,791 --> 00:35:33,416
Yes, it is from the trust.

595
00:35:36,250 --> 00:35:38,791
Mom, as we speak,
5,000 has been credited.

596
00:35:39,208 --> 00:35:42,250
I think we'll be able to raise the funds
needed for your surgery.

597
00:35:42,791 --> 00:35:48,208
Listen, your father's good deeds
don't have to bear fruit only through him.

598
00:35:48,833 --> 00:35:51,166
It could happen through strangers too.

599
00:35:52,666 --> 00:35:53,541
Go.

600
00:36:04,125 --> 00:36:05,583
It ran out of paper.

601
00:36:07,583 --> 00:36:08,458
Okay.

602
00:36:11,583 --> 00:36:12,500
It's working now.

603
00:36:13,583 --> 00:36:14,458
Here you go.

604
00:36:22,291 --> 00:36:23,458
Brother, your EB cards.

605
00:36:23,916 --> 00:36:25,625
Okay. Have you paid them all?

606
00:36:25,958 --> 00:36:26,875
Thank you so much.

607
00:36:35,666 --> 00:36:37,166
Saravana, I don't see any receipts.

608
00:36:47,583 --> 00:36:51,375
You see, the printer
at the office broke down.

609
00:36:53,666 --> 00:36:55,666
We couldn't issue any receipts today.

610
00:36:57,541 --> 00:37:00,083
So, I personally noted
that it had been paid.

611
00:37:00,500 --> 00:37:02,958
No problem, as long as it's been paid.
Thank you so much.

612
00:37:04,583 --> 00:37:06,250
Okay, good night.

613
00:37:33,166 --> 00:37:34,958
Since 1998.

614
00:37:35,458 --> 00:37:37,666
So, where in Chennai
is your main branch located?

615
00:37:38,291 --> 00:37:40,750
The main branch is not in Chennai.

616
00:37:42,083 --> 00:37:44,708
- It's in Madurai.
- Oh, Madurai. Okay.

617
00:37:45,416 --> 00:37:48,416
Ma'am, I'm ready to take
the 2BHK on Pallavan Street.

618
00:37:49,208 --> 00:37:51,291
{\an8}Here's the five lakh for the lease.

619
00:37:53,125 --> 00:37:55,000
Ma'am, please check once.

620
00:37:55,833 --> 00:37:58,291
- It will be all in.
- Please check once.

621
00:37:58,375 --> 00:38:00,916
- I'm sure it's all in.
- Ma'am, it's 5 lakhs!

622
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:02,250
Please check once!

623
00:38:02,333 --> 00:38:03,958
There's no harm in checking.

624
00:38:04,333 --> 00:38:07,875
Sir, I've been running this company
for over 10 years.

625
00:38:08,291 --> 00:38:09,916
I have met many clients!

626
00:38:10,625 --> 00:38:12,416
I can easily judge
by a few clients' appearances.

627
00:38:13,458 --> 00:38:14,500
Trust is everything.

628
00:38:15,208 --> 00:38:16,083
Okay, Ma'am.

629
00:38:16,458 --> 00:38:18,833
The minimum lease period
as per the contract is one year.

630
00:38:18,916 --> 00:38:22,250
If you wish to end the contract,
please notify three months in advance.

631
00:38:22,333 --> 00:38:23,208
Okay, Ma'am.

632
00:38:23,291 --> 00:38:26,041
Ma'am, where is this house owner located?

633
00:38:27,125 --> 00:38:29,125
Your house owner is in Canada.

634
00:38:29,208 --> 00:38:31,416
Oh, Canada! Okay, okay, Ma'am.

635
00:38:31,500 --> 00:38:32,458
If you need anything,
reach out to me.

636
00:38:32,541 --> 00:38:34,458
- Sure! Thank you, Ma'am.
- Okay.

637
00:38:34,541 --> 00:38:35,541
Thank you! Thank you!

638
00:38:49,833 --> 00:38:52,125
Hey, fool!
I just saw the reports you sent in.

639
00:38:52,208 --> 00:38:54,000
It has nothing to do
with the scenario you mentioned.

640
00:38:54,083 --> 00:38:56,416
We would've done many case studies
in college on this matter.

641
00:38:56,750 --> 00:38:59,250
<i>You were always confused.</i>

642
00:38:59,333 --> 00:39:00,750
<i>- You can't even identify a case...</i>
- Shall I pay him?

643
00:39:00,833 --> 00:39:02,375
Mom, shut up.
He's busy talking.

644
00:39:02,458 --> 00:39:04,083
How would you even diagnose?

645
00:39:04,166 --> 00:39:05,666
I can't believe you became a Doctor.

646
00:39:05,875 --> 00:39:08,500
And your parents
have built you a hospital.

647
00:39:08,625 --> 00:39:10,250
I pity your patients!

648
00:39:10,625 --> 00:39:11,958
Hang up the phone, rascal!

649
00:39:14,791 --> 00:39:17,416
Yes, Sir! 100% correct, Sir!

650
00:39:19,625 --> 00:39:21,791
You're right. When we compare it
with the previous report,

651
00:39:21,875 --> 00:39:23,791
{\an8}since it's not there,
it's no longer a threat.

652
00:39:23,875 --> 00:39:24,791
{\an8}Thank you, sir.

653
00:39:28,416 --> 00:39:30,083
{\an8}There's been a huge phenomenal change.

654
00:39:31,375 --> 00:39:33,291
{\an8}When we checked her current report,

655
00:39:33,375 --> 00:39:37,208
the tumor was from the previous
diagnosis itself.

656
00:39:38,541 --> 00:39:40,750
There's no need for us
to proceed with the surgery.

657
00:39:41,250 --> 00:39:45,291
{\an8}Hey, didn't I tell you that nothing's
wrong with me, and I'm doing well.

658
00:39:45,375 --> 00:39:46,666
Mom, please shut up.

659
00:39:47,833 --> 00:39:50,875
{\an8}Doctor, didn't you mention it's a
severe cancer and surgery is critical?

660
00:39:51,083 --> 00:39:52,500
I, too, Googled her condition.

661
00:39:52,583 --> 00:39:54,041
It showed up as severe cancer.

662
00:39:54,125 --> 00:39:56,166
But now you're saying
no need for surgery.

663
00:39:56,375 --> 00:39:57,291
I seriously don't understand.

664
00:39:57,375 --> 00:40:00,541
{\an8}If you Google it, it'll say
any sickness is a severe condition.

665
00:40:01,125 --> 00:40:03,416
I have been confused many times
Googling for answers.

666
00:40:03,541 --> 00:40:05,625
So, please don't believe Google.

667
00:40:06,125 --> 00:40:09,333
Please follow whatever doctors prescribe.

668
00:40:10,375 --> 00:40:12,375
Does that mean my mother is cured?

669
00:40:12,458 --> 00:40:14,666
Hey, didn't you hear me earlier?

670
00:40:14,750 --> 00:40:17,250
That nothing's wrong with me
and I'm doing well.

671
00:40:17,416 --> 00:40:19,083
Yet you've been asking him questions.

672
00:40:19,291 --> 00:40:21,166
Nothing's wrong with me.
I'm doing well.

673
00:40:21,250 --> 00:40:22,166
She's been cured!

674
00:40:22,625 --> 00:40:25,166
Correct!
I'm prescribing you tablets for 30 days.

675
00:40:25,250 --> 00:40:27,125
If you follow it,
everything will be well.

676
00:40:29,833 --> 00:40:32,166
Sorry, Sir,
we don't need the money right now.

677
00:40:32,625 --> 00:40:35,083
Thank you for donating
in response to the Facebook post.

678
00:40:35,291 --> 00:40:36,166
Okay, Sir!

679
00:40:37,791 --> 00:40:40,250
Mom, let's return the money.

680
00:40:40,333 --> 00:40:41,750
Why should we return the money?

681
00:40:41,833 --> 00:40:43,541
Now you don't need surgery.

682
00:40:43,791 --> 00:40:45,333
Let's return the money
to everyone who donated.

683
00:40:45,416 --> 00:40:46,541
We don't have to return it.

684
00:40:46,625 --> 00:40:47,791
I'll let you know. Wait.

685
00:40:48,250 --> 00:40:49,125
Mom!

686
00:40:49,291 --> 00:40:50,666
Let's wrap this up sooner.

687
00:40:51,041 --> 00:40:52,000
Why do we have to wait?

688
00:40:52,083 --> 00:40:54,666
Don't you still get it,
why we got this money?

689
00:40:54,750 --> 00:40:58,083
Think about it. Why did I fall sick,
and why were we in financial hardship?

690
00:40:58,166 --> 00:40:59,958
And when we got money,
why did I cure myself?

691
00:41:00,041 --> 00:41:02,250
Think about it.
Don't you still understand?

692
00:41:02,333 --> 00:41:04,208
All these years,
you were despising your father.

693
00:41:04,291 --> 00:41:06,750
Only now has he made sense
and made the money available for us.

694
00:41:06,833 --> 00:41:08,625
And you're giving it up easily.

695
00:41:08,708 --> 00:41:09,916
Why did we get this money?

696
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:12,416
Didn't I mention that
I want to start "Janaki Amma Studios"?

697
00:41:12,500 --> 00:41:14,125
This money is for that.

698
00:41:17,666 --> 00:41:20,541
Mom, have you lost your mind?

699
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:23,916
These people have been
crediting continuously.

700
00:41:24,125 --> 00:41:25,000
Mom!

701
00:41:25,625 --> 00:41:27,208
<i>Hello, this is Avinash speaking.</i>

702
00:41:27,333 --> 00:41:30,333
<i>I came across a post about raising funds
for Janaki Ma'am's treatment.</i>

703
00:41:30,416 --> 00:41:31,375
<i>Were you able to arrange for the funds?</i>

704
00:41:31,500 --> 00:41:33,166
Not yet, Sir.

705
00:41:33,333 --> 00:41:35,500
<i>Oh, I get it.
I have 10,000 rupees to donate.</i>

706
00:41:35,583 --> 00:41:36,708
<i>I will transfer it to your account.</i>

707
00:41:36,791 --> 00:41:38,416
<i>Please use that for your treatment.</i>

708
00:41:38,500 --> 00:41:39,416
Thank you, Sir.

709
00:41:40,291 --> 00:41:43,375
Janaki Ma'am
is still in critical condition.

710
00:41:43,458 --> 00:41:45,958
Your help is very important to her.

711
00:41:46,666 --> 00:41:49,708
Please spread the message
to as many people as possible.

712
00:41:49,791 --> 00:41:51,166
<i>Okay, I'll share it with everyone.</i>

713
00:41:51,250 --> 00:41:52,208
Thank you, Sir.

714
00:41:54,916 --> 00:41:55,791
Mom,

715
00:41:56,500 --> 00:41:57,583
what are you doing?

716
00:41:58,125 --> 00:41:59,000
Sit down!

717
00:42:00,208 --> 00:42:02,416
Let's resume Rambo Trust.

718
00:42:02,500 --> 00:42:03,375
Why?

719
00:42:03,541 --> 00:42:05,708
So that, like father, we'd make money
to give away as good deeds.

720
00:42:05,791 --> 00:42:06,958
Are you planning to do the same?

721
00:42:07,041 --> 00:42:08,416
First, listen closely to what I am saying.

722
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:11,041
Let's resume Rambo Trust.

723
00:42:11,250 --> 00:42:14,000
It'll bring in donations.
And we'll help people in need.

724
00:42:14,208 --> 00:42:17,000
Whatever extra we have, let's put it
on rotation and start making our movie.

725
00:42:17,083 --> 00:42:20,541
Mom, it doesn't sound right to me.

726
00:42:20,625 --> 00:42:23,708
Hey, we're not going to con people.

727
00:42:23,916 --> 00:42:26,958
We'll put the money in rotation
and eventually return it.

728
00:42:27,041 --> 00:42:29,083
I don't know.
I'm afraid to do this.

729
00:42:29,166 --> 00:42:30,916
I have a bad feeling
that we'll get caught in a huge problem.

730
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:33,750
I want to work hard
and become a Hero in cinema.

731
00:42:35,750 --> 00:42:37,958
Your father was honest,
but he didn't do squat.

732
00:42:38,541 --> 00:42:39,916
There's no point in being honest.

733
00:42:40,208 --> 00:42:42,000
You focus on becoming a Hero.

734
00:42:42,333 --> 00:42:43,750
I'll handle the rest.

735
00:42:44,166 --> 00:42:45,875
The people who are donating
won't even know

736
00:42:46,041 --> 00:42:48,125
if we raised enough funds
to meet our requirements.

737
00:42:48,416 --> 00:42:51,500
Until we decide to put a cap on it,
we'll continue to receive funds.

738
00:42:51,583 --> 00:42:52,583
Let it keep coming.

739
00:42:58,250 --> 00:43:00,375
- Remember what Thalaivar quoted?
- What?

740
00:43:00,625 --> 00:43:02,166
To create a few Heroes,

741
00:43:02,458 --> 00:43:04,208
- we can do whatever it takes.
- Mom!

742
00:43:06,958 --> 00:43:08,500
He never quoted anything like it.

743
00:43:09,250 --> 00:43:10,541
Why are you guiding the wrong way?

744
00:43:15,333 --> 00:43:16,958
Buddy, do you know Steve Jobs...

745
00:43:17,083 --> 00:43:19,666
Hey, don't patronize me
as you do with others.

746
00:43:20,125 --> 00:43:21,958
Just explain how the daily profits work.

747
00:43:22,625 --> 00:43:25,083
Fine, I'll let you in on the secret.
Don't tell anyone.

748
00:43:25,416 --> 00:43:28,083
<i>You're aware
that I work for a trading company.</i>

749
00:43:28,166 --> 00:43:31,250
<i>All the rich people in town are
investing in our trading company.</i>

750
00:43:31,333 --> 00:43:35,083
<i>Our job is to invest money in accounts
instructed by our Senior Analyst.</i>

751
00:43:35,166 --> 00:43:37,125
<i>And to withdraw from respective accounts.</i>

752
00:43:37,208 --> 00:43:39,333
Are you personally trading
without the company's knowledge?

753
00:43:39,416 --> 00:43:42,208
- Hey, shut up and mind your business.
<i>- My juniors at work...</i>

754
00:43:42,291 --> 00:43:45,500
<i>are personally profiting
without the company's knowledge.</i>

755
00:43:45,583 --> 00:43:48,291
Hey, you did personal trading
and bought a car so soon.

756
00:43:48,375 --> 00:43:50,208
We're helping strangers make profits.

757
00:43:50,291 --> 00:43:51,916
If not us, who will take care of us?

758
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:54,875
- Mind your business.
<i>- I helped many strangers make a profit.</i>

759
00:43:54,958 --> 00:43:56,333
<i>Why wouldn't I help myself, Saravana?</i>

760
00:43:56,416 --> 00:43:58,333
I worked at that company for over a year.

761
00:43:58,416 --> 00:44:00,458
<i>After analyzing closely, I'm suggesting</i>

762
00:44:00,541 --> 00:44:01,791
<i>that we can definitely make daily profits.</i>

763
00:44:01,875 --> 00:44:04,625
<i>Generally, people expect
a 10% profit daily.</i>

764
00:44:04,708 --> 00:44:06,291
<i>They're the certified fools.</i>

765
00:44:06,375 --> 00:44:08,833
<i>Our target will be only 2%.</i>

766
00:44:08,916 --> 00:44:10,250
<i>It's very easy to achieve.</i>

767
00:44:10,333 --> 00:44:11,708
You calculate yourself.

768
00:44:11,791 --> 00:44:14,250
You can make 60% profit in a month
without risk.

769
00:44:17,250 --> 00:44:19,166
Sir, there are 20 EB cards.

770
00:44:19,250 --> 00:44:20,333
I'm here to pay the EB bill.

771
00:44:21,000 --> 00:44:24,291
Hey, bring me exact change
for the respective cards.

772
00:44:24,375 --> 00:44:26,625
You know to come early in the morning
to beat the crowd.

773
00:44:26,708 --> 00:44:28,333
Can't you bring exact change?

774
00:44:28,500 --> 00:44:30,125
Take this away and return with change.

775
00:44:30,208 --> 00:44:32,041
Sir, you know, people come early
to pay the bill.

776
00:44:32,125 --> 00:44:33,166
You should be prepared with change.

777
00:44:33,250 --> 00:44:36,791
I'm not a bus conductor
to tender exact change.

778
00:44:36,875 --> 00:44:37,750
Get lost!

779
00:45:13,916 --> 00:45:17,791
Sir, the printer isn't working.
Could you please check?

780
00:45:18,333 --> 00:45:19,208
I'll check!

781
00:45:25,250 --> 00:45:27,541
This printer is always a problem.

782
00:45:30,208 --> 00:45:32,416
Hey, it's an old junk model.

783
00:45:32,791 --> 00:45:34,541
We've placed an order for new printers.

784
00:45:34,625 --> 00:45:37,375
But they'll deliver them
only after they're outdated.

785
00:45:37,458 --> 00:45:40,583
This is our Government.
There's nothing we could do about it.

786
00:45:40,666 --> 00:45:42,666
I think the printer has broken down.

787
00:45:42,750 --> 00:45:45,166
If we wait for a technician,
it'll get delayed.

788
00:45:45,250 --> 00:45:46,291
You do one thing.

789
00:45:46,375 --> 00:45:48,291
After paying all the bills...

790
00:45:48,375 --> 00:45:50,750
...then make a manual entry
of all the receipts.

791
00:45:50,833 --> 00:45:51,916
After the system is ready,

792
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:53,666
- then you can feed the data.
- Okay, Sir.

793
00:45:53,750 --> 00:45:56,750
We do this often
when there's a technical problem.

794
00:45:57,208 --> 00:46:01,708
- Okay, sir.
- I'll drop my wife off at Prince Jewelry.

795
00:46:01,791 --> 00:46:02,958
- Please manage.
- Okay.

796
00:46:03,083 --> 00:46:05,375
Girls, move to that line.

797
00:46:06,208 --> 00:46:08,583
Join that counter.
Very nice!

798
00:46:09,666 --> 00:46:10,875
You continue your work.

799
00:46:30,541 --> 00:46:32,375
The printer is not working.
Here's the manual receipt.

800
00:46:39,291 --> 00:46:40,333
- Sir.
- Hand it to me.

801
00:46:45,416 --> 00:46:47,041
The printer is not working.
Here's the manual receipt.

802
00:46:51,958 --> 00:46:54,041
- Sir, EB bill.
- Oh, it's you.

803
00:46:55,041 --> 00:46:55,958
Hand it to me.

804
00:47:01,625 --> 00:47:04,291
- What's all this?
- Didn't you ask for change?

805
00:47:04,375 --> 00:47:05,416
Now pay the bill.

806
00:47:07,333 --> 00:47:08,916
Oh, he's the troublemaker.

807
00:47:21,333 --> 00:47:24,208
Sir, suddenly it's printing now.
What shall I do?

808
00:47:24,375 --> 00:47:25,541
It has a mind of its own.

809
00:47:25,625 --> 00:47:27,791
It'll keep going on and off.

810
00:47:28,291 --> 00:47:30,291
Like my wife's mood swings
and anger.

811
00:47:30,375 --> 00:47:33,416
There's a phone number on that door.

812
00:47:33,500 --> 00:47:36,125
Call that technician
and get it fixed.

813
00:47:36,333 --> 00:47:37,208
Okay, Sir.

814
00:47:41,625 --> 00:47:42,500
Bye, Sir.

815
00:47:52,750 --> 00:47:54,625
<i>I'm the King</i>

816
00:47:54,750 --> 00:47:56,583
<i>From this moment on, I rule</i>

817
00:47:56,750 --> 00:47:58,541
<i>I'm the King</i>

818
00:47:58,625 --> 00:48:00,750
<i>I'm about to sound the call</i>

819
00:48:00,833 --> 00:48:03,625
Hey, Satha,
if you get me guaranteed profits...

820
00:48:03,708 --> 00:48:05,916
- I'll invest more money.
- It's easy peasy, Buddy.

821
00:48:06,625 --> 00:48:09,250
If you make this work,
our lives will change for good.

822
00:48:09,333 --> 00:48:10,541
<i>King, King, King</i>

823
00:48:10,625 --> 00:48:12,625
<i>Out here, I'm the King</i>

824
00:48:12,875 --> 00:48:14,583
<i>King, King, King</i>

825
00:48:14,666 --> 00:48:16,750
<i>I'm about to sound the call</i>

826
00:48:21,208 --> 00:48:23,875
Saravana, why is your printer
constantly breaking down?

827
00:48:23,958 --> 00:48:24,833
Why are you staring at me?

828
00:48:24,916 --> 00:48:27,416
Hey, what can he do
if the machine malfunctions?

829
00:48:27,666 --> 00:48:29,708
Don't keep nagging him.

830
00:48:29,791 --> 00:48:31,541
Hey, there are too many people.

831
00:48:31,791 --> 00:48:32,708
Why can't you work efficiently?

832
00:48:32,916 --> 00:48:34,000
Get back to work.
Finish up soon.

833
00:48:34,083 --> 00:48:35,000
I'll handle it. You get lost!

834
00:48:36,541 --> 00:48:38,666
Gopi, sir, asked not to work
if the printer isn't working.

835
00:48:38,750 --> 00:48:40,791
Who's Gopi to bark orders?

836
00:48:40,875 --> 00:48:44,500
Listen to me.
Issue a manual receipt to everyone.

837
00:48:44,583 --> 00:48:45,833
And get back to work, son.

838
00:48:46,250 --> 00:48:50,041
I dropped my wife off
at the Chinese beauty parlor.

839
00:48:50,125 --> 00:48:51,833
I'll drop her off at home and return.

840
00:48:51,916 --> 00:48:52,875
Please handle it, dear.

841
00:48:55,291 --> 00:48:56,500
I feel like quitting the job.

842
00:48:56,583 --> 00:48:58,500
Don't you ever say you're quitting.

843
00:48:58,583 --> 00:49:00,000
I don't want unnecessary problems.

844
00:49:00,083 --> 00:49:04,458
Whenever you say you are quitting,
I get a migraine.

845
00:49:04,541 --> 00:49:07,250
- Please don't say it.
- I think of running away, sir.

846
00:49:07,333 --> 00:49:10,333
Run away?
What's your problem in life? Spill it!

847
00:49:10,416 --> 00:49:12,250
This printer and Gopi, sir,
are my problem.

848
00:49:12,333 --> 00:49:13,791
To hell with Gopi!

849
00:49:13,875 --> 00:49:16,291
You continue to issue manual receipts.

850
00:49:16,375 --> 00:49:18,666
I'm here for you.
I have your back.

851
00:49:19,500 --> 00:49:22,291
My wife...
Today is a new moon day.

852
00:49:22,375 --> 00:49:28,125
I have to take her to the temple
in Mylapore.

853
00:49:28,208 --> 00:49:32,041
Exactly, in four hours,
I'll return to the office.

854
00:49:32,250 --> 00:49:33,791
Please take care of the counters.

855
00:49:33,875 --> 00:49:35,916
- Sure, sir.
- Your printer is working well, right?

856
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:37,791
Hey! Why does your printer
keep breaking down?

857
00:49:37,875 --> 00:49:40,083
Why do you keep harping
that it's his printer?

858
00:49:40,166 --> 00:49:43,708
If he quits his job,
are you going to sit at the counter?

859
00:49:43,791 --> 00:49:45,458
There's something wrong with that printer.

860
00:49:45,541 --> 00:49:48,083
Why are you so obsessed with the printer?

861
00:49:48,166 --> 00:49:50,500
I've instructed him to issue
manual receipts.

862
00:49:50,625 --> 00:49:51,541
If there's an issue in billing,
we'll be in trouble.

863
00:49:51,625 --> 00:49:54,000
Didn't I tell you
I'm taking his responsibility?

864
00:49:54,083 --> 00:49:56,458
It's me who assured him that
manual receipts won't be an issue.

865
00:49:56,541 --> 00:49:58,291
From today onward,
he's like a son to me.

866
00:49:58,375 --> 00:50:01,000
No matter what the issue is,
I'm responsible for it.

867
00:50:01,083 --> 00:50:03,708
Just because he doesn't talk back,
don't keep nagging him.

868
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:04,958
Get lost!

869
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:07,000
Do as you please!

870
00:50:08,625 --> 00:50:11,333
My wife has food poisoning.

871
00:50:11,416 --> 00:50:13,291
Since this morning, she's been vomiting.

872
00:50:13,375 --> 00:50:16,583
I have to take her to Dr. Arun in Guindy.

873
00:50:16,666 --> 00:50:19,416
I applied for two days of sick leave.

874
00:50:19,541 --> 00:50:21,583
- You take care of my counter, too.
- Okay, Sir.

875
00:50:21,666 --> 00:50:25,166
If Gopi gives you a hard time,
please call me.

876
00:50:26,416 --> 00:50:28,833
Saravana, lately the collection is low.

877
00:50:28,916 --> 00:50:32,500
Unlike before, customers don't wish
to pay their bills ahead of the due date.

878
00:50:32,708 --> 00:50:33,583
There's nothing we could do.

879
00:50:33,666 --> 00:50:36,125
Unlike before,
the public has gotten smarter.

880
00:50:36,208 --> 00:50:37,375
No one can fool them.

881
00:50:37,458 --> 00:50:40,541
The public has gotten smarter;
no one can fool them. Isn't it?

882
00:50:40,625 --> 00:50:43,500
<i>Unlike before,
the public has gotten smarter.</i>

883
00:50:43,583 --> 00:50:44,833
<i>No one can fool them.</i>

884
00:50:45,041 --> 00:50:46,666
<i>I'm no villain</i>

885
00:50:47,208 --> 00:50:48,750
<i>I'm no hero</i>

886
00:50:49,125 --> 00:50:50,541
<i>I'm no joker</i>

887
00:50:50,625 --> 00:50:52,875
<i>I stand above them all
I'm the King!</i>

888
00:50:53,083 --> 00:50:54,583
<i>I'm neither "That-God"</i>

889
00:50:55,166 --> 00:50:56,041
<i>- Nor I'm "This-Satan"</i>
- Yes, man.

890
00:50:56,125 --> 00:50:57,541
As you mentioned,
everyone paid on time.

891
00:50:57,750 --> 00:51:00,083
The public has gotten smarter.
No one can fool them.

892
00:51:00,833 --> 00:51:02,833
<i>I'm no gangster
No monster either</i>

893
00:51:02,916 --> 00:51:04,583
<i>I'm here to claim my rightful share</i>

894
00:51:04,666 --> 00:51:06,875
<i>There's no right or wrong anymore</i>

895
00:51:06,958 --> 00:51:08,583
<i>I'm shutting your mouth for good</i>

896
00:51:08,666 --> 00:51:10,375
Buddy, you gave me 2 lakhs.

897
00:51:10,458 --> 00:51:11,916
10 days' profit, 1 lakh.

898
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:14,333
It's not enough for my situation.
I need more!

899
00:51:14,416 --> 00:51:16,500
Let's collaborate
to do it on a larger scale.

900
00:51:16,583 --> 00:51:19,416
As per your information,
we're getting 60% returns.

901
00:51:19,500 --> 00:51:21,500
I'll start a new company in my area.

902
00:51:21,583 --> 00:51:22,458
We'll find investors.

903
00:51:22,625 --> 00:51:23,875
If we lend it at interest, we get 10%.

904
00:51:23,958 --> 00:51:25,541
We offer 20% guaranteed returns!

905
00:51:25,791 --> 00:51:27,333
You're the inside man.
And I'll handle it outside.

906
00:51:31,833 --> 00:51:33,500
Madam, please check if it's all in there.

907
00:51:33,708 --> 00:51:35,583
I can judge from a client's appearance.

908
00:51:35,666 --> 00:51:38,125
I can sense from your appearance
that it's all in there.

909
00:51:38,375 --> 00:51:40,000
Why don't you count it once?

910
00:51:40,083 --> 00:51:41,333
Your name is Saroja.

911
00:51:41,791 --> 00:51:43,083
My mother's name is also Saroja.

912
00:51:43,166 --> 00:51:44,416
My father's name is also Nagaraj.

913
00:51:44,500 --> 00:51:46,375
Vishnu is my father's name.

914
00:51:46,458 --> 00:51:48,166
If I still go ahead and count the money...

915
00:51:48,250 --> 00:51:49,958
it'll be like I'm suspecting
my own mother.

916
00:51:50,041 --> 00:51:52,208
It'll be like I'm suspecting
my own father.

917
00:51:52,791 --> 00:51:55,000
- I have trust in you, Sir.
- Dad!

918
00:51:55,458 --> 00:51:57,458
You heard her.
Give it back to her.

919
00:51:58,291 --> 00:51:59,666
What happened?
I don't understand.

920
00:51:59,750 --> 00:52:02,833
Sorry, Ma'am,
the bundle was short of 1000 rupees.

921
00:52:02,916 --> 00:52:04,375
Father did ask me to put it back.

922
00:52:04,458 --> 00:52:05,791
But I forgot, Ma'am.

923
00:52:05,875 --> 00:52:08,750
Brother, you must not cheat anyone.

924
00:52:09,333 --> 00:52:10,333
It's a big mistake.

925
00:52:10,791 --> 00:52:12,333
- Understand?
- I'm sorry, Ma'am.

926
00:52:12,416 --> 00:52:13,291
Don't repeat it.

927
00:52:13,375 --> 00:52:15,208
<i>Suddenly, I turned dangerous</i>

928
00:52:15,291 --> 00:52:17,416
<i>I was just one
Now I'm a movement</i>

929
00:52:17,500 --> 00:52:19,250
<i>I was once Civil</i>

930
00:52:19,333 --> 00:52:21,458
<i>But now I turned into a Devil</i>

931
00:52:21,541 --> 00:52:24,041
Sir, here's the 1st month rent
of your property.

932
00:52:24,125 --> 00:52:26,625
Mithra, it's not yet the 1st of the month,
and you already paid the rent.

933
00:52:26,708 --> 00:52:27,666
Sir, like I mentioned

934
00:52:27,750 --> 00:52:30,583
Standard Property Management
will pay sharply before the due date.

935
00:52:30,666 --> 00:52:31,583
{\an8}Nice!

936
00:52:34,250 --> 00:52:36,625
Love, Drama, Action, Thriller.

937
00:52:36,708 --> 00:52:38,333
- Add this too.
- Comedy?

938
00:52:38,583 --> 00:52:39,583
Fine, adding comedy too.

939
00:52:39,666 --> 00:52:42,166
Love, Drama, Action, Thriller, and Comedy.

940
00:52:42,250 --> 00:52:44,875
- That means our genre is a hit!
- Are you sure?

941
00:52:44,958 --> 00:52:46,958
Only if we rip off from local movies,
they'd call us copycats.

942
00:52:47,041 --> 00:52:48,208
But if I rip off a Korean film...

943
00:52:48,291 --> 00:52:50,083
they'd call us Master of craft.

944
00:52:54,208 --> 00:52:55,125
Okay, Auntie.

945
00:52:56,208 --> 00:52:57,583
Is it possible to meet
that girl in person?

946
00:52:57,666 --> 00:53:00,375
Sure, Karthi!
I'll check with the Doctor right away.

947
00:53:00,625 --> 00:53:02,750
Life may make us prisoners trapped in it.

948
00:53:02,833 --> 00:53:04,625
But breaking out of that prison
or remaining trapped

949
00:53:04,708 --> 00:53:05,958
is in our hands!

950
00:53:06,041 --> 00:53:07,333
Remove hands from the dialogue.

951
00:53:07,416 --> 00:53:08,666
- You should not use your hands.
- Sorry, Director.

952
00:53:08,875 --> 00:53:10,250
They'll never agree to creative ideas.

953
00:53:10,958 --> 00:53:12,000
- Hello, Doctor.
- Yes!

954
00:53:12,083 --> 00:53:13,541
It's regarding patient Pavithra.

955
00:53:13,625 --> 00:53:16,416
A trustee named Karthi
is here to meet her.

956
00:53:16,500 --> 00:53:18,291
- Shall we come over?
- No!

957
00:53:18,791 --> 00:53:20,791
To me, God is everything.

958
00:53:20,875 --> 00:53:21,833
Oh, is it?

959
00:53:22,041 --> 00:53:23,833
My first God...

960
00:53:24,458 --> 00:53:25,833
- ...Money!
- Yes, Doctor.

961
00:53:25,916 --> 00:53:27,083
I forgot about it.

962
00:53:27,166 --> 00:53:29,666
You blinked 5 times.
You must blink only 3 times.

963
00:53:29,750 --> 00:53:31,291
Moreover, you must not blink
during the take.

964
00:53:31,375 --> 00:53:32,541
Hey, read the dialogue.
Roll camera.

965
00:53:32,625 --> 00:53:34,250
- Next take. Okay.
- Next?

966
00:53:34,333 --> 00:53:37,000
They're planning to shift her
to another hospital.

967
00:53:37,083 --> 00:53:39,333
You can pay me, and I'll pass it on.

968
00:53:40,833 --> 00:53:41,875
150 rupees.

969
00:53:42,333 --> 00:53:44,666
- And he cross-checked so many times.
- I don't get it.

970
00:53:44,750 --> 00:53:46,500
I meant 150 RUPEES.

971
00:53:46,625 --> 00:53:48,458
- I want a receipt.
- For 150 rupees?

972
00:53:50,208 --> 00:53:51,666
A good person won't harm anyone.

973
00:53:51,750 --> 00:53:54,083
Even an evil person won't harm anyone.

974
00:53:54,333 --> 00:53:56,333
Both won't harm?
What kind of stupid dialogue is this?

975
00:53:56,458 --> 00:53:58,291
In our film,
there will be no violence.

976
00:53:58,375 --> 00:53:59,333
But I'll be violent.

977
00:53:59,416 --> 00:54:00,500
Move to the next take.

978
00:54:00,583 --> 00:54:02,791
He does not care for anything.

979
00:54:02,875 --> 00:54:03,750
Shit!

980
00:54:03,875 --> 00:54:05,500
There's no modulation or emotion.

981
00:54:05,583 --> 00:54:07,250
Why can't this face project some emotions?

982
00:54:07,333 --> 00:54:08,666
Acting is like a penance.

983
00:54:08,791 --> 00:54:10,125
Why don't you show me how to repent?

984
00:54:10,208 --> 00:54:11,500
He's testing me.

985
00:54:11,666 --> 00:54:12,875
Roll camera. Watch me.

986
00:54:17,333 --> 00:54:19,000
Here, quench your thirst.

987
00:54:19,250 --> 00:54:20,125
In fact, you were good.

988
00:54:20,208 --> 00:54:21,958
Only actors should perform,
not the director.

989
00:54:22,041 --> 00:54:24,666
- Only actors should emote.
- Why the heck did you challenge me?

990
00:54:24,750 --> 00:54:25,875
My assistants are around.

991
00:54:25,958 --> 00:54:27,125
Hey, cut camera!

992
00:54:27,208 --> 00:54:28,583
Hey, why are you recording?

993
00:54:28,750 --> 00:54:32,708
<i>If I pull off a crime without a flaw
People will call it brilliance</i>

994
00:54:32,791 --> 00:54:36,541
<i>Once you become a VIP,
History turns into mystery</i>

995
00:54:36,625 --> 00:54:38,750
It's very tough
even to deliver 10% returns.

996
00:54:38,833 --> 00:54:40,750
How are you able to offer a 20% return?

997
00:54:40,833 --> 00:54:43,958
{\an8}That's Quick money for you.
We don't invest in Indian companies.

998
00:54:44,041 --> 00:54:45,208
We invest in US companies.

999
00:54:45,291 --> 00:54:47,166
Let me give you
a piece of confidential information.

1000
00:54:47,250 --> 00:54:48,291
We have a scheme called Ruby Coin.

1001
00:54:48,375 --> 00:54:50,000
It's not the chump change you carry.

1002
00:54:50,083 --> 00:54:51,833
In the future,
there will be no physical currency.

1003
00:54:51,916 --> 00:54:52,833
It'll all be digital currency.

1004
00:54:52,916 --> 00:54:54,416
If you invest in Ruby Coin...

1005
00:54:54,500 --> 00:54:57,208
in the next year,
you'll be the richest person in this area.

1006
00:54:57,291 --> 00:54:59,500
For now, I'll invest three lakhs.

1007
00:54:59,583 --> 00:55:01,125
First, I'll invest one lakh.

1008
00:55:01,291 --> 00:55:03,708
You return 20% interest.
Later, I'll decide.

1009
00:55:03,791 --> 00:55:07,375
<i>Stacks of money
Doesn't that say enough?</i>

1010
00:55:07,583 --> 00:55:09,375
<i>Indeed, it's con-money</i>

1011
00:55:09,458 --> 00:55:11,625
<i>Whatever I touch becomes a hit</i>

1012
00:55:11,708 --> 00:55:14,000
Buddy, if we keep the money in rotation

1013
00:55:14,083 --> 00:55:16,750
- for sure we'll become rich in a year.
- You're right, Satha.

1014
00:55:16,833 --> 00:55:18,625
I hope we won't get caught.

1015
00:55:18,708 --> 00:55:21,791
We're rotating the public money from EB

1016
00:55:21,875 --> 00:55:23,333
and pay it back before the due date.

1017
00:55:23,458 --> 00:55:26,500
Similarly, we take money
from the customers as an investment

1018
00:55:26,583 --> 00:55:28,666
and invest that money
in your trading company.

1019
00:55:28,750 --> 00:55:31,125
As you guarantee a 60% profit as return

1020
00:55:31,208 --> 00:55:34,041
is how I can guarantee
the customers 20% profit as return.

1021
00:55:34,125 --> 00:55:35,750
We won't get caught
if we keep up this technique.

1022
00:55:35,875 --> 00:55:37,291
Because we're not conning people.

1023
00:55:37,375 --> 00:55:39,041
Yeah, we're not conning people.

1024
00:55:39,125 --> 00:55:40,750
- But they're getting conned by us.
- I ought to!

1025
00:55:41,208 --> 00:55:43,250
Get lost!
No use in telling you.

1026
00:55:43,333 --> 00:55:47,208
<i>Let unrest rise in every heart...
Nurture it, and it becomes a storm</i>

1027
00:55:47,291 --> 00:55:50,583
<i>One bite of that rock-solid roti
Grandpa's dentures turned red quickly</i>

1028
00:55:50,666 --> 00:55:52,166
<i>Let the whole city rise and applaud</i>

1029
00:55:52,250 --> 00:55:55,000
<i>Tighten the cage...
Watch me tear it apart</i>

1030
00:55:55,083 --> 00:55:57,166
<i>Even Harry Potter gets knocked out
In one shot</i>

1031
00:55:57,250 --> 00:55:59,500
<i>If needed,
I unleash Power Rangers Ninja Storm</i>

1032
00:56:00,916 --> 00:56:02,875
Uncle, I'm still a debtor.

1033
00:56:03,375 --> 00:56:04,333
Not the borrowing one.

1034
00:56:04,583 --> 00:56:05,458
But the lender.

1035
00:56:08,291 --> 00:56:10,125
<i>I'm the Lord
I run things now</i>

1036
00:56:10,416 --> 00:56:12,125
<i>Every empire starts small</i>

1037
00:56:12,458 --> 00:56:13,833
<i>When it comes to money...
I'm the Boss</i>

1038
00:56:13,916 --> 00:56:16,208
<i>Let God Himself try to stop me</i>

1039
00:56:16,291 --> 00:56:17,875
<i>Gotta live larger than life</i>

1040
00:56:17,958 --> 00:56:19,916
<i>We should become the talk of the town</i>

1041
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:21,916
<i>On the penthouse terrace</i>

1042
00:56:22,000 --> 00:56:24,291
<i>Buddy... I'll descend on the helipad</i>

1043
00:56:29,541 --> 00:56:31,375
<i>I'm the King</i>

1044
00:56:31,458 --> 00:56:33,416
<i>From this moment on, I rule</i>

1045
00:56:33,500 --> 00:56:35,250
<i>I'm the King</i>

1046
00:56:35,333 --> 00:56:37,625
<i>I'm about to sound the call</i>

1047
00:56:37,708 --> 00:56:39,333
<i>King, King, King...</i>

1048
00:56:39,875 --> 00:56:40,750
How come an Audi car?

1049
00:56:40,958 --> 00:56:44,000
- You see...
- Stop! Engagement ring. I got it.

1050
00:56:44,083 --> 00:56:45,875
It's a gift from your father-in-law.
Am I right?

1051
00:56:46,625 --> 00:56:48,250
- Yes.
- I don't mind how the girl is.

1052
00:56:48,333 --> 00:56:50,916
But I want a father-in-law
like Saravanan's father-in-law.

1053
00:56:51,000 --> 00:56:52,875
Such a humble person.
Lucky boy.

1054
00:56:53,875 --> 00:56:55,666
I did tell you, people.
But no one believed me.

1055
00:56:55,958 --> 00:56:57,750
- Look over there.
- You're right, Sir.

1056
00:56:57,833 --> 00:57:00,000
Hey! Where are you looking?

1057
00:57:00,375 --> 00:57:02,416
Look at the Rolex watch he's wearing.

1058
00:57:02,500 --> 00:57:04,458
Saravanan's father-in-law gifted him.

1059
00:57:04,541 --> 00:57:06,500
You're settled for life
'cause of your father-in-law

1060
00:57:06,583 --> 00:57:08,125
I don't know if one exists for me.

1061
00:57:08,250 --> 00:57:09,833
<i>I'm no villain</i>

1062
00:57:10,250 --> 00:57:11,208
<i>I'm no hero</i>

1063
00:57:11,291 --> 00:57:13,791
I'm investing 53 lakhs.

1064
00:57:13,875 --> 00:57:14,916
I'm investing 40 lakhs.

1065
00:57:15,000 --> 00:57:16,583
I'm investing 20 lakhs.

1066
00:57:16,666 --> 00:57:18,416
It's hard-earned money, Son.

1067
00:57:18,500 --> 00:57:19,916
<i>Nor I'm "This-Satan"</i>

1068
00:57:20,041 --> 00:57:21,708
<i>I'm not Just-Human either</i>

1069
00:57:21,791 --> 00:57:24,125
- Thank you.
<i>- I'm the King who reigns supreme</i>

1070
00:57:24,458 --> 00:57:26,458
{\an8}Hey, it's the Old Korean Boy.

1071
00:57:26,541 --> 00:57:28,500
Directors have already
ripped off this story part by part.

1072
00:57:28,625 --> 00:57:29,500
Hey!

1073
00:57:30,291 --> 00:57:33,083
You said if you rip off from Korean movies
people call us Master of the craft.

1074
00:57:33,166 --> 00:57:35,291
Can't you even copy properly?

1075
00:57:35,833 --> 00:57:38,166
It's a rip-off!
Still, it will work with the audience.

1076
00:57:38,250 --> 00:57:39,125
- Thank you, Sir.
- Okay, Sir.

1077
00:57:39,208 --> 00:57:40,083
Pose well.

1078
00:57:40,166 --> 00:57:41,041
Another pose.

1079
00:57:41,333 --> 00:57:42,250
Change pose.

1080
00:57:44,583 --> 00:57:46,125
Oh, Old Boy?

1081
00:57:47,833 --> 00:57:48,958
Have you watched it already?

1082
00:57:50,291 --> 00:57:51,500
It's not the same movie.

1083
00:57:51,583 --> 00:57:53,875
- Oh!
- You can't even copy a poster.

1084
00:57:53,958 --> 00:57:55,208
- Hey!
- Stop right there.

1085
00:57:55,291 --> 00:57:56,166
- Hey!
- Don't do it.

1086
00:57:56,250 --> 00:57:57,708
- Don't!
- Hey, Kumar, stop right there.

1087
00:57:59,583 --> 00:58:00,500
Hello!

1088
00:58:00,666 --> 00:58:01,875
- Me?
- Yes, you!

1089
00:58:01,958 --> 00:58:05,291
- Tell me!
- How can you not have AC or car parking?

1090
00:58:05,375 --> 00:58:07,041
- How do you expect me to dine here?
- Don't dine here!

1091
00:58:07,541 --> 00:58:08,416
Dude!

1092
00:58:08,500 --> 00:58:11,208
That's why I suggested
going to Cafe Coffee Day.

1093
00:58:11,291 --> 00:58:12,208
But you never listened.

1094
00:58:12,291 --> 00:58:15,416
Hello! This table is very lucky for us.

1095
00:58:15,500 --> 00:58:16,958
We're planning to invest in this table.

1096
00:58:17,041 --> 00:58:19,500
Tell me how many lakhs you need.
I'll write you a single check.

1097
00:58:19,791 --> 00:58:21,750
Table and four chairs.
It's only 3,000 rupees.

1098
00:58:21,833 --> 00:58:23,208
Pay and carry it over your head.

1099
00:58:23,291 --> 00:58:24,416
Or else drag it out of here.

1100
00:58:24,583 --> 00:58:26,166
- Shit!
- Why would you?

1101
00:58:29,291 --> 00:58:32,166
Ma'am, this month's toll collection
is 10.25 crore rupees.

1102
00:58:32,250 --> 00:58:33,125
Okay, Krishna.

1103
00:58:33,333 --> 00:58:34,333
- You may leave.
- Thank you, Ma'am.

1104
00:58:34,916 --> 00:58:38,833
After marriage, Dad is planning
to give this toll as a gift to you.

1105
00:58:38,916 --> 00:58:40,541
<i>King, King, King</i>

1106
00:58:40,625 --> 00:58:42,708
<i>Out here, I'm the King</i>

1107
00:58:42,833 --> 00:58:44,500
<i>King, King, King</i>

1108
00:58:44,583 --> 00:58:46,916
<i>- I'm about to sound the call</i>
- Rithi...

1109
00:58:47,375 --> 00:58:48,333
...is pregnant, buddy.

1110
00:58:48,666 --> 00:58:50,583
<i>Out here, I'm the King</i>

1111
00:58:50,875 --> 00:58:52,541
<i>King, King, King</i>

1112
00:58:52,625 --> 00:58:54,875
<i>I'm about to sound the call</i>

1113
00:59:08,375 --> 00:59:10,250
Brother, quickly finish the work.

1114
00:59:11,208 --> 00:59:12,125
Buddy!

1115
00:59:12,708 --> 00:59:14,333
You had requested to borrow
10 crores from Ganesh Sait.

1116
00:59:14,416 --> 00:59:15,291
Yes!

1117
00:59:16,125 --> 00:59:18,041
Shall I arrange that money for you?

1118
00:59:19,208 --> 00:59:21,666
I need 10 crores as investment.

1119
00:59:21,750 --> 00:59:22,791
You say Rithi is pregnant.

1120
00:59:23,791 --> 00:59:24,791
How are you going to manage?

1121
00:59:27,250 --> 00:59:29,250
All these years,
I looked after my father's business.

1122
00:59:29,666 --> 00:59:31,208
I know how to start my own business.

1123
00:59:32,041 --> 00:59:33,416
How are you going to raise
10 crore in investment?

1124
00:59:33,708 --> 00:59:35,208
Hey, it's a huge risk.

1125
00:59:35,291 --> 00:59:36,625
You're already in a lot of trouble.

1126
00:59:36,958 --> 00:59:38,458
How would you arrange the money for me?

1127
00:59:38,708 --> 00:59:40,333
Let it go, Buddy. I'll handle it.

1128
00:59:40,625 --> 00:59:42,750
Trust me. I know an investor.

1129
00:59:43,625 --> 00:59:45,041
I'll say it's for me
and pass on the funds to you.

1130
00:59:45,250 --> 00:59:46,125
If you make a profit,

1131
00:59:46,208 --> 00:59:48,083
I'll be relieved of my problems, too.

1132
00:59:48,416 --> 00:59:49,416
That's a good point.

1133
00:59:49,875 --> 00:59:50,750
It makes sense, though.

1134
00:59:51,458 --> 00:59:52,333
But think about it.

1135
00:59:52,416 --> 00:59:54,791
If it's not an issue, arrange the money.

1136
00:59:54,958 --> 00:59:55,833
Okay?

1137
00:59:58,125 --> 01:00:00,500
Why did you ask me to withdraw
all the money from the bank so urgently?

1138
01:00:00,583 --> 01:00:02,416
Hey, Satha, I came across a great deal.

1139
01:00:02,500 --> 01:00:05,250
If we invest 10 crores in two days,
they'll return 15 crores.

1140
01:00:05,333 --> 01:00:06,208
Think about it.

1141
01:00:06,291 --> 01:00:09,500
We'll make a profit in two days
that would take us a year to earn.

1142
01:00:10,083 --> 01:00:11,875
5 crores in profit in two days.

1143
01:00:12,166 --> 01:00:13,333
- Are you serious?
- Yes!

1144
01:00:13,416 --> 01:00:15,166
A huge consignment is arriving
at the harbor.

1145
01:00:15,500 --> 01:00:17,791
<i>It's enough
if we safely take it outside the harbor.</i>

1146
01:00:18,541 --> 01:00:19,916
We'll make 20 crores.

1147
01:00:21,083 --> 01:00:22,916
But I need 10 crores for expenses.

1148
01:00:23,083 --> 01:00:24,541
I only need 5 crores.

1149
01:00:24,625 --> 01:00:26,041
But if we invest 10 crores

1150
01:00:26,541 --> 01:00:30,541
Ganesh Sait said he will return
15 crores in two days.

1151
01:00:30,625 --> 01:00:34,083
Once I close this deal,
she and I will leave for Kolkata.

1152
01:00:34,375 --> 01:00:35,291
Is the client trustworthy?

1153
01:00:35,416 --> 01:00:38,333
Like you're my school friend,
he's my college friend.

1154
01:00:38,916 --> 01:00:40,625
But I'm short of cash.

1155
01:00:40,833 --> 01:00:42,625
I have 50 lakhs in savings.

1156
01:00:42,708 --> 01:00:43,666
Shall I go home and bring it?

1157
01:00:43,750 --> 01:00:45,291
Hey, super! You bring it.

1158
01:00:45,416 --> 01:00:47,166
I, too, shall go to the EB office
and bring some money.

1159
01:00:50,625 --> 01:00:53,916
Didn't you complain that your printer
keeps breaking down?

1160
01:00:54,125 --> 01:00:56,125
- It's working fine.
- Sir, I did tell you.

1161
01:00:56,583 --> 01:00:58,000
It goes on and off.

1162
01:00:58,208 --> 01:01:00,833
Oh! Okay, you carry on.

1163
01:01:17,750 --> 01:01:19,000
{\an8}Hey, get in line.

1164
01:01:19,208 --> 01:01:20,791
Fall in line. Come on, quick.

1165
01:01:20,958 --> 01:01:22,750
{\an8}Stop chattering and stay quiet.

1166
01:01:23,458 --> 01:01:26,458
Sir, I can handle this crowd.

1167
01:01:26,750 --> 01:01:27,625
Why trouble yourself?

1168
01:01:27,750 --> 01:01:29,916
How come you became so helpful?

1169
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:32,208
Gangadhar went on medical leave
and requested to cover for him.

1170
01:01:32,291 --> 01:01:33,208
So, I am here.

1171
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:52,041
Saravana, thanks for getting me tickets
for Enthiran FDFS.

1172
01:01:52,125 --> 01:01:54,083
I told Gopi that I'm sick.

1173
01:01:54,166 --> 01:01:55,250
You maintain the same.

1174
01:01:55,333 --> 01:01:58,000
Hey, why did you ask him
to help with your counter?

1175
01:01:58,125 --> 01:02:01,250
I asked him to cover for me
so you won't be alone at the counter.

1176
01:02:01,583 --> 01:02:02,750
I'm going to watch my Hero's film.

1177
01:02:02,833 --> 01:02:04,750
I'm very excited. Let me go!

1178
01:02:04,875 --> 01:02:05,958
Hello? Hello?

1179
01:02:10,000 --> 01:02:14,250
<i>Dear audience! Did you celebrate
Enthiran's carnival in your town?</i>

1180
01:02:14,916 --> 01:02:18,541
<i>Courier your video to us,
recorded on a DVD.</i>

1181
01:02:18,666 --> 01:02:20,458
<i>We will air your video
in the coming weeks.</i>

1182
01:02:22,458 --> 01:02:23,625
{\an8}Hello, and Vanakkam,
this is Adam speaking.

1183
01:02:23,708 --> 01:02:26,041
{\an8}I'm happy to meet you all
in the Superstar special show.

1184
01:02:26,208 --> 01:02:28,375
{\an8}Today, Enthiran has been released,

1185
01:02:28,458 --> 01:02:31,250
{\an8}and Superstar's fans are celebrating
in theaters worldwide.

1186
01:02:31,416 --> 01:02:34,500
{\an8}Let's see who's the first lucky caller
on this show.

1187
01:02:34,583 --> 01:02:36,041
{\an8}- Hello!
<i>- Hello...</i>

1188
01:02:36,291 --> 01:02:37,916
{\an8}<i>Am I speaking to VJ Adams?</i>

1189
01:02:38,333 --> 01:02:39,333
{\an8}Yeah, tell me.

1190
01:02:40,041 --> 01:02:42,708
{\an8}<i>I'm calling from Rajini sir's residence.</i>

1191
01:02:43,916 --> 01:02:45,541
{\an8}<i>Sir would like to speak to you.</i>

1192
01:02:45,666 --> 01:02:47,583
{\an8}<i>One minute.
I'll pass the phone to him.</i>

1193
01:02:48,041 --> 01:02:49,125
{\an8}Please give him the phone.

1194
01:02:51,041 --> 01:02:52,916
Good morning, Adams.
This is Rajinikanth speaking.

1195
01:02:55,541 --> 01:02:57,083
{\an8}Sir, very good morning, sir.

1196
01:02:58,125 --> 01:02:59,333
Dear, how are you?

1197
01:02:59,500 --> 01:03:00,958
I'm a big fan of your show.
Good job!

1198
01:03:01,208 --> 01:03:02,833
Fantastic! Hats off! Hats off!

1199
01:03:02,916 --> 01:03:05,458
{\an8}Sir! Sir! I'm doing extremely well.

1200
01:03:05,583 --> 01:03:07,333
{\an8}Sir, I'm at a loss for words.

1201
01:03:07,541 --> 01:03:09,000
{\an8}Sir, I'm a big fan of yours.

1202
01:03:10,333 --> 01:03:11,916
I heard, Adams.
Thank you. Thank you.

1203
01:03:12,708 --> 01:03:15,500
{\an8}Sir, I have come to your doorstep
on each of your birthdays.

1204
01:03:15,583 --> 01:03:18,625
Oh, no, what's this, dear?
Why didn't you call me?

1205
01:03:18,833 --> 01:03:21,291
{\an8}Sir, how could I?
I don't have your number.

1206
01:03:21,375 --> 01:03:22,625
{\an8}Come on, Adams.

1207
01:03:22,708 --> 01:03:25,000
It's, after all, a number.
Here, note it down.

1208
01:03:25,083 --> 01:03:26,791
{\an8}90941133...

1209
01:03:34,166 --> 01:03:36,625
{\an8}Sir, you gave your number
over live telecast.

1210
01:03:38,833 --> 01:03:40,666
Are you serious, Adams?
Isn't this your personal number?

1211
01:03:40,750 --> 01:03:43,208
{\an8}Sir, you called in to a live show.

1212
01:03:43,291 --> 01:03:44,291
What's all this, dear?

1213
01:03:44,416 --> 01:03:45,416
Remove the number during the edit.

1214
01:03:45,541 --> 01:03:47,416
{\an8}Sir, it's already live.

1215
01:03:47,583 --> 01:03:48,875
{\an8}<i>How could this happen?</i>

1216
01:03:48,958 --> 01:03:50,500
Please request everyone not to call me.

1217
01:03:50,666 --> 01:03:52,000
{\an8}Alaikum Salaam. God bless you.

1218
01:03:53,458 --> 01:03:54,333
{\an8}Sir!

1219
01:03:54,750 --> 01:03:56,750
{\an8}To all the audiences watching the show.

1220
01:03:56,875 --> 01:03:58,875
{\an8}For God's sake,
don't call and trouble him.

1221
01:03:59,000 --> 01:04:01,500
{\an8}And in the history of Television,

1222
01:04:01,583 --> 01:04:03,166
{\an8}this is the only show where
Rajini sir called in.

1223
01:04:03,375 --> 01:04:05,916
{\an8}And I'm the only host who spoke to him,
and here's a song for you.

1224
01:04:06,208 --> 01:04:07,125
{\an8}I'm going to speak to him.

1225
01:04:07,416 --> 01:04:08,291
Here you go, Sir!

1226
01:04:11,083 --> 01:04:13,000
- Hello?
- Thalaiva! My God!

1227
01:04:13,083 --> 01:04:14,416
{\an8}<i>This is Erode Hari speaking.</i>

1228
01:04:14,500 --> 01:04:17,250
{\an8}<i>I'm your ardent fan.
I installed a 60-foot cut-out for you.</i>

1229
01:04:17,666 --> 01:04:18,541
Wrong number, Sir.

1230
01:04:18,625 --> 01:04:22,208
{\an8}<i>-Thalaiva, you looked like a real Robot!</i>
- I'm not a robot, but a human.

1231
01:04:23,041 --> 01:04:26,000
Are you going to work
or just speak over the phone?

1232
01:04:26,083 --> 01:04:27,416
Hey, please wait!

1233
01:04:29,916 --> 01:04:31,958
<i>I worship you like a God.</i>

1234
01:04:32,125 --> 01:04:33,333
Hey, I'm not a God!

1235
01:04:33,958 --> 01:04:34,833
Hand me your card!

1236
01:04:36,750 --> 01:04:37,625
Hey!

1237
01:04:38,083 --> 01:04:38,958
Who the hell are you?

1238
01:04:39,458 --> 01:04:42,000
How long should I wait?
You're always on the phone.

1239
01:04:42,083 --> 01:04:43,208
Hey, please stay silent.

1240
01:04:43,291 --> 01:04:44,750
<i>I'm your devotee!</i>

1241
01:04:44,833 --> 01:04:46,166
Devotee? Whose devotee?

1242
01:04:46,250 --> 01:04:47,291
I'm warning you. Hey!

1243
01:04:47,375 --> 01:04:48,375
Hey, what the hell?

1244
01:04:48,500 --> 01:04:49,666
Next movie update?

1245
01:04:50,000 --> 01:04:50,875
Who are you?

1246
01:04:51,166 --> 01:04:52,041
Hey!

1247
01:04:52,250 --> 01:04:53,125
Hang up!

1248
01:04:53,208 --> 01:04:54,083
Hang up!

1249
01:04:54,666 --> 01:04:56,458
{\an8}Are you going to take our payments,
or shall I file a complaint against you?

1250
01:04:56,541 --> 01:04:57,416
{\an8}Hey, shut up!

1251
01:05:33,583 --> 01:05:36,083
Saravana, can you manage?

1252
01:05:36,208 --> 01:05:37,083
Okay, Sir.

1253
01:05:37,166 --> 01:05:38,500
Everyone, shift to that queue.

1254
01:06:09,916 --> 01:06:10,791
Buddy, over here.

1255
01:06:11,708 --> 01:06:13,750
Look, there are 10 crores in it.

1256
01:06:14,000 --> 01:06:17,166
Fine, inform the investor
that we'll return it in 2 days.

1257
01:06:17,333 --> 01:06:18,208
Okay, Buddy.

1258
01:06:18,375 --> 01:06:20,041
I'm borrowing from you
for the first time.

1259
01:06:22,250 --> 01:06:23,500
- Bye, Buddy!
- Bye.

1260
01:06:42,125 --> 01:06:43,875
<i>Saravana, did you watch the news?</i>

1261
01:06:43,958 --> 01:06:45,750
<i>Someone has murdered Sabari.</i>

1262
01:06:47,458 --> 01:06:49,458
{\an8}<i>Popular businessman
Bhaskar's son Sabari,</i>

1263
01:06:49,541 --> 01:06:51,333
<i>during an illegal business deal,</i>

1264
01:06:51,416 --> 01:06:53,833
{\an8}<i>was shot dead in a crossfire
between two gangs.</i>

1265
01:06:53,916 --> 01:06:56,500
{\an8}<i>A special squad has been assigned
to nab the killers,</i>

1266
01:06:56,583 --> 01:06:57,958
{\an8}<i>and an investigation is underway.</i>

1267
01:07:02,500 --> 01:07:04,541
It's better if you leave from here.
Get out!

1268
01:07:06,291 --> 01:07:08,708
- He was my only son.
<i>- I told you not to yell and leave.</i>

1269
01:07:09,083 --> 01:07:10,500
Sabari...

1270
01:07:11,791 --> 01:07:13,291
Oh, God, no!

1271
01:07:13,708 --> 01:07:16,666
- Saravana, Sabari...
- Sit down.

1272
01:07:18,416 --> 01:07:20,625
- Sit down.
- Please look at me, Son.

1273
01:07:21,916 --> 01:07:23,208
Sabari!

1274
01:07:24,958 --> 01:07:27,083
Who's going to call me mother anymore?

1275
01:07:27,333 --> 01:07:28,708
Please look at me.

1276
01:07:28,875 --> 01:07:30,291
You never paid heed to me.

1277
01:07:30,625 --> 01:07:31,958
And now I'm here without a son.

1278
01:07:33,375 --> 01:07:36,583
Hey, Murthy, find out who shot him.

1279
01:07:36,666 --> 01:07:39,083
- Oh, no!
- No one should be spared alive.

1280
01:07:52,458 --> 01:07:54,166
<i>There's 25,000 in it.</i>

1281
01:07:54,500 --> 01:07:56,541
<i>Use this to pay this month's EMI.
We'll handle the rest later.</i>

1282
01:07:57,833 --> 01:07:59,458
<i>I'm borrowing from you
for the first time.</i>

1283
01:08:14,833 --> 01:08:18,166
<i>Think about it. If you don't have
any problem, make the arrangement.</i>

1284
01:08:20,875 --> 01:08:22,958
Didn't you request help through
Rambo Trust for treatment 4 months ago?

1285
01:08:23,041 --> 01:08:25,250
No, Brother.
My treatment was over 2 years ago.

1286
01:08:26,083 --> 01:08:27,458
Two years, you say?

1287
01:08:31,833 --> 01:08:33,250
Do you know the value of a Trust?

1288
01:08:33,333 --> 01:08:35,291
It's a grave sin to break one's trust.

1289
01:08:36,916 --> 01:08:38,833
A person came home claiming
he was the owner of the house.

1290
01:08:38,958 --> 01:08:41,625
In 10 days, if you don't return
the money to the respective people,

1291
01:08:41,750 --> 01:08:43,208
I'll file a complaint with the police.

1292
01:08:43,375 --> 01:08:46,750
Many fraudsters are roaming around
claiming they're homeowners.

1293
01:08:46,833 --> 01:08:48,000
Don't trust anyone.

1294
01:08:48,083 --> 01:08:50,375
Mithra, it's the 10th of the month.
You haven't paid the rent.

1295
01:08:50,458 --> 01:08:52,291
There's an issue with the bank.

1296
01:08:52,375 --> 01:08:53,750
You'll get your rent in 5 days.

1297
01:08:54,000 --> 01:08:55,125
I will handle it.

1298
01:08:55,208 --> 01:08:56,791
It's because of you we're in this pickle.

1299
01:08:56,875 --> 01:08:58,750
Chutti Anna,
did you happen to see Saravana?

1300
01:08:59,208 --> 01:09:02,916
I've been trying for 20 days
his phone is not reachable.

1301
01:09:10,125 --> 01:09:11,083
You haven't paid rent in a while.

1302
01:09:11,166 --> 01:09:12,458
We signed everything at Standard Property.

1303
01:09:12,541 --> 01:09:13,708
Standard Property is a scam, Sir.

1304
01:09:13,791 --> 01:09:15,541
She's a fraud, and so is her company.

1305
01:09:15,625 --> 01:09:17,916
- I'll take you to the Police station.
- File a complaint, damn it!

1306
01:09:18,041 --> 01:09:20,083
- Who are you?
- I'm the house owner.

1307
01:09:20,458 --> 01:09:21,541
Please repeat what you said.

1308
01:09:21,625 --> 01:09:23,375
I'm the house owner.
How many times should I repeat?

1309
01:09:23,458 --> 01:09:25,041
I ought to!
How many will claim the same?

1310
01:09:25,125 --> 01:09:26,000
Why are you beating me up?

1311
01:09:26,083 --> 01:09:26,958
How many of you are out there?

1312
01:09:27,041 --> 01:09:28,083
- Why are you beating me?
- I will beat you!

1313
01:09:28,250 --> 01:09:30,166
{\an8}<i>Jacky and Janaki,</i>

1314
01:09:30,250 --> 01:09:33,833
{\an8}<i>in the name of Rambo Trust,
conned many and swindled money.</i>

1315
01:09:33,916 --> 01:09:35,166
<i>A pregnant woman, Mithra,</i>

1316
01:09:35,250 --> 01:09:38,291
<i>in the pretense of leasing out a house,
has scammed many people.</i>

1317
01:09:38,375 --> 01:09:40,041
We are all educated, yet we got conned.

1318
01:09:40,125 --> 01:09:42,458
I don't know who truly is my house owner.

1319
01:09:47,708 --> 01:09:48,625
How can I claim
I did not pay the EB bill?

1320
01:09:48,708 --> 01:09:51,208
Listen, I paid my bill.
I will file a complaint.

1321
01:09:51,291 --> 01:09:52,583
- This is fraud.
- Who is a fraud?

1322
01:09:52,708 --> 01:09:53,958
- I have been paying regularly.
- You or me?

1323
01:09:54,041 --> 01:09:55,583
Manual receipt.

1324
01:09:55,666 --> 01:09:57,708
Please leave now
and come back in the evening.

1325
01:09:59,208 --> 01:10:00,750
Saravana is a good boy.

1326
01:10:04,000 --> 01:10:06,333
Saravana... I don't think so.

1327
01:10:06,416 --> 01:10:07,958
What?
Why would they shut down power?

1328
01:10:10,166 --> 01:10:11,375
All are manual receipts.

1329
01:10:11,458 --> 01:10:13,666
I'll call you. Please sit down.
I'll call you. Please sit down.

1330
01:10:13,916 --> 01:10:15,125
- Hey, where's the EB money?
- Dad!

1331
01:10:15,208 --> 01:10:17,041
- You better confess.
- Dad, I did not take it.

1332
01:10:17,166 --> 01:10:19,250
{\an8}Saravana...
I'll call you all one by one.

1333
01:10:19,500 --> 01:10:21,708
They left the fuse right here.

1334
01:10:29,041 --> 01:10:30,125
Hey, Saravana!

1335
01:10:41,875 --> 01:10:43,916
<i>- Operator!
- Hey, Operator!</i>

1336
01:10:45,166 --> 01:10:47,625
Why would they
switch off the power in a theater?

1337
01:10:47,791 --> 01:10:50,000
It's a crucial scene.
And they chose to cut the power.

1338
01:10:50,083 --> 01:10:50,958
I'm worked up!

1339
01:10:51,375 --> 01:10:52,375
You're right!

1340
01:10:52,916 --> 01:10:54,458
Hey, Gangadhara, I warned you.

1341
01:10:54,541 --> 01:10:56,916
The printer kept getting busted,
and I knew something fishy was going on.

1342
01:10:57,125 --> 01:10:58,000
You never listened!

1343
01:10:58,083 --> 01:10:59,125
You were coddling him.

1344
01:10:59,250 --> 01:11:01,583
He kept issuing manual receipts
and screwed us over.

1345
01:11:01,666 --> 01:11:03,333
You kept yelling
that you'll take responsibility.

1346
01:11:03,416 --> 01:11:04,291
Stop it!

1347
01:11:04,625 --> 01:11:06,791
I'm already very pissed off.

1348
01:11:08,916 --> 01:11:10,333
Sir, sir, sir, don't do it.

1349
01:11:10,416 --> 01:11:11,416
Hey, don't go inside!

1350
01:11:11,500 --> 01:11:13,875
Hey! Hey! Hey, step aside.

1351
01:11:13,958 --> 01:11:14,875
Do you know who he is?

1352
01:11:14,958 --> 01:11:16,166
- First, tell me, who are you?
- Do you not know me?

1353
01:11:16,250 --> 01:11:18,625
I'm the one who answers the phone
when you call the EB office.

1354
01:11:18,708 --> 01:11:20,041
- Oh, it's you!
- Yeah!

1355
01:11:20,125 --> 01:11:21,583
Oh, why are you beating me up?

1356
01:11:21,833 --> 01:11:23,375
How dare you not answer our calls?

1357
01:11:23,458 --> 01:11:24,875
Sir, they're carrying me.

1358
01:11:24,958 --> 01:11:26,250
- Wait, wait!
- Hey, carry and throw him away.

1359
01:11:26,333 --> 01:11:28,208
- They whacked me.
- I saw.

1360
01:11:28,375 --> 01:11:29,708
It's all because of you.

1361
01:11:29,791 --> 01:11:31,541
Sir, they're flying me in the air
like a kite.

1362
01:11:31,625 --> 01:11:32,791
- Please save me, Sir.
- Oh, no!

1363
01:11:32,875 --> 01:11:33,833
I'm afraid of heights.

1364
01:11:33,916 --> 01:11:36,541
Why are they carrying him like Superman?

1365
01:11:36,625 --> 01:11:38,250
They're carrying me
like the ants carrying their food.

1366
01:11:38,333 --> 01:11:39,291
Hey, put him down, people.

1367
01:11:39,375 --> 01:11:40,291
Please calm down.

1368
01:11:40,375 --> 01:11:42,083
You cut off our electricity
and are living in luxury here.

1369
01:11:43,708 --> 01:11:45,375
Sir, I can't take it anymore.

1370
01:12:03,333 --> 01:12:05,041
Bloody sinners. Please spare me.

1371
01:12:05,125 --> 01:12:11,291
In my experience,
I've never witnessed such a sequence.

1372
01:12:11,875 --> 01:12:13,958
It's very pathetic!

1373
01:12:14,166 --> 01:12:15,666
{\an8}<i>It has now come to light</i>

1374
01:12:15,750 --> 01:12:18,958
<i>that an EB official collected
electricity bill payments from the public,</i>

1375
01:12:19,041 --> 01:12:21,958
<i>issued fake receipts,
and swindled crores of rupees.</i>

1376
01:12:33,125 --> 01:12:34,291
Why is there no electricity
at the station?

1377
01:12:34,375 --> 01:12:35,291
What's with the commotion?

1378
01:12:44,375 --> 01:12:46,625
Tell me, where you have hidden the money?

1379
01:12:50,625 --> 01:12:52,083
NAME - JANAKI
AGE - 55

1380
01:12:52,333 --> 01:12:53,791
NAME - JACKIE
AGE - 25

1381
01:12:54,375 --> 01:12:56,041
NAME - MITHRA
AGE - 23

1382
01:12:56,541 --> 01:12:58,000
NAME - SARAVANA
AGE - 25

1383
01:13:02,125 --> 01:13:03,750
Sir, his face is visible in this clip.

1384
01:13:04,333 --> 01:13:05,708
He took away your son.

1385
01:13:12,125 --> 01:13:13,125
Kalyana Sundaram!

1386
01:13:31,583 --> 01:13:35,625
<i>Mangalapuram witnessed a series
of different scams in a single day.</i>

1387
01:13:35,708 --> 01:13:39,291
You used donations as a pretext
to scam countless people.

1388
01:13:39,375 --> 01:13:40,333
Don't you feel ashamed?

1389
01:13:40,416 --> 01:13:42,458
<i>Jacky and Janaki,</i>

1390
01:13:42,541 --> 01:13:47,208
<i>using the Rambo Trust as a front,
conned people out of their money.</i>

1391
01:13:47,291 --> 01:13:48,500
Where have you stashed the money?

1392
01:13:48,750 --> 01:13:50,000
<i>A pregnant woman Mithra,</i>

1393
01:13:50,083 --> 01:13:53,791
<i>in the pretense of leasing out a house,
has scammed many people.</i>

1394
01:13:54,416 --> 01:13:55,833
Where have you stashed the money?

1395
01:13:56,541 --> 01:13:57,416
Tell me!

1396
01:13:57,500 --> 01:13:59,041
<i>An EB officer, Saravanan,</i>

1397
01:13:59,125 --> 01:14:02,541
<i>pocketed electricity bill payments
by issuing fake receipts,</i>

1398
01:14:02,625 --> 01:14:04,833
<i>swindling crores.</i>

1399
01:14:04,916 --> 01:14:06,833
<i>Also, he started something
called Quick Money.</i>

1400
01:14:06,916 --> 01:14:09,166
<i>He swindled more
from the people for Mangalapuram.</i>

1401
01:14:09,250 --> 01:14:12,166
<i>Has come to the authorities' notice.</i>

1402
01:14:12,250 --> 01:14:14,708
"Saravana has been arrested
by the police."

1403
01:14:18,708 --> 01:14:20,625
Madam, you can't do this
inside the Police station.

1404
01:14:20,833 --> 01:14:22,208
Sir, please take her away.

1405
01:14:22,875 --> 01:14:24,333
You bloody fraud!

1406
01:14:25,416 --> 01:14:27,541
I can't believe
I was in love with you all these years.

1407
01:14:29,916 --> 01:14:30,833
Sorry, Aishu.

1408
01:14:37,583 --> 01:14:40,541
Despite you being in debt, I was ready
to get my daughter married to you.

1409
01:14:41,208 --> 01:14:44,500
I never imagined you were a con artist.

1410
01:14:46,500 --> 01:14:48,916
It's a good thing we learned your
true nature before the wedding.

1411
01:14:56,500 --> 01:14:59,458
Hey! We've seen plenty of people
put on an act in front of the police.

1412
01:14:59,541 --> 01:15:01,916
Don't hide the truth and confess.
That would be good for you.

1413
01:15:02,041 --> 01:15:03,375
- Where did you stash the money?
- I am...

1414
01:15:03,750 --> 01:15:05,333
...telling the truth, Sir.

1415
01:15:05,958 --> 01:15:06,916
The money is with Sabari.

1416
01:15:09,416 --> 01:15:12,125
You better confess where you stashed it
or who's holding the money?

1417
01:15:12,208 --> 01:15:13,791
I swear I gave it to Saravana.

1418
01:15:15,291 --> 01:15:16,166
Saravanan?

1419
01:15:16,250 --> 01:15:18,708
Why is everyone pointing at Saravanan?

1420
01:15:19,708 --> 01:15:21,666
Are you trying to blame him and escape?

1421
01:15:21,791 --> 01:15:25,000
Sir, I swear
I gave the money to Saravana!

1422
01:15:28,166 --> 01:15:30,666
Every one of you is pointing at Saravanan.

1423
01:15:30,750 --> 01:15:33,416
You'd better confess where you stashed
the money you looted from the Trust.

1424
01:15:33,500 --> 01:15:34,416
Confess, damn it!

1425
01:15:36,166 --> 01:15:37,125
Tell him!

1426
01:15:37,541 --> 01:15:38,541
Speak up!

1427
01:15:39,041 --> 01:15:41,375
Sir, in the next cell,

1428
01:15:42,000 --> 01:15:43,833
there is Saravanan.
I gave him the money.

1429
01:15:43,916 --> 01:15:44,791
Hey!

1430
01:15:52,375 --> 01:15:54,958
Sir, I feel sorry for this old woman.

1431
01:15:55,125 --> 01:15:57,666
But this man looks like a criminal.

1432
01:15:58,625 --> 01:16:01,958
You look like my daughter,
who went missing when she was a child.

1433
01:16:02,583 --> 01:16:04,791
I'm your son, standing right beside you,
yet you still choose to lie.

1434
01:16:05,500 --> 01:16:06,833
Am I not your only son?

1435
01:16:08,041 --> 01:16:10,500
Are you guys putting up a family drama?

1436
01:16:10,583 --> 01:16:11,708
- Sir...
- You better confess!

1437
01:16:11,791 --> 01:16:14,375
Sir, I swear, we gave it to Saravanan...

1438
01:16:14,458 --> 01:16:16,875
Wait! I'm giving you one last chance.

1439
01:16:19,166 --> 01:16:20,083
Mocking me?

1440
01:16:20,375 --> 01:16:23,000
Sir, sir, sir, sir, sir! Oh, no!

1441
01:16:24,916 --> 01:16:27,041
You guys are pointing fingers
at each other.

1442
01:16:27,125 --> 01:16:28,541
You people are lying one after the other.

1443
01:16:28,625 --> 01:16:31,583
Confess now and tell us
where you've hidden the cash.

1444
01:16:31,791 --> 01:16:33,375
Didn't I give it to you?
Tell him.

1445
01:16:33,500 --> 01:16:34,833
I gave the money to you.

1446
01:16:34,916 --> 01:16:37,541
Saravana, we gave you the money.
Please give up the location.

1447
01:16:37,625 --> 01:16:39,083
I swear
I gave all the money to my friend.

1448
01:16:39,458 --> 01:16:40,458
But now he's dead.

1449
01:16:40,541 --> 01:16:42,041
For no reason, don't get me beaten up.

1450
01:16:42,291 --> 01:16:44,041
Don't embarrass me in front of women.
Please tell the truth.

1451
01:16:44,166 --> 01:16:45,583
Sir, we gave him the money.

1452
01:16:45,916 --> 01:16:47,958
- He has the money.
- Sir, I gave him the money.

1453
01:16:48,041 --> 01:16:50,541
Hey, I'm certain now.

1454
01:16:50,750 --> 01:16:52,458
They're putting up a major act.

1455
01:16:53,750 --> 01:16:55,708
But one thing they've rehearsed well.

1456
01:16:56,166 --> 01:16:57,583
Pitch-perfect performances.

1457
01:17:02,250 --> 01:17:03,125
Yes, Sir.

1458
01:17:04,000 --> 01:17:04,875
Yes!

1459
01:17:06,208 --> 01:17:07,083
Yes, Sir.

1460
01:17:09,500 --> 01:17:10,500
Encounter?

1461
01:17:11,208 --> 01:17:12,125
Did he mention an encounter?

1462
01:17:12,666 --> 01:17:13,625
Encounter?

1463
01:17:13,708 --> 01:17:14,875
I'll make the arrangements.

1464
01:17:20,750 --> 01:17:22,958
Hey, show me your hands.

1465
01:17:24,750 --> 01:17:25,625
Show me your bloody hands!

1466
01:17:35,375 --> 01:17:36,958
- Sir, let's escape.
- Hey, let go of me!

1467
01:17:37,041 --> 01:17:37,916
Hey!

1468
01:17:38,000 --> 01:17:39,958
- Hey, cuff him!
- Let go of me!

1469
01:17:41,083 --> 01:17:42,791
- Bloody man.
- Mom, let's go.

1470
01:17:42,875 --> 01:17:43,875
Let's go!

1471
01:17:47,916 --> 01:17:49,750
Hey, where are the accused?

1472
01:17:52,041 --> 01:17:53,083
Why did you let them escape?

1473
01:18:06,500 --> 01:18:07,416
Here's the thing.

1474
01:18:08,125 --> 01:18:09,208
This vehicle is headed to Karnataka.

1475
01:18:09,833 --> 01:18:10,875
I'll get dropped here.

1476
01:18:11,375 --> 01:18:12,708
Wherever you people wish to go,

1477
01:18:13,583 --> 01:18:14,750
please go safely.

1478
01:18:14,833 --> 01:18:15,708
Safely?

1479
01:18:16,291 --> 01:18:19,958
Boss, you return my money
and go wherever you wish.

1480
01:18:20,041 --> 01:18:22,041
Return my money,
and I'll be on my way.

1481
01:18:22,125 --> 01:18:23,708
Don't you guys believe anything I said?

1482
01:18:24,333 --> 01:18:25,666
I swear I don't have the money.

1483
01:18:26,250 --> 01:18:28,916
I gave the money to my friend,
and now he's dead.

1484
01:18:29,208 --> 01:18:30,125
- Hey!
- One day...

1485
01:18:30,750 --> 01:18:33,291
I'm a con artist myself,
and you're trying to con me.

1486
01:18:33,375 --> 01:18:36,333
You're trying to get rid of us
and swindle all the money.

1487
01:18:36,416 --> 01:18:38,291
Hey, I won't let it happen!

1488
01:18:38,375 --> 01:18:41,375
- You better return my 42 lakhs--
- Hey, fool!

1489
01:18:42,208 --> 01:18:43,208
It's 53 lakhs.

1490
01:18:43,583 --> 01:18:45,875
Yeah, if you don't return my 53 lakhs...

1491
01:18:46,041 --> 01:18:47,958
I won't spare you.
Pay up, damn it!

1492
01:18:48,041 --> 01:18:51,541
Right! Return my 82 lakhs,
and go wherever you wish.

1493
01:18:51,625 --> 01:18:52,916
82 lakhs?

1494
01:18:53,625 --> 01:18:55,583
You have invested more than we have.

1495
01:18:56,500 --> 01:18:57,750
You people still do not
understand the situation.

1496
01:18:59,375 --> 01:19:01,458
Like you, many people have
entrusted me with their money.

1497
01:19:01,791 --> 01:19:03,791
I have no idea
how I am going to return it.

1498
01:19:04,625 --> 01:19:05,708
But I swear I will return it.

1499
01:19:06,250 --> 01:19:07,791
Right now, I don't have the money.

1500
01:19:08,083 --> 01:19:09,041
I understand, Son.

1501
01:19:09,791 --> 01:19:11,333
I understand your problem.

1502
01:19:11,416 --> 01:19:12,333
What do you understand?

1503
01:19:12,416 --> 01:19:14,541
Hey, he's promising to return the money.

1504
01:19:16,375 --> 01:19:17,833
How long would it take
for you to return it?

1505
01:19:19,041 --> 01:19:22,000
Mom, I'm extremely pissed!

1506
01:19:22,125 --> 01:19:23,500
Right from the beginning,
I was against it.

1507
01:19:23,625 --> 01:19:24,541
But you dragged me into this.

1508
01:19:24,625 --> 01:19:26,375
Because of him,
I got thrashed in the Police station.

1509
01:19:26,458 --> 01:19:27,750
Right now, we're running from the law.

1510
01:19:27,833 --> 01:19:29,833
And you're supporting him.
Shut up!

1511
01:19:30,250 --> 01:19:32,666
Hey, I want my money back.

1512
01:19:33,291 --> 01:19:34,541
If I intended to cheat you all...

1513
01:19:35,083 --> 01:19:37,166
why would I break you all
out of the prison?

1514
01:19:37,250 --> 01:19:40,333
Hey, you're the reason
the Police caught us?

1515
01:19:40,666 --> 01:19:41,625
But you're speaking like a saint.

1516
01:19:41,708 --> 01:19:43,833
Listen, I don't care about them.

1517
01:19:43,916 --> 01:19:45,000
I want my money.

1518
01:19:45,250 --> 01:19:46,666
Without the money, I won't leave.

1519
01:19:46,750 --> 01:19:50,791
Bloody, you can't move from here
until you return my money.

1520
01:19:50,875 --> 01:19:52,333
- I'll kill you!
- Sir, in Tamil cinema...

1521
01:19:52,416 --> 01:19:53,500
you're going to be a popular Hero.

1522
01:19:53,583 --> 01:19:54,583
How could you behave like this?

1523
01:19:54,708 --> 01:19:57,333
Looking at your actions,
I won't even become a junior artist.

1524
01:19:57,416 --> 01:19:58,375
Hey, return my money.

1525
01:19:58,500 --> 01:20:00,083
- Return my money!
- Sir! Sir!

1526
01:20:00,541 --> 01:20:01,458
Sir, let go of me.

1527
01:20:02,583 --> 01:20:05,125
<i>The gang of fraudsters
escaped from police custody.</i>

1528
01:20:05,208 --> 01:20:06,583
<i>The police are looking for them.</i>

1529
01:20:13,625 --> 01:20:14,583
Kalyana Sundaram.

1530
01:20:16,625 --> 01:20:17,583
Sir!

1531
01:20:19,041 --> 01:20:21,000
The Principal has summoned you.

1532
01:20:22,041 --> 01:20:22,916
I'm coming.

1533
01:20:23,375 --> 01:20:26,041
Let's go immediately
and file a complaint with the Police.

1534
01:20:26,125 --> 01:20:27,375
Meanwhile, I'll go and meet the Principal.

1535
01:20:29,416 --> 01:20:30,333
Police!

1536
01:20:51,208 --> 01:20:54,041
Kalyana Sundaram figured out
where we were hiding.

1537
01:20:55,541 --> 01:20:56,833
That's why he kidnapped Jeeva.

1538
01:20:57,125 --> 01:20:58,666
Why did he even kidnap Jeeva?

1539
01:20:59,416 --> 01:21:00,541
He's a child.

1540
01:21:01,416 --> 01:21:03,000
He did not do anything.
He's innocent.

1541
01:21:03,250 --> 01:21:05,000
Only if he kidnaps the child
could he get to us.

1542
01:21:05,083 --> 01:21:06,541
I'm well aware
of Kalyana Sundaram's traits.

1543
01:21:07,208 --> 01:21:10,083
If he gets to us, he'll kill us for sure.

1544
01:21:11,416 --> 01:21:13,541
Wait, let's see what Saravanan has to say.

1545
01:21:14,166 --> 01:21:15,916
Once he's here, we'll discuss it.

1546
01:21:16,041 --> 01:21:17,958
What do you think he's going to say?

1547
01:21:18,916 --> 01:21:21,208
If you bring him up again,
I'll get pissed.

1548
01:21:21,333 --> 01:21:22,500
He's the reason
we've been staying hidden for years.

1549
01:21:22,583 --> 01:21:24,875
Still, you think he's going to fix it.

1550
01:21:25,250 --> 01:21:26,583
He wouldn't have left
if it were his child.

1551
01:21:27,083 --> 01:21:28,125
Tell me!

1552
01:21:28,208 --> 01:21:29,833
He must have already fled town.

1553
01:21:30,041 --> 01:21:31,083
He's not coming back!

1554
01:21:31,541 --> 01:21:32,833
Yet you're supporting him--

1555
01:21:41,041 --> 01:21:42,083
I did not run away.

1556
01:21:44,875 --> 01:21:45,958
I came to inform you all before leaving.

1557
01:21:47,708 --> 01:21:48,916
I'm going to Mangalapuram.

1558
01:21:51,750 --> 01:21:53,583
I know you people are angry with me.

1559
01:21:58,166 --> 01:21:59,625
I'm the root cause of all the problems.

1560
01:22:01,958 --> 01:22:03,041
I will fix it!

1561
01:22:05,416 --> 01:22:08,583
Are you all wondering if I really mean it?

1562
01:22:10,083 --> 01:22:11,041
Maybe...

1563
01:22:13,375 --> 01:22:14,250
I'm not

1564
01:22:16,333 --> 01:22:17,958
Jeeva's biological father.

1565
01:22:21,375 --> 01:22:23,125
However, according to Jeeva...

1566
01:22:27,375 --> 01:22:28,375
I'm his father!

1567
01:22:34,291 --> 01:22:35,250
He must be anticipating...

1568
01:22:38,291 --> 01:22:39,958
that I'll come and save him.

1569
01:22:47,833 --> 01:22:48,875
You, people, don't have to come with me.

1570
01:22:52,375 --> 01:22:53,250
I'm leaving.

1571
01:22:54,000 --> 01:22:54,875
Saravana!

1572
01:22:55,916 --> 01:22:57,250
I'm coming with you too.

1573
01:22:57,333 --> 01:23:00,791
<i>My love, are you the song of my life?</i>

1574
01:23:01,291 --> 01:23:03,791
<i>My whole world lives in you</i>

1575
01:23:03,875 --> 01:23:06,333
Mithra, what are you waiting for?

1576
01:23:08,625 --> 01:23:09,500
Let's go!

1577
01:23:25,583 --> 01:23:29,041
<i>My sky, my moon</i>

1578
01:23:29,583 --> 01:23:33,250
{\an8}<i>You are the meaning of my life</i>

1579
01:23:33,625 --> 01:23:37,125
<i>Everywhere I look,
I see your face,</i>

1580
01:23:37,541 --> 01:23:41,291
<i>For you are my precious one</i>

1581
01:23:41,708 --> 01:23:45,083
<i>My love, are you the song of my life?</i>

1582
01:23:45,666 --> 01:23:48,916
<i>My whole world lives in you</i>

1583
01:23:50,125 --> 01:23:51,041
Dad...

1584
01:23:51,625 --> 01:23:52,625
...Da!

1585
01:23:52,708 --> 01:23:59,625
<i>Shall I sing to you as a father would?</i>

1586
01:24:00,666 --> 01:24:05,625
<i>For I sowed you within my very life,</i>

1587
01:24:05,958 --> 01:24:08,166
<i>My son</i>

1588
01:24:11,416 --> 01:24:15,291
<i>Listening to countless stories
In your baby babble...</i>

1589
01:24:15,375 --> 01:24:16,791
<i>Together in your playful mischief,</i>

1590
01:24:17,041 --> 01:24:19,333
<i>Your laughter turned our home
Into a song</i>

1591
01:24:19,416 --> 01:24:22,750
<i>Climb onto my shoulders, my son,</i>

1592
01:24:23,041 --> 01:24:26,833
<i>So that one day you may rise
Beyond me</i>

1593
01:24:27,375 --> 01:24:30,750
<i>Not for you to follow
In my footsteps forever,</i>

1594
01:24:31,083 --> 01:24:34,708
<i>But for you to go farther and faster
Than I ever did</i>

1595
01:24:35,333 --> 01:24:38,666
<i>Yet my love for you
Shall remain unchanged</i>

1596
01:24:39,375 --> 01:24:42,583
<i>May my affection never change</i>

1597
01:24:43,416 --> 01:24:48,041
{\an8}<i>For I planted you
Within my very life,</i>

1598
01:24:48,708 --> 01:24:51,416
<i>my son</i>

1599
01:24:51,500 --> 01:24:54,875
<i>My love, are you the song of my life?</i>

1600
01:24:55,333 --> 01:24:58,541
<i>- My whole world lives in you</i>
- Quickly make me a dosa, Mom.

1601
01:25:00,041 --> 01:25:02,250
- Grandma?
- Eat, my dear!

1602
01:25:03,333 --> 01:25:06,375
<i>Shall I sing to you as a father would?</i>

1603
01:25:15,250 --> 01:25:18,750
<i>My precious life,</i>

1604
01:25:19,375 --> 01:25:23,125
<i>Both my eyes search for you</i>

1605
01:25:23,375 --> 01:25:26,541
{\an8}<i>My dear son,</i>

1606
01:25:27,416 --> 01:25:31,250
<i>Let me sing a lullaby</i>

1607
01:25:31,333 --> 01:25:34,666
<i>My precious life,</i>

1608
01:25:35,375 --> 01:25:39,208
<i>Both my eyes search for you</i>

1609
01:25:39,416 --> 01:25:42,541
<i>Let me sing a lullaby</i>

1610
01:25:43,208 --> 01:25:47,000
{\an8}<i>Let me sing a lullaby</i>

1611
01:25:53,833 --> 01:25:57,333
Sir, we made a mistake by escaping
from your police station.

1612
01:25:57,916 --> 01:25:59,750
But they have nothing to do
with this matter.

1613
01:26:00,416 --> 01:26:01,625
I'm the root cause of it.

1614
01:26:02,791 --> 01:26:03,958
I will surrender myself to the Police.

1615
01:26:06,666 --> 01:26:08,125
Oh!

1616
01:26:08,333 --> 01:26:12,125
So you people are under the
impression that you escaped from me?

1617
01:26:13,208 --> 01:26:16,250
I let you all escape.

1618
01:26:28,875 --> 01:26:29,958
Let them escape.

1619
01:26:33,708 --> 01:26:35,125
I'm not in the service anymore.

1620
01:26:35,208 --> 01:26:36,583
I'm a retired officer now.

1621
01:26:36,833 --> 01:26:40,583
According to the people of Mangalapuram,
I'm an honest inspector.

1622
01:26:43,666 --> 01:26:45,916
<i>I upheld that name and retired
from the service.</i>

1623
01:26:46,250 --> 01:26:47,916
Please wait.
Please wait, Madam.

1624
01:26:48,000 --> 01:26:49,458
{\an8}What is your problem, people?

1625
01:26:49,541 --> 01:26:51,958
We were upset,
so we came to bid you goodbye.

1626
01:26:52,041 --> 01:26:53,625
{\an8}I'm not getting transferred.

1627
01:26:53,833 --> 01:26:55,875
<i>I'm just retiring.
I'm happy!</i>

1628
01:26:55,958 --> 01:26:58,750
<i>But those fools are unaware
of the other side of me.</i>

1629
01:26:58,833 --> 01:27:02,625
I'm the person who'd do anything
for the right price.

1630
01:27:04,041 --> 01:27:06,916
<i>Bribery, forgery, kidnapping,
fake encounters,</i>

1631
01:27:07,000 --> 01:27:08,625
<i>drug supply, I've done it all.</i>

1632
01:27:08,708 --> 01:27:11,250
<i>The only motive is money.</i>

1633
01:27:11,333 --> 01:27:15,750
<i>After retirement, until I die,
I wish to live rich.</i>

1634
01:27:15,833 --> 01:27:18,583
<i>After my retirement,
I had a lot of money.</i>

1635
01:27:18,666 --> 01:27:21,041
Initially, I started small-time betting.

1636
01:27:21,125 --> 01:27:22,000
I won!

1637
01:27:22,083 --> 01:27:25,166
<i>After that,
I got the desire to keep winning more.</i>

1638
01:27:25,250 --> 01:27:26,958
<i>Later, I lost everything in betting.</i>

1639
01:27:27,041 --> 01:27:29,833
{\an8}<i>In the end, I realized I lost everything.</i>

1640
01:27:31,416 --> 01:27:34,583
During my service,
I let many criminals, like you, escape.

1641
01:27:34,666 --> 01:27:35,666
Do you know why?

1642
01:27:36,208 --> 01:27:39,166
Because one day, you may end up
being useful to me.

1643
01:27:39,625 --> 01:27:41,958
I am aware that you people
are not that great at what you do.

1644
01:27:42,208 --> 01:27:43,791
<i>But I read your case files.</i>

1645
01:27:44,625 --> 01:27:46,958
At that point, you didn't seem like
small-timers either.

1646
01:27:51,125 --> 01:27:52,958
- Sir?
- Give the phone to the boy.

1647
01:27:53,041 --> 01:27:53,916
Okay, Sir.

1648
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:02,958
Hey! Your father wants to talk to you.

1649
01:28:03,250 --> 01:28:04,208
Here you go!

1650
01:28:05,875 --> 01:28:07,791
- That's awesome!
- It's a fluke.

1651
01:28:09,500 --> 01:28:10,458
Hello!

1652
01:28:11,458 --> 01:28:12,625
- Jeeva!
- Hey!

1653
01:28:14,166 --> 01:28:15,125
Dad?

1654
01:28:17,375 --> 01:28:19,833
Jeeva, this is Mom speaking.

1655
01:28:20,583 --> 01:28:22,708
I hope nothing's wrong and you're safe.

1656
01:28:22,916 --> 01:28:24,833
Nothing to worry, Mom, I'm safe.

1657
01:28:25,291 --> 01:28:29,291
But they have chained
my wheelchair to a pillar.

1658
01:28:29,375 --> 01:28:31,916
This place looks like a big factory.

1659
01:28:32,083 --> 01:28:33,833
But I don't know the location.

1660
01:28:33,916 --> 01:28:36,541
Right now, with me,
there are only two uncles.

1661
01:28:37,166 --> 01:28:38,916
Jeeva, did anyone out there hit you?

1662
01:28:39,291 --> 01:28:40,833
No, Dad, no one hit me.

1663
01:28:43,541 --> 01:28:44,458
Hello, Dad?

1664
01:28:44,708 --> 01:28:45,833
- Uncle!
- What is it?

1665
01:28:45,916 --> 01:28:47,791
The call got disconnected.
Here you go.

1666
01:28:51,458 --> 01:28:52,541
You dropped the catch.

1667
01:28:52,625 --> 01:28:54,583
Hey, shut up!

1668
01:28:57,500 --> 01:28:59,916
Until you people follow my orders...

1669
01:29:00,250 --> 01:29:02,083
Jeeva will be safe.

1670
01:29:03,541 --> 01:29:06,958
If you guys try to pull something smart...

1671
01:29:07,583 --> 01:29:09,000
he won't be alive.

1672
01:29:12,083 --> 01:29:13,416
I want money!

1673
01:29:13,958 --> 01:29:15,250
I want a lot of money!

1674
01:29:16,000 --> 01:29:21,666
I want enough wealth to last me
until I've had my fill of life.

1675
01:29:22,750 --> 01:29:28,208
It takes people like you to plan a scam
so carefully and pull it off flawlessly.

1676
01:29:29,250 --> 01:29:30,708
And I am certain about it.

1677
01:29:32,291 --> 01:29:33,791
Sir, we're not such people.

1678
01:29:34,791 --> 01:29:36,500
You have the wrong perspective about us.

1679
01:29:36,583 --> 01:29:38,750
Sir, from what you're asking...

1680
01:29:39,041 --> 01:29:42,625
I think you believe
we're holding crores somewhere.

1681
01:29:42,833 --> 01:29:44,708
How could we give you something
we don't have?

1682
01:29:45,333 --> 01:29:46,625
Then, forget about Jeeva.

1683
01:29:48,166 --> 01:29:49,458
Sir, we'll do whatever you ask of us.

1684
01:29:52,291 --> 01:29:53,291
But one condition.

1685
01:29:54,583 --> 01:29:56,000
If we deliver what you demand...

1686
01:29:56,791 --> 01:29:57,791
...you must release Jeeva.

1687
01:30:10,541 --> 01:30:12,541
He's holding Jeeva hostage
and asking us to make money for him.

1688
01:30:12,625 --> 01:30:14,000
And you've given him your word.

1689
01:30:14,083 --> 01:30:15,250
How could you agree to it?

1690
01:30:15,500 --> 01:30:17,583
What else to do?
It's not like he'll let us go scot-free.

1691
01:30:17,708 --> 01:30:21,083
I thought we'd outsmarted Kalyana Sundaram
for 7 years and gone into hiding.

1692
01:30:21,166 --> 01:30:22,250
In one second, he broke my bubble.

1693
01:30:23,125 --> 01:30:25,708
We did not cheat him
but got cheated by him.

1694
01:30:25,833 --> 01:30:27,625
He's not an ordinary man
like you peg him to be.

1695
01:30:28,166 --> 01:30:31,083
You don't get it.
He's asking us to get him crores.

1696
01:30:31,375 --> 01:30:33,750
- That means we have to steal again.
- We don't have another choice.

1697
01:30:34,250 --> 01:30:36,666
If that gets us back, Jeeva,
I'm ready to steal.

1698
01:30:37,041 --> 01:30:38,791
For God's sake, don't do anything.

1699
01:30:39,291 --> 01:30:41,833
Citing my son as an excuse,
I sinned a lot.

1700
01:30:42,791 --> 01:30:44,875
If he's in this situation,
it's our bad karma.

1701
01:30:47,208 --> 01:30:48,375
We keep piling on sins...

1702
01:30:48,958 --> 01:30:49,833
Forget about it.

1703
01:30:49,916 --> 01:30:52,500
Let's find another way to save Jeeva.

1704
01:30:53,125 --> 01:30:55,083
I spoke to him after thinking it through.

1705
01:30:55,166 --> 01:30:56,416
We don't have another choice.

1706
01:30:57,875 --> 01:30:59,083
Did you ever think about this?

1707
01:30:59,416 --> 01:31:01,583
We are all escaped criminals.

1708
01:31:03,041 --> 01:31:05,916
How do you expect us
to go unnoticed by the people?

1709
01:31:06,041 --> 01:31:07,416
Did you think it through?

1710
01:31:07,791 --> 01:31:11,208
We were in hiding for our previous crimes.

1711
01:31:11,958 --> 01:31:13,541
If we commit another crime
and get caught...

1712
01:31:14,166 --> 01:31:15,416
...they'll tear us apart.

1713
01:31:19,583 --> 01:31:20,500
But I have a solution.

1714
01:31:22,500 --> 01:31:23,375
We must do it.

1715
01:31:26,583 --> 01:31:28,416
We must do something
without getting caught.

1716
01:31:28,500 --> 01:31:30,333
If you have anything good,
then share it, damn it.

1717
01:31:30,458 --> 01:31:31,916
I don't know, either.
I'm thinking as well.

1718
01:31:32,000 --> 01:31:32,916
Please give me some time.

1719
01:31:34,125 --> 01:31:35,041
Time?

1720
01:31:35,916 --> 01:31:36,833
Take your time.

1721
01:31:37,000 --> 01:31:40,166
You have made us wait for 7 years
in the hope of getting our money back.

1722
01:31:40,791 --> 01:31:41,666
We'll keep waiting!

1723
01:31:44,166 --> 01:31:45,750
While you guys are waiting,

1724
01:31:46,166 --> 01:31:48,125
shall I make some tea?

1725
01:31:58,000 --> 01:31:59,625
Do you have faith that he'll save Jeeva?

1726
01:32:02,583 --> 01:32:03,541
I don't have faith in him.

1727
01:32:05,291 --> 01:32:07,583
I have a feeling
that he'll get us caught again.

1728
01:32:09,541 --> 01:32:10,458
Stay cautious!

1729
01:32:14,583 --> 01:32:16,416
This time we should not get caught.

1730
01:32:17,250 --> 01:32:18,958
It should be him.
Do you understand?

1731
01:32:23,208 --> 01:32:25,750
You overheard us
and are stepping out casually.

1732
01:32:27,208 --> 01:32:28,166
Get lost!

1733
01:32:31,291 --> 01:32:32,750
I'm sure you're going to
tell him everything.

1734
01:32:35,666 --> 01:32:37,750
Will you? Bloody hag!

1735
01:32:38,458 --> 01:32:40,291
She's become a nuisance.

1736
01:32:47,416 --> 01:32:48,875
<i>The printer broke down at the office.</i>

1737
01:32:52,125 --> 01:32:53,791
<i>We won't get caught using this technique.</i>

1738
01:33:06,333 --> 01:33:09,583
In Nigeria, they installed
a fake toll booth and swindled crores.

1739
01:33:09,666 --> 01:33:11,333
Nigeria is far-fetched.

1740
01:33:11,541 --> 01:33:13,458
You can find many similar cases in India.

1741
01:33:13,583 --> 01:33:15,291
How could anyone pull off such a big scam?

1742
01:33:15,375 --> 01:33:16,708
It may sound like a big scam.

1743
01:33:16,875 --> 01:33:17,750
Think about it.

1744
01:33:17,833 --> 01:33:19,416
Imagine someone installs a toll booth

1745
01:33:19,500 --> 01:33:21,333
on a road you take regularly
and asks for your money.

1746
01:33:21,916 --> 01:33:23,166
Are you going to ask them for proof?

1747
01:33:23,458 --> 01:33:24,875
You'd eventually pay the toll and move on.

1748
01:33:25,375 --> 01:33:28,958
Because people don't have the time
to question anyone.

1749
01:33:29,250 --> 01:33:30,500
That's how these scams are successful.

1750
01:33:30,666 --> 01:33:32,000
So, when are you getting caught?

1751
01:33:32,083 --> 01:33:35,375
- Hello! We're running the toll legally.
- Legal how?

1752
01:33:35,458 --> 01:33:38,750
<i>Within a 60-kilometer radius of Chennai,
there shouldn't be a single toll plaza.</i>

1753
01:33:38,833 --> 01:33:40,750
<i>But in Chennai, there are 6 toll booths.</i>

1754
01:33:40,833 --> 01:33:42,791
And two toll booths belong to your father.

1755
01:33:43,041 --> 01:33:46,250
If the Nigerian scamster is looting
by installing a fake toll booth...

1756
01:33:47,041 --> 01:33:48,833
...you're joining hands with the
department and scamming people.

1757
01:33:49,250 --> 01:33:51,291
- That's the difference!
- Don't act too smart. Get lost!

1758
01:33:52,708 --> 01:33:54,458
<i>You're the inside man.
And I'll handle it outside.</i>

1759
01:34:04,250 --> 01:34:06,083
I have an idea
that won't get us caught right away.

1760
01:34:06,916 --> 01:34:07,875
Say it!

1761
01:34:08,250 --> 01:34:11,833
Is it a bank, an ATM,
a casino, or a jewelry shop?

1762
01:34:11,958 --> 01:34:13,250
Where are we breaking in?

1763
01:34:13,333 --> 01:34:14,750
You mentioned what we would call a heist.

1764
01:34:15,083 --> 01:34:18,291
If we do it, we'll be caught in a day
and locked up in prison.

1765
01:34:19,375 --> 01:34:20,416
But we're not going to...

1766
01:34:22,041 --> 01:34:24,083
...pull of a heist but a scam!

1767
01:34:24,291 --> 01:34:25,458
Scam uh?

1768
01:34:26,041 --> 01:34:26,958
Good!

1769
01:34:31,500 --> 01:34:32,750
Madam has approved!

1770
01:34:33,625 --> 01:34:35,250
That means we're up for sacrifice.

1771
01:34:42,875 --> 01:34:44,125
This is Mangalapuram.

1772
01:34:45,958 --> 01:34:48,541
There used to be a toll booth
near this ring road.

1773
01:34:48,791 --> 01:34:51,916
Three years ago, a person filed a case

1774
01:34:52,166 --> 01:34:54,375
and temporarily shut down the toll gate.

1775
01:34:54,833 --> 01:34:59,291
The toll gate that was shut down
back then, we're going to reinstate it...

1776
01:34:59,625 --> 01:35:02,541
and swindle crores from the people.

1777
01:35:04,208 --> 01:35:07,000
Fake toll? That's a fantastic plan!

1778
01:35:07,458 --> 01:35:09,791
But it sounds like
a huge scam to pull off.

1779
01:35:11,666 --> 01:35:12,666
It's a small scam.

1780
01:35:23,875 --> 01:35:26,625
Sir, there's an unwritten rule
for every scam.

1781
01:35:27,083 --> 01:35:28,708
We cannot continue a scam for long.

1782
01:35:28,833 --> 01:35:30,666
If we continue to do it,
we'll get caught.

1783
01:35:32,000 --> 01:35:34,458
<i>In China, a man kidnapped
a billionaire gangster's son</i>

1784
01:35:34,541 --> 01:35:35,625
<i>and demanded two crores in ransom.</i>

1785
01:35:35,708 --> 01:35:37,708
<i>In a few days, two crores got spent.</i>

1786
01:35:37,791 --> 01:35:39,208
<i>Again, he carried out another kidnapping.</i>

1787
01:35:39,291 --> 01:35:41,291
<i>But this time, not the son
but the billionaire himself.</i>

1788
01:35:41,416 --> 01:35:42,333
<i>Do you know why?</i>

1789
01:35:42,416 --> 01:35:44,041
<i>To learn how to become rich.</i>

1790
01:35:44,125 --> 01:35:46,250
<i>And the billionaire
narrated a story with a smile.</i>

1791
01:35:46,333 --> 01:35:47,375
"Create your Own brand."

1792
01:35:47,458 --> 01:35:49,083
<i>If you see, the current CEOs</i>

1793
01:35:49,166 --> 01:35:52,625
<i>once launched a new product in the market
and became successful.</i>

1794
01:35:52,750 --> 01:35:55,416
Today, that gangster is the
top billionaire in that country.

1795
01:35:57,333 --> 01:36:00,250
Sir, the toll gate
will fetch us mere crores.

1796
01:36:00,916 --> 01:36:04,583
But as you demanded,
you need money until your last breath

1797
01:36:05,125 --> 01:36:06,625
For that,
I have an interesting idea, Sir.

1798
01:36:20,875 --> 01:36:22,708
{\an8}FUTURE OF ELECTRICITY
HYDRO GENERATOR SOLUTIONS

1799
01:36:23,958 --> 01:36:25,833
{\an8}Hi, Sir, this is Rohit.

1800
01:36:26,291 --> 01:36:28,333
{\an8}RIT Gold Medalist
in Electrical Engineering.

1801
01:36:28,416 --> 01:36:31,666
Electricity has become crucial
in people's lives.

1802
01:36:31,750 --> 01:36:34,083
What do people do
during a power shutdown?

1803
01:36:34,166 --> 01:36:35,166
They use a generator.

1804
01:36:35,250 --> 01:36:38,833
The petrol that runs the generator
is 70 rupees per liter.

1805
01:36:38,916 --> 01:36:42,291
However, water is enough
to use the Hydro-Generator.

1806
01:36:42,375 --> 01:36:44,291
If you see, this Hydro-Generator

1807
01:36:44,666 --> 01:36:46,125
will be the future electricity.

1808
01:36:47,041 --> 01:36:50,375
Once, if we launch
this Hydro-Generator in the market,

1809
01:36:50,458 --> 01:36:53,625
we could bring huge changes
to the Indian economy.

1810
01:36:54,041 --> 01:36:58,416
A part of the money we make from the toll,
we're going to invest in this project.

1811
01:36:58,916 --> 01:37:00,416
If you sign a contract with him

1812
01:37:00,958 --> 01:37:02,500
and transfer the patent under your name,

1813
01:37:02,750 --> 01:37:05,500
all the billionaires will come
looking for you to do business.

1814
01:37:16,583 --> 01:37:18,583
{\an8}"Old Korean Family," you say?

1815
01:37:18,666 --> 01:37:20,083
The idea sounds good.

1816
01:37:21,333 --> 01:37:22,583
Who is the Director?

1817
01:37:23,041 --> 01:37:23,916
It's him.

1818
01:37:24,583 --> 01:37:25,500
Oh!

1819
01:37:26,583 --> 01:37:28,833
- Who is the Hero?
- That's him too.

1820
01:37:30,750 --> 01:37:32,958
- Are you going to do both?
- Yes!

1821
01:37:34,416 --> 01:37:35,708
He writes lyrics too.

1822
01:37:40,833 --> 01:37:43,125
You see, in the future,

1823
01:37:43,750 --> 01:37:46,375
you mentioned you may sing as well.

1824
01:37:46,833 --> 01:37:47,708
So, I said it.

1825
01:37:53,291 --> 01:37:55,208
You'll don all the roles.

1826
01:37:55,333 --> 01:37:57,000
And won't give others an opportunity.

1827
01:37:58,541 --> 01:38:00,166
Fine, let's do it!

1828
01:38:47,250 --> 01:38:48,291
For the city to believe us,

1829
01:38:48,541 --> 01:38:50,291
we must publish the toll gate article
in the newspaper.

1830
01:38:50,583 --> 01:38:52,208
<i>I know a reporter who can help us.</i>

1831
01:38:59,583 --> 01:39:01,333
Drive! Let's follow him.

1832
01:39:02,208 --> 01:39:04,916
{\an8}Selvam, please deliver a pizza to home.

1833
01:39:09,208 --> 01:39:10,416
The Police are checking.

1834
01:39:10,833 --> 01:39:12,541
{\an8}I've already printed the receipt.

1835
01:39:12,833 --> 01:39:14,125
You pay the fine
and take your vehicle.

1836
01:39:18,125 --> 01:39:20,750
Where are you from?
And where are you headed?

1837
01:39:21,666 --> 01:39:22,541
Show me your license!

1838
01:39:25,958 --> 01:39:26,833
Sir, show me your license!

1839
01:39:29,625 --> 01:39:32,333
Twinkle, twinkle, little star.

1840
01:39:34,583 --> 01:39:36,708
Twinkle, twinkle, little star.

1841
01:39:37,333 --> 01:39:39,000
Twinkle, twinkle, little star.

1842
01:39:46,125 --> 01:39:49,041
Sir, think it's an Anglo Indian family.

1843
01:39:49,333 --> 01:39:50,958
Looks like it's a serious matter.
Shall I let them go?

1844
01:39:51,041 --> 01:39:52,166
Let them go!

1845
01:39:53,625 --> 01:39:54,583
You may leave!

1846
01:40:28,333 --> 01:40:30,583
Flat No.6, Arnaa. Is it pizza, right?

1847
01:40:30,666 --> 01:40:32,750
- Yes!
- Here, please keep the change.

1848
01:40:43,291 --> 01:40:44,791
Okay, the pizza is ready.

1849
01:40:58,083 --> 01:40:59,958
- Sir, pizza.
- I'll get your money.

1850
01:41:04,625 --> 01:41:05,500
Thank you.

1851
01:41:23,291 --> 01:41:24,166
Let's go in!

1852
01:41:29,000 --> 01:41:29,916
He passed out!

1853
01:41:35,791 --> 01:41:37,458
- Hello?
- Madam, there's an emergency.

1854
01:41:38,458 --> 01:41:39,541
It's food poisoning.

1855
01:41:39,916 --> 01:41:42,208
- Could you please send an ambulance?
- Okay, Sir, please give me the address.

1856
01:41:47,416 --> 01:41:49,333
This is the mock-up
of the article to publish.

1857
01:41:49,416 --> 01:41:50,625
TOLL IN MANGALAPURAM AGAIN?

1858
01:41:58,583 --> 01:41:59,458
There's a problem.

1859
01:41:59,541 --> 01:42:00,583
- Problem?
- Problem?

1860
01:42:00,666 --> 01:42:02,291
{\an8}- What happened?
- It's a server connection mail.

1861
01:42:02,375 --> 01:42:03,583
{\an8}It'll get delivered
only when he's in the office.

1862
01:42:04,125 --> 01:42:05,291
Let's drop the plan.

1863
01:42:06,041 --> 01:42:07,791
Let's not risk it.
Get out of there.

1864
01:42:08,041 --> 01:42:09,166
Get out of there. We'll leave!

1865
01:42:09,250 --> 01:42:10,166
What do we do now?

1866
01:42:10,375 --> 01:42:11,708
Let's not risk it.
Get out of there.

1867
01:42:12,041 --> 01:42:14,458
Mom, I'm discussing.
What do we do?

1868
01:42:15,541 --> 01:42:17,416
- Quickly, pack it up.
- Where are we going?

1869
01:42:21,375 --> 01:42:24,250
Hey, Saravana,
where are you going in Arnaa's car?

1870
01:42:24,333 --> 01:42:25,541
Mom, I'll explain it later.

1871
01:42:25,666 --> 01:42:27,166
Hey, Jacky, please listen closely.

1872
01:42:27,250 --> 01:42:28,833
Go upstairs and make sure
he doesn't wake up.

1873
01:42:29,000 --> 01:42:29,875
I can't do it. Get lost!

1874
01:42:29,958 --> 01:42:31,583
Hey, Jacky, please listen.
You must go!

1875
01:42:31,666 --> 01:42:33,375
Hey! I already told you.

1876
01:42:33,458 --> 01:42:34,833
That I won't go upstairs,
yet you're asking me to.

1877
01:42:34,916 --> 01:42:37,333
- I can't go!
- Hey, Jacky, please listen.

1878
01:42:37,416 --> 01:42:38,916
Damn you, man. I can't do it.

1879
01:42:39,000 --> 01:42:40,791
Brother, this is your sister speaking.

1880
01:42:41,375 --> 01:42:43,416
For God's sake, go upstairs.
Please don't refuse.

1881
01:42:43,500 --> 01:42:44,666
Bloody, cunning girl.

1882
01:42:44,958 --> 01:42:48,833
If I see you, I'll fry you, damn it!

1883
01:42:48,916 --> 01:42:50,875
Bloody, brother! Listen to
what he's saying and go upstairs.

1884
01:42:50,958 --> 01:42:51,916
Bloody?

1885
01:42:52,500 --> 01:42:53,625
Get lost, you crazy girl.
I can't do it.

1886
01:42:53,708 --> 01:42:55,541
Jacky, I'll handle it here.
You go upstairs!

1887
01:42:59,791 --> 01:43:01,416
Once again, you trapped me.

1888
01:43:02,250 --> 01:43:03,625
You never consider me as your child.

1889
01:43:04,500 --> 01:43:06,583
You keep sacrificing me
at every given chance.

1890
01:43:07,375 --> 01:43:09,291
<i>- Hey, stop talking and go upstairs.</i>
- Hey, hold on, I'm going.

1891
01:43:24,458 --> 01:43:27,125
Sir! Arnaa, Sir, ordered a pizza.

1892
01:43:27,208 --> 01:43:28,750
Arnaa, Sir, just went home.

1893
01:43:29,083 --> 01:43:29,958
Is it so?

1894
01:43:33,041 --> 01:43:34,625
Hello? Hello, Arnaa, Sir?

1895
01:43:35,208 --> 01:43:36,833
Can you hear me? Can you?

1896
01:43:38,791 --> 01:43:41,750
Sir, could you please call Arnaa, Sir?

1897
01:43:42,291 --> 01:43:44,625
I think the network is poor.
I'm not able to hear him.

1898
01:43:47,000 --> 01:43:48,000
Hello, Sir?

1899
01:43:48,125 --> 01:43:49,250
Come to the parking lot right away.

1900
01:43:49,333 --> 01:43:51,125
- Sir?
- Don't ask me anything.

1901
01:43:51,291 --> 01:43:52,666
- Come right away.
- I'm coming, sir.

1902
01:44:16,166 --> 01:44:18,083
- Hello?
- Sir, I'm at the parking lot.

1903
01:44:18,166 --> 01:44:20,583
Do you see the flat
and the black-colored gate?

1904
01:44:20,666 --> 01:44:23,958
- Flat? I'm at the office parking lot.
- Pizza delivery, right?

1905
01:44:24,041 --> 01:44:26,375
Sir, I'm Daily News Admin, Guna, speaking.

1906
01:44:26,458 --> 01:44:28,458
I thought you were the pizza delivery guy.
Sorry, Guna!

1907
01:44:28,541 --> 01:44:30,750
Pizza delivery is here at the office.

1908
01:44:30,875 --> 01:44:31,916
I'll send him to your house.

1909
01:44:39,375 --> 01:44:41,083
Sir, placed the order
at the wrong address.

1910
01:44:41,166 --> 01:44:42,291
He asked you to come home.

1911
01:44:44,333 --> 01:44:45,875
It's done.
The mail has been sent.

1912
01:44:45,958 --> 01:44:47,708
Super! Get here quickly.

1913
01:44:50,416 --> 01:44:52,000
Hey, Arnaa is gaining consciousness.

1914
01:44:52,083 --> 01:44:53,875
- Is he up?
- You handle it.

1915
01:44:53,958 --> 01:44:54,958
We'll be there in 10 minutes.

1916
01:44:55,041 --> 01:44:58,000
- What do I do?
- Hey, Jacky, please do something!

1917
01:44:58,083 --> 01:44:59,333
This is why I didn't want to come here.

1918
01:44:59,416 --> 01:45:01,958
Brother, please manage the situation.

1919
01:45:02,041 --> 01:45:05,208
When I see you next,
I'm going to thrash you royally.

1920
01:45:05,291 --> 01:45:07,833
Stop speaking nonsense
and do something to him.

1921
01:45:11,250 --> 01:45:12,125
Cork ball!

1922
01:45:17,875 --> 01:45:19,041
How did you manage it?

1923
01:45:20,458 --> 01:45:21,958
All of you planned against me...

1924
01:45:22,666 --> 01:45:24,125
and turned me into a murderer.

1925
01:45:25,375 --> 01:45:26,250
Super!

1926
01:45:52,958 --> 01:45:53,833
Oh, God!

1927
01:45:55,416 --> 01:45:56,791
Uncle, you're out!

1928
01:46:03,125 --> 01:46:05,833
I hope you won't tell anyone
about me getting out.

1929
01:46:05,916 --> 01:46:07,666
I won't tell anyone, Uncle.

1930
01:46:07,750 --> 01:46:09,041
Shall we play?

1931
01:46:09,166 --> 01:46:12,041
I have invited Dhoni.
He'll arrive in an hour.

1932
01:46:12,625 --> 01:46:14,291
We'll get together
on the terrace and play.

1933
01:46:14,375 --> 01:46:15,750
Is Dhoni coming to play as well?

1934
01:46:16,125 --> 01:46:17,416
Yay! Jolly!

1935
01:46:17,625 --> 01:46:19,958
Super! I'm going to the terrace.

1936
01:46:20,208 --> 01:46:21,166
Brat!

1937
01:46:28,875 --> 01:46:30,708
Hey, I think the ambulance has arrived.

1938
01:46:30,791 --> 01:46:32,416
I'm alone inside the flat.
What do I do now?

1939
01:46:32,500 --> 01:46:34,625
It'll take me 5 minutes to reach.
What do we do now?

1940
01:46:37,375 --> 01:46:39,583
Son, I'll handle it!

1941
01:46:48,833 --> 01:46:52,416
Mom, you have a stent in your heart,
and you're performing stunts.

1942
01:46:53,458 --> 01:46:54,375
What happened?

1943
01:46:55,916 --> 01:46:58,000
The vehicle shut down.
It's not starting.

1944
01:46:58,083 --> 01:46:59,833
We're heading to pick up
an emergency patient.

1945
01:47:00,000 --> 01:47:02,500
His house is at the corner.
Please move your vehicle.

1946
01:47:02,708 --> 01:47:04,416
I'm telling you
that I can't start the vehicle.

1947
01:47:04,583 --> 01:47:07,916
Reverse and take the entry
on the other side of the road.

1948
01:47:08,250 --> 01:47:09,333
Why would you torture us?

1949
01:47:45,416 --> 01:47:47,625
- Are you Arnaa from Flat No. 6?
- Yes!

1950
01:47:47,708 --> 01:47:49,458
You called for an ambulance
because you got food poisoning.

1951
01:48:11,458 --> 01:48:12,666
Check it out.
The toll news is out in the papers.

1952
01:48:13,458 --> 01:48:15,583
"A toll booth in Mangalapuram again?"

1953
01:48:16,166 --> 01:48:18,333
- She is not recognizable.
- Isn't she?

1954
01:48:18,791 --> 01:48:19,708
Perfect!

1955
01:48:19,791 --> 01:48:21,541
TOLL IN MANGALAPURAM AGAIN?

1956
01:48:22,291 --> 01:48:24,083
We need to perform
a major surgery immediately.

1957
01:48:24,291 --> 01:48:25,833
Your health condition is very bad.

1958
01:48:26,208 --> 01:48:27,500
This is a critical surgery.

1959
01:48:27,875 --> 01:48:28,833
It's impossible to perform.

1960
01:48:28,916 --> 01:48:30,708
But we have no choice
but to perform the surgery.

1961
01:48:31,791 --> 01:48:33,916
I'm sorry, sir.
I don't get you.

1962
01:48:35,291 --> 01:48:36,291
Can you do it...

1963
01:48:37,416 --> 01:48:38,333
or not?

1964
01:48:45,333 --> 01:48:47,875
They must've shut down
the power by mistake.

1965
01:48:47,958 --> 01:48:50,791
{\an8}By the time you get home,
the power will be back on.

1966
01:48:50,958 --> 01:48:53,708
Right away, go to this woman
Lakshmi's house

1967
01:48:53,791 --> 01:48:55,083
- and switch on the power.
- Okay, sir.

1968
01:48:55,166 --> 01:48:57,375
She has an infant
and is struggling without electricity.

1969
01:48:57,458 --> 01:49:00,333
Sir, there has been a mistake
in the billing. I'm sorry, sir.

1970
01:49:00,416 --> 01:49:02,958
It's common to make mistakes at work.

1971
01:49:03,125 --> 01:49:04,541
But you must rectify them.

1972
01:49:04,750 --> 01:49:06,416
You're saying the counter is closed?

1973
01:49:06,500 --> 01:49:09,166
Go ahead and pay it online.

1974
01:49:09,416 --> 01:49:12,166
Call us afterward,
and we'll reconnect your service.

1975
01:49:12,250 --> 01:49:13,375
I'm a retired CE.

1976
01:49:14,166 --> 01:49:15,458
What does it matter?

1977
01:49:15,541 --> 01:49:17,166
That doesn't mean I'll restore
the connection right away.

1978
01:49:17,250 --> 01:49:19,916
What kind of progress did you achieve
during your period?

1979
01:49:20,000 --> 01:49:22,666
Do you know that there are 16,000
connections under my section?

1980
01:49:22,875 --> 01:49:25,541
Ideally, there should be
150 to 200 staff members here.

1981
01:49:25,625 --> 01:49:27,833
But only eight employees
are working at this office.

1982
01:49:28,208 --> 01:49:30,666
Yet you're demanding
that one employee be sent to your house.

1983
01:49:30,750 --> 01:49:33,291
Do whatever you want.
I'll handle it.

1984
01:49:33,416 --> 01:49:38,000
The retired CE was arrogant
when he was in power.

1985
01:49:38,083 --> 01:49:41,333
Cut off his power for two days.

1986
01:49:41,416 --> 01:49:42,291
Okay, sir.

1987
01:49:42,583 --> 01:49:47,291
A toll plaza is being set up
in Mangalapuram once again.

1988
01:49:47,666 --> 01:49:50,083
Toll? Are they reopening it?

1989
01:49:57,875 --> 01:49:58,791
Saravana--

1990
01:49:58,875 --> 01:50:00,083
Hey, Saravana! Is that you?

1991
01:50:01,083 --> 01:50:02,291
Hey, keep your voice down.

1992
01:50:02,375 --> 01:50:04,875
I really thought an old man
was sitting opposite me.

1993
01:50:05,000 --> 01:50:05,875
Forget about it.

1994
01:50:06,208 --> 01:50:07,583
How are you? What are you up to?

1995
01:50:08,125 --> 01:50:09,250
I'm just existing, dude.

1996
01:50:10,208 --> 01:50:14,041
Dude, after you left, I invested
in the business and kept it going.

1997
01:50:14,583 --> 01:50:16,458
It seemed like I was making money.

1998
01:50:16,541 --> 01:50:17,750
Later, I lost it all.

1999
01:50:19,125 --> 01:50:21,750
In life, we may win
through shortcuts quickly.

2000
01:50:22,000 --> 01:50:23,833
But it does not last.

2001
01:50:25,250 --> 01:50:28,375
It lasts only
if you're honest and hard-working.

2002
01:50:28,708 --> 01:50:30,166
It's something I learned the hard way.

2003
01:50:30,666 --> 01:50:32,958
In life, we have made many mistakes
without thinking twice.

2004
01:50:34,250 --> 01:50:36,458
Forget about it.
Do you know something?

2005
01:50:36,583 --> 01:50:39,458
Aishu and her family left town
after the mess you created.

2006
01:50:39,583 --> 01:50:40,833
They settled down in the USA.

2007
01:50:40,958 --> 01:50:41,916
Are you aware of it?

2008
01:50:42,166 --> 01:50:43,083
I heard about it.

2009
01:50:44,416 --> 01:50:45,500
We'll fix everything.

2010
01:50:46,625 --> 01:50:47,500
Okay, Satha!

2011
01:50:48,458 --> 01:50:50,083
I'm going to commit another big scam.

2012
01:50:51,291 --> 01:50:52,500
I need your help.

2013
01:50:52,583 --> 01:50:54,083
What? Once again, you want my help?

2014
01:50:54,166 --> 01:50:55,041
- Hey!
- Calm down.

2015
01:50:55,125 --> 01:50:57,333
I'm still recovering
from the previous scam.

2016
01:50:57,458 --> 01:50:58,416
Do you know something?

2017
01:50:58,500 --> 01:51:03,208
Even the kids in my area have
started mocking me, "Quick, Satha."

2018
01:51:03,416 --> 01:51:05,458
I have reformed
and am trying to live an honest life.

2019
01:51:05,541 --> 01:51:07,875
- Spare me! I'm leaving.
- Satha!

2020
01:51:08,625 --> 01:51:09,500
Hey!

2021
01:51:14,583 --> 01:51:16,000
Two teas.
Put it under my tab.

2022
01:51:16,083 --> 01:51:17,083
No more credit.

2023
01:51:17,791 --> 01:51:19,916
- Oh, is it?
- Of course!

2024
01:51:20,250 --> 01:51:22,500
- Hey, Satha, please.
- Dude, I can't do it.

2025
01:51:22,583 --> 01:51:24,583
- Is this how you see us?
- Sir?

2026
01:51:25,583 --> 01:51:26,833
Please don't keep him company.

2027
01:51:27,500 --> 01:51:30,916
He'll lure you
to invest in Quick Money and stuff.

2028
01:51:31,000 --> 01:51:31,958
Don't trust him!

2029
01:51:33,041 --> 01:51:35,625
He's one of the reasons
many have left this town.

2030
01:51:36,083 --> 01:51:36,958
Did you hear him?

2031
01:51:37,833 --> 01:51:39,875
- Hey, Sakthi, come here.
- Yes, brother?

2032
01:51:41,625 --> 01:51:45,250
Here, there are 12 EB cards
and money to pay the bill.

2033
01:51:45,333 --> 01:51:47,916
Pay the bill at the EB office.

2034
01:51:48,000 --> 01:51:49,916
And demand a printed bill.

2035
01:51:50,000 --> 01:51:51,250
If they say the printer is not working

2036
01:51:51,625 --> 01:51:55,333
and if you bring me
a paper that says "paid."

2037
01:51:55,958 --> 01:51:58,333
- I'll tear you like paper.
- I understood.

2038
01:51:58,541 --> 01:52:00,083
You keep repeating this every month.

2039
01:52:00,166 --> 01:52:01,208
I know how to pay the bill.

2040
01:52:01,291 --> 01:52:03,916
Not just every month.
I'll tell you every day.

2041
01:52:04,083 --> 01:52:05,541
Only the victim knows how hard it hit.

2042
01:52:05,625 --> 01:52:06,583
Go!

2043
01:52:07,625 --> 01:52:09,208
It all started here.

2044
01:52:09,958 --> 01:52:10,875
You're right!

2045
01:52:15,791 --> 01:52:16,916
The town is convinced now.

2046
01:52:17,708 --> 01:52:19,583
Next, we must convince the MLA.

2047
01:52:25,541 --> 01:52:26,500
Why are you staring at me?

2048
01:52:27,166 --> 01:52:28,333
It's not like I am MLA's wife.

2049
01:52:29,166 --> 01:52:30,666
I can't come with you.

2050
01:52:31,000 --> 01:52:32,000
Not a chance!

2051
01:52:32,416 --> 01:52:36,458
Jacky, one day when you were
down with a cold and fever...

2052
01:52:36,958 --> 01:52:40,041
didn't I nurse you back to health?

2053
01:52:45,666 --> 01:52:47,583
If something were to happen to me,

2054
01:52:47,958 --> 01:52:51,333
the people who are the reason for it
are none but

2055
01:52:51,916 --> 01:52:53,208
my biological mother!

2056
01:52:53,750 --> 01:52:55,000
I hope everyone heard it.

2057
01:53:01,208 --> 01:53:03,000
- What's your name?
- Gangadharan, Sir.

2058
01:53:03,208 --> 01:53:04,625
You look like a senior citizen.

2059
01:53:04,833 --> 01:53:06,541
I was afraid you'd mess up my hair.

2060
01:53:06,625 --> 01:53:08,291
But you're quite an artist.

2061
01:53:08,708 --> 01:53:11,541
You inform the others
that I no longer want them.

2062
01:53:11,666 --> 01:53:13,958
From now on,
only you should do my hair.

2063
01:53:14,083 --> 01:53:16,250
Sir, our company has introduced
a new product.

2064
01:53:16,333 --> 01:53:18,500
It's an eye mask. It's enough
if you wear it for 5 minutes.

2065
01:53:18,625 --> 01:53:19,708
You'd feel refreshed all day.

2066
01:53:19,791 --> 01:53:20,708
- Is it?
- Yes, Sir.

2067
01:53:20,875 --> 01:53:21,750
Do it!

2068
01:53:22,125 --> 01:53:23,583
Give me 2 minutes. I'll be back.

2069
01:53:23,666 --> 01:53:24,583
Thank you.

2070
01:53:26,125 --> 01:53:27,333
I'm going to put an eye mask on him.

2071
01:53:27,458 --> 01:53:30,125
Inform MLA Senthil that
he'll be getting a call from the Minister.

2072
01:53:31,083 --> 01:53:33,166
- Hey, the cheapo MLA is coming.
- Please, welcome.

2073
01:53:33,708 --> 01:53:34,625
Have some tea.

2074
01:53:34,875 --> 01:53:37,083
Seems like you convinced the CM.

2075
01:53:37,166 --> 01:53:38,958
Deputy CM is known to us.

2076
01:53:39,333 --> 01:53:40,875
And we used it to our advantage.

2077
01:53:41,416 --> 01:53:46,458
Rapta's CEO, Kamala Keerthivasan,
is currently on a video call.

2078
01:53:46,625 --> 01:53:48,250
She wants to talk to you for 2 minutes.

2079
01:53:48,625 --> 01:53:49,500
Madam, he's here.

2080
01:53:52,125 --> 01:53:54,916
Vardharajan, Sir! Okay, Sir.

2081
01:53:56,458 --> 01:53:59,125
If you come to Delhi,
you must visit our house.

2082
01:53:59,791 --> 01:54:01,708
Please don't forget. Okay, okay.

2083
01:54:04,291 --> 01:54:05,708
Hi, Senthil Ji.

2084
01:54:05,791 --> 01:54:07,208
- Vanakkam.
- One second.

2085
01:54:07,541 --> 01:54:08,666
- Excuse me.
- Yes, Ma'am.

2086
01:54:08,750 --> 01:54:09,625
Water, please.

2087
01:54:09,916 --> 01:54:10,833
Thank you.

2088
01:54:15,375 --> 01:54:19,291
Senthil Ji, I spoke with Minister
Vardharajan regarding the toll booth.

2089
01:54:19,375 --> 01:54:21,416
He'll be calling you right now.

2090
01:54:22,291 --> 01:54:23,416
Sir, please set your phone aside.

2091
01:54:24,625 --> 01:54:27,541
You can't use your phone
while wearing the eye mask.

2092
01:54:27,625 --> 01:54:30,250
Oh, I can't use the phone, right?
One minute.

2093
01:54:31,500 --> 01:54:34,166
But I could play a song for 5 minutes.

2094
01:55:00,291 --> 01:55:02,333
The plan is messed up.
The Minister played a song on his phone.

2095
01:55:02,416 --> 01:55:03,291
It's over!

2096
01:55:03,916 --> 01:55:05,125
- What are you saying?
- It's over!

2097
01:55:05,250 --> 01:55:06,958
- Plan drop! Plan drop!
- What do we do now?

2098
01:55:07,041 --> 01:55:08,125
We can't do anything.

2099
01:55:08,375 --> 01:55:10,458
Don't panic.
We'll find a way out.

2100
01:55:10,541 --> 01:55:11,541
Let's not risk it and leave.

2101
01:55:11,666 --> 01:55:12,666
That's safe for us.

2102
01:55:13,666 --> 01:55:14,666
I didn't get a call yet.

2103
01:55:26,000 --> 01:55:28,541
Hey, I think the video is freezing.

2104
01:55:28,625 --> 01:55:29,708
- It's not working.
- Oh, no!

2105
01:55:29,875 --> 01:55:31,958
It's nothing, Sir.
It must be a patchy network.

2106
01:55:32,041 --> 01:55:33,708
- That's it. Nothing else.
- Oh, sorry.

2107
01:55:48,250 --> 01:55:50,625
She's trying to say something.
But I cannot hear her.

2108
01:55:50,708 --> 01:55:52,541
Sir, give me 2 minutes.

2109
01:55:52,750 --> 01:55:53,916
Tell me what phone he is using.

2110
01:55:59,000 --> 01:56:01,708
- iPhone 6S.
- iPhone... 6S.

2111
01:56:03,500 --> 01:56:06,791
Wait a minute.
You can't dial when a song is on.

2112
01:56:06,875 --> 01:56:08,500
But there's an option to receive the call.

2113
01:56:08,583 --> 01:56:09,583
We can forward the call.

2114
01:56:10,291 --> 01:56:12,916
Saravana, even if a song is playing
on iPhone 6S,

2115
01:56:13,000 --> 01:56:14,666
you can use another app
in the background.

2116
01:56:14,791 --> 01:56:17,250
Go to settings, put your number,
and forward the call.

2117
01:56:17,833 --> 01:56:18,833
Call forwarding activated.

2118
01:56:18,916 --> 01:56:21,541
Somehow, make MLA Senthil
call the Minister.

2119
01:56:23,250 --> 01:56:25,875
- Do you hear me?
- Tell me, Madam.

2120
01:56:25,958 --> 01:56:27,875
{\an8}Sir, Madam, is back online.

2121
01:56:27,958 --> 01:56:31,458
Senthil Ji, Minister Vardharajan
has been trying to reach you for a while.

2122
01:56:31,666 --> 01:56:33,416
{\an8}Immediately, please call him.

2123
01:56:43,000 --> 01:56:44,083
Vannakam, Sir.

2124
01:56:46,041 --> 01:56:48,208
What's happening?
Why am I not able to reach you?

2125
01:56:48,416 --> 01:56:51,375
Sir, I think there's an issue
with the network.

2126
01:56:51,583 --> 01:56:55,625
Listen, she is the CEO of Rapta Group.

2127
01:56:55,708 --> 01:56:57,875
{\an8}Kamala Keerthivasan. She's a big shot.

2128
01:56:58,333 --> 01:56:59,250
Also, she's related to influential people.

2129
01:56:59,333 --> 01:57:01,833
Sort out the toll matter for her.

2130
01:57:01,916 --> 01:57:04,083
Sure, Sir.
Now that you've said I'll sort it out.

2131
01:57:04,166 --> 01:57:06,125
If possible,
you inaugurate the toll as well.

2132
01:57:07,000 --> 01:57:08,875
The CM has personally asked
that you be considered for the job.

2133
01:57:08,958 --> 01:57:11,416
{\an8}Sure, Sir. I'll sort it out.

2134
01:57:13,166 --> 01:57:15,250
{\an8}He spoke to me. Don't worry.
I'll take care, Ma'am.

2135
01:57:15,333 --> 01:57:16,750
Super, Senthil Ji.

2136
01:57:17,000 --> 01:57:18,291
If you're in Delhi, please visit our home.

2137
01:57:18,375 --> 01:57:19,875
{\an8}- Please don't forget.
- I will surely visit.

2138
01:57:19,958 --> 01:57:21,666
{\an8}- Okay.
- Sure, I'll come.

2139
01:57:21,750 --> 01:57:22,625
Bye!

2140
01:57:24,375 --> 01:57:25,583
Phew!

2141
01:57:27,166 --> 01:57:29,625
If you encounter any problems
regarding the toll, reach out to me.

2142
01:57:29,708 --> 01:57:30,833
- He has spoken.
- Sir!

2143
01:57:31,916 --> 01:57:34,291
Sir, she invited you to Delhi.

2144
01:57:34,875 --> 01:57:36,500
Generally, she does not invite everyone.

2145
01:57:37,000 --> 01:57:39,916
You're eligible
to become a Central Minister.

2146
01:57:40,125 --> 01:57:41,041
I understand.

2147
01:57:41,125 --> 01:57:43,583
Bloody moron,
how did you even become an MLA?

2148
01:57:43,666 --> 01:57:45,750
- People of Tamil Nadu are--
- Did you say something?

2149
01:57:45,833 --> 01:57:46,958
I was praying!

2150
01:57:47,041 --> 01:57:48,291
I was praying, Sir.

2151
01:57:48,375 --> 01:57:50,541
- Oh, you were praying. Okay.
- Yes!

2152
01:57:51,083 --> 01:57:52,000
- Vanakkam!
- Okay, sir.

2153
01:58:18,916 --> 01:58:21,333
Hey, this was fantastic.

2154
01:58:21,625 --> 01:58:22,583
You look refreshed, Sir.

2155
01:58:22,916 --> 01:58:24,666
- What's next? Okay.
- Let me clean up, Sir.

2156
01:58:25,625 --> 01:58:30,958
<i>I'm going to rip you both apart,
shredding you.</i>

2157
01:58:31,875 --> 01:58:32,875
<i>Son, don't do it!</i>

2158
01:58:33,625 --> 01:58:34,541
Jacky!

2159
01:58:34,750 --> 01:58:41,708
<i>Any child is a good child at birth.</i>

2160
01:58:42,583 --> 01:58:49,333
<i>Whether the child turns out good or evil
depends on how the mother raises them.</i>

2161
01:58:49,416 --> 01:58:50,750
<i>- Hey!
- Please don't do it.</i>

2162
01:58:50,833 --> 01:58:52,625
<i>Please spare me, Son.</i>

2163
01:58:54,458 --> 01:58:55,375
<i>Latest news!</i>

2164
01:58:55,458 --> 01:59:00,000
<i>The new movie "Old Korean Boy,"
directed by Kumar, is releasing on Pongal.</i>

2165
01:59:00,416 --> 01:59:02,041
<i>Vanakkam, my name is Kumar.</i>

2166
01:59:02,291 --> 01:59:06,500
{\an8}<i>I'm the director of Old Korean Boy,
and it's my dream project.</i>

2167
01:59:06,833 --> 01:59:09,166
{\an8}<i>I got Hero Sir's dates at the right time.</i>

2168
01:59:11,125 --> 01:59:12,000
<i>I'm very happy.</i>

2169
01:59:12,083 --> 01:59:14,166
<i>- It has come out well.</i>
- Jacky, eat before it gets cold.

2170
01:59:14,250 --> 01:59:15,458
- Please eat.
<i>- I need the audience's support.</i>

2171
01:59:15,916 --> 01:59:16,791
I'm talking to you--

2172
01:59:22,791 --> 01:59:23,791
Hey, why did you?

2173
01:59:25,041 --> 01:59:26,125
What happened?

2174
01:59:30,375 --> 01:59:31,958
<i>I wrote this script with you in mind.</i>

2175
01:59:32,041 --> 01:59:33,833
<i>I can't easily replace you.</i>

2176
01:59:33,916 --> 01:59:35,833
<i>No matter how many years it takes,
I'll wait for you.</i>

2177
02:00:05,916 --> 02:00:07,250
Sorry, Jacky.

2178
02:00:09,833 --> 02:00:10,708
It's all...

2179
02:00:12,375 --> 02:00:13,458
...my fault!

2180
02:00:18,416 --> 02:00:23,666
As a mother, I should've stopped you
from making these mistakes.

2181
02:00:25,541 --> 02:00:26,833
But you did warn me.

2182
02:00:28,708 --> 02:00:29,958
And I didn't listen to you.

2183
02:00:33,833 --> 02:00:35,375
I can't believe...

2184
02:00:38,000 --> 02:00:39,333
I destroyed my son's life.

2185
02:00:42,125 --> 02:00:43,583
Only now do I realize it.

2186
02:00:44,375 --> 02:00:45,541
When I think about it...

2187
02:00:47,250 --> 02:00:48,833
my heart feels heavy.

2188
02:00:53,333 --> 02:00:54,250
My son...

2189
02:00:55,666 --> 02:00:57,083
I made a mistake.

2190
02:00:57,416 --> 02:00:59,125
I made a grave mistake.

2191
02:01:01,541 --> 02:01:06,416
I destroyed my son's life.

2192
02:01:08,875 --> 02:01:10,250
I'm not a good mother.

2193
02:01:15,208 --> 02:01:16,166
Is there dosa flour left?

2194
02:01:18,583 --> 02:01:20,625
I'm hungry.
Please make me a dosa.

2195
02:01:30,333 --> 02:01:31,500
It's okay, Mom, we'll overcome this.

2196
02:01:44,500 --> 02:01:45,500
I get it.

2197
02:01:45,833 --> 02:01:47,291
How are you going to
handle the Police station?

2198
02:01:47,708 --> 02:01:49,791
A slight suspicion is enough
for them to lock us up.

2199
02:01:52,875 --> 02:01:55,291
Hey, why are you people always fighting?

2200
02:01:55,416 --> 02:01:58,083
Sir, it's my own house.

2201
02:01:58,166 --> 02:02:00,041
He's beating me
whenever I go near the house.

2202
02:02:01,208 --> 02:02:03,041
Sir, there's an ongoing case in court.

2203
02:02:03,125 --> 02:02:05,125
If he comes near the house
before the verdict, I will beat him.

2204
02:02:05,208 --> 02:02:06,583
Sir, you're well aware of the situation.

2205
02:02:06,666 --> 02:02:09,000
If it's been past 10 years,
that house will belong to him.

2206
02:02:09,250 --> 02:02:10,833
How do you expect me to sit idle?

2207
02:02:10,916 --> 02:02:12,708
Sir, I'm the victim here.

2208
02:02:12,791 --> 02:02:15,375
Not just him, even his father
comes near the house, I'll beat him.

2209
02:02:15,458 --> 02:02:17,083
Hey, what nonsense is this?

2210
02:02:17,166 --> 02:02:18,666
Look, he's being violent
right in front of you.

2211
02:02:18,750 --> 02:02:20,958
Sir, then ask him to pay me
the 5 lakhs he took from me.

2212
02:02:21,041 --> 02:02:22,291
Hey, it's your own house, right?

2213
02:02:22,375 --> 02:02:24,166
Why don't you pay him 5 lakhs and end it?

2214
02:02:24,250 --> 02:02:26,791
Why would I pay him the money
I never took from him?

2215
02:02:26,875 --> 02:02:28,166
I will proceed legally.

2216
02:02:28,250 --> 02:02:29,916
Until then, the house is mine.

2217
02:02:35,208 --> 02:02:36,666
Sir, my name is Meikannan.

2218
02:02:37,000 --> 02:02:39,041
- Okay.
- I'm a senior citizen.

2219
02:02:40,583 --> 02:02:42,833
I'm here to file a complaint.

2220
02:02:43,250 --> 02:02:46,041
Would it be possible to meet
the inspector at this station?

2221
02:02:46,125 --> 02:02:48,791
Oh, you'd only meet the inspector, is it?

2222
02:02:49,041 --> 02:02:50,166
Why wouldn't you file a complaint with me?

2223
02:02:50,250 --> 02:02:51,791
Oh, no, you misunderstood, Sir.

2224
02:02:52,958 --> 02:02:56,916
In Mangalapuram,
a major scam is about to be carried out.

2225
02:02:57,500 --> 02:02:59,208
They're going to swindle crores.

2226
02:02:59,750 --> 02:03:03,416
So, I wanted to meet the inspector
and file a complaint.

2227
02:03:04,208 --> 02:03:05,208
Please wait!

2228
02:03:08,166 --> 02:03:10,125
{\an8}- What scam?
- One minute.

2229
02:03:12,500 --> 02:03:13,375
{\an8}Take a look at this.

2230
02:03:14,333 --> 02:03:18,083
There's news about reopening the
toll booth on the Mangalapuram ring road.

2231
02:03:19,250 --> 02:03:20,166
As per the rules,

2232
02:03:20,625 --> 02:03:23,625
{\an8}there shouldn't be a toll within
a 60-kilometer radius of Chennai city.

2233
02:03:23,791 --> 02:03:26,958
{\an8}But the Rapta group has acquired
permission to reopen the toll.

2234
02:03:27,875 --> 02:03:28,875
Through this toll...

2235
02:03:29,208 --> 02:03:32,500
they're going to swindle crores
from the people.

2236
02:03:34,416 --> 02:03:35,291
So,

2237
02:03:36,041 --> 02:03:37,791
I want to file a complaint against them.

2238
02:03:38,000 --> 02:03:38,875
Oh, oh!

2239
02:03:38,958 --> 02:03:40,750
{\an8}Complaint against the Rapta group?

2240
02:03:41,166 --> 02:03:43,291
{\an8}I won't be surprised if you
file a complaint against everyone.

2241
02:03:44,833 --> 02:03:45,750
{\an8}Hey, fool!

2242
02:03:46,291 --> 02:03:48,083
{\an8}Toll doesn't come under State control.

2243
02:03:48,833 --> 02:03:51,625
{\an8}I reckon he's here
to file a controversial complaint.

2244
02:03:59,416 --> 02:04:01,416
I want to file a complaint
against the Minister.

2245
02:04:04,375 --> 02:04:05,375
{\an8}What's he saying?

2246
02:04:06,166 --> 02:04:07,125
{\an8}Minister?

2247
02:04:18,375 --> 02:04:19,583
Sir, I'm not sure who he is.

2248
02:04:19,666 --> 02:04:21,500
There's someone here
to file a complaint against the toll.

2249
02:04:21,583 --> 02:04:24,125
Fine, pretend to file a CSR
and send him away.

2250
02:04:24,291 --> 02:04:27,041
More will follow to file a complaint.
Please handle it.

2251
02:04:27,125 --> 02:04:30,041
Constable, if anyone files
a complaint against toll, don't file it.

2252
02:04:30,125 --> 02:04:31,083
- Okay?
- Okay, Sir.

2253
02:04:50,875 --> 02:04:56,208
Sir, Rapta Company CEO,
Kamala Keerthivasan is on a video call.

2254
02:04:57,083 --> 02:04:58,375
Please talk to her.

2255
02:04:58,916 --> 02:05:00,333
{\an8}- Sure!
- Hi, Sir.

2256
02:05:00,916 --> 02:05:02,958
{\an8}This is Kamala Keerthivasan here.

2257
02:05:03,166 --> 02:05:06,083
{\an8}- How are you, Sir?
- Hi, Ma'am, I'm doing well.

2258
02:05:06,208 --> 02:05:09,000
I'm at Mount Everest
for an official meeting.

2259
02:05:09,208 --> 02:05:10,333
Oh, is it?

2260
02:05:10,750 --> 02:05:12,125
Mount Everest?

2261
02:05:12,416 --> 02:05:13,916
You gasp for breath
just by climbing stairs.

2262
02:05:14,250 --> 02:05:16,000
She's lying scaling than Everest.

2263
02:05:16,166 --> 02:05:20,500
{\an8}Sir, did MLA Senthil call you
regarding the toll booth?

2264
02:05:20,750 --> 02:05:22,833
{\an8}It's regarding the toll, right?
I'll sort it out.

2265
02:05:22,958 --> 02:05:26,000
{\an8}Okay, Sir. Thank you.
Thank you so much, Sir.

2266
02:05:26,083 --> 02:05:28,625
{\an8}- Thank you.
- Please visit us when you're in Delhi.

2267
02:05:28,875 --> 02:05:30,125
{\an8}- Don't forget.
- Okay.

2268
02:05:30,208 --> 02:05:31,791
- I'll visit for sure.
- Madam!

2269
02:05:31,875 --> 02:05:33,166
Hey, you never stepped out
of this district.

2270
02:05:33,250 --> 02:05:34,333
Don't get us caught by blabbering.
Hang up!

2271
02:05:36,458 --> 02:05:37,750
She thanked you, Sir.

2272
02:05:40,875 --> 02:05:42,625
Hey, here you go.

2273
02:05:50,958 --> 02:05:52,458
Uncle, I can't reach it.

2274
02:05:52,541 --> 02:05:53,958
Please help me pick up the food.

2275
02:05:54,041 --> 02:05:55,833
You need help?
Fine, I'm coming.

2276
02:06:00,208 --> 02:06:01,083
Take it.

2277
02:06:06,083 --> 02:06:06,958
Hold it!

2278
02:06:07,333 --> 02:06:09,416
You're good at catching things.
Now catch!

2279
02:06:09,958 --> 02:06:11,375
It's down here. Catch it.

2280
02:06:12,416 --> 02:06:13,291
Catch it!

2281
02:06:14,166 --> 02:06:15,375
Hey, you caught it!

2282
02:06:16,291 --> 02:06:17,833
Fine, take it.

2283
02:06:19,083 --> 02:06:20,708
It's for you to take it.

2284
02:06:20,916 --> 02:06:22,291
Uncle, please let it go.

2285
02:06:26,458 --> 02:06:27,333
Eat!

2286
02:06:36,791 --> 02:06:39,541
I served dinner at the dining table.
Please have it.

2287
02:06:42,833 --> 02:06:44,333
Do you really love Jeeva?

2288
02:06:46,833 --> 02:06:49,041
Are you truly trying to save Jeeva?

2289
02:06:58,625 --> 02:07:00,166
I reckon you'd never trust me.

2290
02:07:04,208 --> 02:07:05,125
That's not what I meant.

2291
02:07:06,666 --> 02:07:07,708
You're well aware...

2292
02:07:08,750 --> 02:07:11,500
that I grew up in an orphanage
since my childhood.

2293
02:07:12,666 --> 02:07:16,875
I wanted the usual life
where I fall in love, get married,

2294
02:07:17,458 --> 02:07:20,833
have a child,
and live happily with my family.

2295
02:07:21,375 --> 02:07:22,916
This is a simple wish.

2296
02:07:24,041 --> 02:07:24,958
However,

2297
02:07:26,041 --> 02:07:27,791
I made a big mistake in my life.

2298
02:07:29,833 --> 02:07:32,041
I trusted the wrong person
and got married to him.

2299
02:07:34,000 --> 02:07:37,208
After that, I couldn't trust anyone.

2300
02:07:39,708 --> 02:07:40,916
Please don't take me the wrong way.

2301
02:07:42,625 --> 02:07:44,416
I don't know
what your impression of me is.

2302
02:07:47,041 --> 02:07:50,208
I truly see Jeeva as my own son.

2303
02:07:53,041 --> 02:07:57,875
When I said I'm Jeeva's father,
I wasn't saying it for the sake of it.

2304
02:08:00,250 --> 02:08:01,208
I meant every word of it.

2305
02:08:24,000 --> 02:08:26,375
<i>- Ching Ch Ching
- Make it explode!</i>

2306
02:08:26,458 --> 02:08:28,750
{\an8}<i>-Ching Ch Ching
- Strike fear!</i>

2307
02:08:28,833 --> 02:08:31,166
{\an8}<i>-Ching Ch Ching
- Run them out!</i>

2308
02:08:31,250 --> 02:08:33,708
{\an8}<i>-Ching Ch Ching
- Intimidate them!</i>

2309
02:08:33,916 --> 02:08:35,625
- 80 rupees.
- I'm a local.

2310
02:08:35,708 --> 02:08:36,708
I'm the worst local.

2311
02:08:36,791 --> 02:08:38,458
I'll chew and spit blade on your face.

2312
02:08:38,541 --> 02:08:40,000
To hell with local. Get lost.

2313
02:08:40,166 --> 02:08:41,583
VIP? Show me your face.

2314
02:08:42,083 --> 02:08:44,041
The camera is being monitored
by the Central Government.

2315
02:08:44,125 --> 02:08:45,916
It's election season.
Shall I upload it to TikTok?

2316
02:08:46,000 --> 02:08:48,250
- I'm from Press, Sir.
- So? Take out your purse.

2317
02:08:48,416 --> 02:08:50,208
The printer is not working.
I'll give you a written receipt.

2318
02:08:51,041 --> 02:08:53,875
Day 1 collection: 13,13,000 rupees.

2319
02:08:53,958 --> 02:08:55,000
Sir, I'm a lawyer.

2320
02:08:55,250 --> 02:08:56,791
I'm asking for the toll fee, not yours.

2321
02:08:56,875 --> 02:08:59,000
- I'm a Doctor.
- That doesn't mean I can let you slide.

2322
02:08:59,083 --> 02:09:00,458
You guys charge exorbitant fees.

2323
02:09:00,541 --> 02:09:02,041
Day 10: 22,00,000 rupees.

2324
02:09:02,125 --> 02:09:03,625
90 rupees sounds too expensive, Sir.

2325
02:09:03,833 --> 02:09:07,083
If 90 rupees seems expensive,
you don't deserve to drive a car.

2326
02:09:07,166 --> 02:09:08,041
He's a Hero, sir.

2327
02:09:08,125 --> 02:09:10,041
The one word I don't like in Tamil
is Hero.

2328
02:09:10,125 --> 02:09:11,166
But I like the comedian.

2329
02:09:11,291 --> 02:09:14,333
Saravana, I was hoping to become a
Hero and enjoy the box office collection.

2330
02:09:14,458 --> 02:09:16,333
But you made me sit in a box
and collect money.

2331
02:09:16,416 --> 02:09:17,291
The printer is not working.

2332
02:09:17,375 --> 02:09:18,875
The printer is not working.
Here's your receipt.

2333
02:09:18,958 --> 02:09:19,833
Toll collection!

2334
02:09:20,000 --> 02:09:20,875
Ready!

2335
02:09:29,166 --> 02:09:30,500
Welcome to the press and media.

2336
02:09:31,458 --> 02:09:35,375
I'm Kalyana Sundaram.
Retired Inspector of Police, Mangalapuram.

2337
02:09:35,458 --> 02:09:37,000
After five years of research,

2338
02:09:37,125 --> 02:09:38,625
I'm very happy to announce

2339
02:09:38,791 --> 02:09:40,583
we have succeeded in creating a

2340
02:09:40,833 --> 02:09:43,250
future electricity generation option.

2341
02:09:43,375 --> 02:09:45,791
It's called Hydro-Generator.

2342
02:09:45,875 --> 02:09:47,791
- Hey, it's Pulp-cane!
- Hey, it's Kalyana Sundaram.

2343
02:09:48,666 --> 02:09:50,666
If you're asking
what's special about our generator,

2344
02:09:50,750 --> 02:09:54,250
in a normal generator,
you must fuel it with petrol or diesel.

2345
02:09:54,333 --> 02:09:57,208
But in our generator,
we don't need that fuel.

2346
02:09:57,291 --> 02:09:59,333
Water is enough to power it.

2347
02:10:01,875 --> 02:10:02,750
Thanks.

2348
02:10:03,041 --> 02:10:04,000
Thank you.

2349
02:10:06,250 --> 02:10:07,833
{\an8}How much are you going to invest in it?

2350
02:10:08,500 --> 02:10:09,541
Okay, I'll think about it.

2351
02:10:11,208 --> 02:10:12,083
20 crores.

2352
02:10:12,166 --> 02:10:14,166
Hello, 30 crores, you say?

2353
02:10:14,250 --> 02:10:15,416
40 crores!

2354
02:10:15,500 --> 02:10:16,916
Is 50 crores your offer?

2355
02:10:23,750 --> 02:10:24,958
Welcome, Saravana!

2356
02:10:25,041 --> 02:10:27,500
As you said,
I received a lot of calls.

2357
02:10:27,583 --> 02:10:29,291
I finished the final deal
with a Delhi client.

2358
02:10:29,416 --> 02:10:30,541
50 crores!

2359
02:10:30,666 --> 02:10:32,333
He's going to pay me
an advance of 1 crore.

2360
02:10:32,791 --> 02:10:33,750
Fantastic, Sir.

2361
02:10:34,375 --> 02:10:37,166
Sir, we collected around 10 crores
through the toll booth.

2362
02:10:39,083 --> 02:10:40,541
Sir, we did whatever you asked of us.

2363
02:10:41,833 --> 02:10:43,333
If you release Jeeva...

2364
02:10:44,250 --> 02:10:45,541
we'll go away somewhere far.

2365
02:10:54,916 --> 02:10:58,833
First of all, I never said
I'd let you guys off the hook.

2366
02:11:01,250 --> 02:11:02,666
Sir, first, you agreed to let us go.

2367
02:11:03,000 --> 02:11:03,958
Now you're going back on your word.

2368
02:11:04,041 --> 02:11:05,500
I was going to let you leave.

2369
02:11:05,583 --> 02:11:09,625
What if someday you guys return
and con me again?

2370
02:11:09,708 --> 02:11:10,958
We won't do anything stupid like that.

2371
02:11:11,041 --> 02:11:12,458
If we finish whatever you asked us to do

2372
02:11:12,833 --> 02:11:14,416
you agreed to let us leave.

2373
02:11:16,750 --> 02:11:18,458
I only agreed to release Jeeva.

2374
02:11:19,125 --> 02:11:20,958
I never agreed to release you all.

2375
02:11:27,166 --> 02:11:30,375
Sir, harm me as you may like.

2376
02:11:30,833 --> 02:11:33,500
But please spare them and release Jeeva.

2377
02:11:35,000 --> 02:11:35,875
Sir.

2378
02:11:35,958 --> 02:11:37,916
May I speak to Jeeva one last time?

2379
02:11:45,416 --> 02:11:47,666
- Yes, Sir.
- Pass the phone to the boy.

2380
02:11:47,916 --> 02:11:48,791
Okay, Sir.

2381
02:11:50,125 --> 02:11:52,208
Your father wishes to talk to you
for one last time.

2382
02:11:52,958 --> 02:11:53,916
Here you go!

2383
02:11:55,750 --> 02:11:57,500
Jeeva, this is Dad speaking.

2384
02:11:57,708 --> 02:11:58,791
Tell me, Dad.

2385
02:12:00,000 --> 02:12:01,750
I made a lot of mistakes in life.

2386
02:12:02,708 --> 02:12:04,541
Also, I encouraged you to make mistakes.

2387
02:12:06,375 --> 02:12:09,125
Hereafter in life,
you must not harm or hurt anyone.

2388
02:12:09,416 --> 02:12:10,375
Okay, Dad.

2389
02:12:16,541 --> 02:12:19,333
Jeeva, how many men are around you?

2390
02:12:21,750 --> 02:12:23,583
It's the same two uncles, Dad.

2391
02:12:25,291 --> 02:12:27,333
But they're a bit far from me.

2392
02:12:31,166 --> 02:12:32,916
- Do you remember my number?
- Yes, Dad!

2393
02:12:33,708 --> 02:12:34,708
Then stand up and run!

2394
02:12:36,500 --> 02:12:38,166
Send your location to my number
and keep running.

2395
02:12:38,250 --> 02:12:40,125
- I'll be there soon!
- Okay, Dad!

2396
02:12:43,583 --> 02:12:46,291
<i>When will I be able to participate
in a running race?</i>

2397
02:12:49,291 --> 02:12:50,333
<i>Next year, Son.</i>

2398
02:12:53,375 --> 02:12:54,833
<i>Yay! Jolly!</i>

2399
02:12:57,541 --> 02:13:00,000
- Brother, he's running away.
- Hey, catch him!

2400
02:13:04,791 --> 02:13:06,791
Hey, stop right there!

2401
02:13:20,375 --> 02:13:21,833
Hey, watch out, kid.

2402
02:13:22,166 --> 02:13:23,666
Listen, this school won't work out.

2403
02:13:23,750 --> 02:13:24,625
We need a high recommendation.

2404
02:13:24,708 --> 02:13:26,541
Looks like a rich people's school.
Let's leave.

2405
02:13:26,625 --> 02:13:29,250
I wish to put Jeeva in a school like this.

2406
02:13:29,333 --> 02:13:30,750
Mom, ask him to
find a way to get admission.

2407
02:13:31,208 --> 02:13:33,166
- Ouch!
- Hey, can't you watch out?

2408
02:13:33,250 --> 02:13:34,833
- You'll stop only when you get hurt.
- Get up!

2409
02:13:35,791 --> 02:13:37,000
<i>Admissions are closed, Sir.</i>

2410
02:13:37,291 --> 02:13:39,166
It's hard to find a seat here.
Please look for another school.

2411
02:13:41,916 --> 02:13:43,750
Dad, my leg is not responding.

2412
02:13:44,458 --> 02:13:45,375
Jeeva!

2413
02:13:48,625 --> 02:13:51,708
Sir, why didn't you mention
that your son is physically challenged?

2414
02:13:52,041 --> 02:13:53,333
The admission is still discreetly open.

2415
02:13:53,500 --> 02:13:55,666
Refer to my name and fill out
the form in the admissions office.

2416
02:13:57,000 --> 02:13:59,250
Dad, I'm not lying.
The leg is not responding.

2417
02:14:00,000 --> 02:14:01,000
<i>There's an option.</i>

2418
02:14:01,208 --> 02:14:04,250
<i>We'll say Jeeva is physically challenged
and, get an admission.</i>

2419
02:14:04,375 --> 02:14:06,333
<i>Two years later,
we'll tell them he recovered.</i>

2420
02:14:07,500 --> 02:14:09,916
Jeeva, what Dad did today
was morally wrong.

2421
02:14:11,041 --> 02:14:11,916
I'm sorry.

2422
02:14:13,041 --> 02:14:14,500
No matter what happens in your life...

2423
02:14:15,375 --> 02:14:16,958
you must not make the mistakes I did.

2424
02:14:17,250 --> 02:14:19,416
<i>I've made plenty of mistakes on purpose,
without considering the impact.</i>

2425
02:14:19,833 --> 02:14:23,750
<i>But the first time I felt guilty was
when I made a small boy</i>

2426
02:14:24,250 --> 02:14:26,041
<i>like Jeeva commit a mistake.</i>

2427
02:14:26,666 --> 02:14:28,458
<i>I'm the reason
why Jeeva is in this situation.</i>

2428
02:14:28,541 --> 02:14:30,000
I'm the cause of all the problems.

2429
02:14:30,666 --> 02:14:31,666
I will fix it!

2430
02:14:32,333 --> 02:14:36,333
<i>Kalyana Sundaram, who knew us well,
missed out on one thing.</i>

2431
02:14:36,833 --> 02:14:38,416
<i>He did not know that Jeeva could walk.</i>

2432
02:14:38,750 --> 02:14:41,208
<i>There's a reason why Jeeva
never got off the wheelchair.</i>

2433
02:14:41,875 --> 02:14:43,250
<i>It's because he made a promise to me.</i>

2434
02:14:43,458 --> 02:14:44,916
Will you promise me one thing?

2435
02:14:45,750 --> 02:14:46,791
Except when you're in the house

2436
02:14:48,125 --> 02:14:50,291
wherever you go or until I say so

2437
02:14:51,125 --> 02:14:52,833
you must not get off the wheelchair.

2438
02:14:53,666 --> 02:14:54,625
Promise?

2439
02:14:54,958 --> 02:14:55,875
Promise!

2440
02:14:58,625 --> 02:15:01,333
When we spoke with Jeeva, he said
that only his wheelchair has been chained.

2441
02:15:01,416 --> 02:15:04,541
<i>They have chained my wheelchair
to a pillar, Mom.</i>

2442
02:15:04,750 --> 02:15:05,750
But he's not chained.

2443
02:15:06,458 --> 02:15:08,791
- Also, he mentioned a factory.
- It looks like a factory.

2444
02:15:10,291 --> 02:15:12,041
Hey, don't run!

2445
02:15:12,875 --> 02:15:14,541
Hey, Saravana, open the door.

2446
02:15:29,208 --> 02:15:30,916
<i>I'm going to commit another big scam.</i>

2447
02:15:31,125 --> 02:15:32,458
<i>I need your help.</i>

2448
02:15:46,750 --> 02:15:48,416
Jeeva, the location is
20 minutes from here.

2449
02:15:48,500 --> 02:15:49,916
Jeeva, are you safe?

2450
02:15:50,000 --> 02:15:51,458
I'm safe and running, Dad.

2451
02:15:51,916 --> 02:15:52,791
Sir!

2452
02:15:53,333 --> 02:15:54,208
Do it now!

2453
02:16:03,791 --> 02:16:05,166
My mother was saying...

2454
02:16:05,750 --> 02:16:07,291
only after I get married to you,

2455
02:16:07,666 --> 02:16:09,541
my life will be bright and shinning.

2456
02:16:11,708 --> 02:16:12,583
Mummy?

2457
02:16:14,458 --> 02:16:15,375
Hey!

2458
02:16:17,958 --> 02:16:18,916
Hey!

2459
02:16:20,083 --> 02:16:20,958
Where are you?

2460
02:16:22,958 --> 02:16:23,875
Hey!

2461
02:16:24,291 --> 02:16:25,833
You're looking in the wrong place.

2462
02:16:25,958 --> 02:16:28,250
I'm here, damn it, not there.

2463
02:16:28,416 --> 02:16:29,541
Come and get me!

2464
02:16:29,916 --> 02:16:31,375
Bloody little devil!

2465
02:16:33,041 --> 02:16:34,291
Hey, open the door!

2466
02:16:34,750 --> 02:16:36,833
On that night,
when Kalyana Sundaram called Jeeva...

2467
02:16:36,958 --> 02:16:38,583
the phone displayed Padi Siva.

2468
02:16:38,666 --> 02:16:40,875
So, he must be held captive near Padi.

2469
02:16:40,958 --> 02:16:42,125
Suppose he's not in Padi?

2470
02:16:43,666 --> 02:16:44,583
- Hello?
- Hello!

2471
02:16:44,666 --> 02:16:46,166
<i>- Sir, it's Saravana speaking.</i>
- Saravana!

2472
02:16:47,041 --> 02:16:48,208
- Is it really you?
<i>- Yes, Sir.</i>

2473
02:16:48,333 --> 02:16:50,125
Where were you all these years?

2474
02:16:50,333 --> 02:16:53,375
I trusted you so much.

2475
02:16:53,583 --> 02:16:56,291
At least you could've told me.

2476
02:16:56,416 --> 02:16:59,250
Fine, tell me now.
Or else my head will explode.

2477
02:16:59,333 --> 02:17:01,125
Tell me what exactly happened.

2478
02:17:01,750 --> 02:17:04,708
Saravana, the entire city of Chennai
will be blacked out.

2479
02:17:04,791 --> 02:17:07,833
To restart the electricity,

2480
02:17:07,916 --> 02:17:10,083
it'll take another 20 minutes.

2481
02:17:10,416 --> 02:17:12,041
Okay, enjoy!

2482
02:17:12,125 --> 02:17:14,208
- Enjoy yourself.
- Thank you, Darling.

2483
02:17:14,291 --> 02:17:16,625
Hey, you're always welcome.

2484
02:17:16,875 --> 02:17:17,875
Bye!

2485
02:17:17,958 --> 02:17:20,916
Please ask him to drive slowly.

2486
02:17:24,333 --> 02:17:26,416
Hey, won't you keep the car ready to go?

2487
02:17:27,291 --> 02:17:29,583
- Hey, drive carefully.
- Hey, don't fall on me.

2488
02:17:34,250 --> 02:17:35,500
Hey, drive slowly.

2489
02:17:38,250 --> 02:17:39,250
I caught you!

2490
02:17:40,541 --> 02:17:41,458
Get lost!

2491
02:17:44,375 --> 02:17:45,875
Mom, ask him to drive more slowly.

2492
02:17:46,333 --> 02:17:47,875
On, on! On, on, on!

2493
02:17:56,500 --> 02:17:57,375
Jeeva!

2494
02:18:01,958 --> 02:18:02,833
Oh, God!

2495
02:18:04,541 --> 02:18:05,500
- Come here.
- Jeeva!

2496
02:18:05,791 --> 02:18:06,666
Dad!

2497
02:18:07,583 --> 02:18:08,500
Hey!

2498
02:18:15,583 --> 02:18:16,458
I'm sorry, Son.

2499
02:18:18,458 --> 02:18:19,791
From now on, I won't be late.

2500
02:18:19,958 --> 02:18:20,833
Okay!

2501
02:18:29,916 --> 02:18:31,458
Hello, Rohit, where are you?

2502
02:18:32,000 --> 02:18:34,000
- Yes, Kalyan, Sir.
- The machine is not working

2503
02:18:34,083 --> 02:18:35,666
But the water is running.
What do I do?

2504
02:18:35,750 --> 02:18:38,000
It's simple.
There's a motor switch next to it.

2505
02:18:38,083 --> 02:18:38,958
Switch it off.

2506
02:18:39,041 --> 02:18:40,833
- Automatically, the water will stop.
- What?

2507
02:18:41,666 --> 02:18:43,166
Did you say to switch off
the motor switch to stop the water?

2508
02:18:43,250 --> 02:18:45,791
Hey, the machine is not working.
What do I do now?

2509
02:18:45,875 --> 02:18:49,333
When the tank overflows,
switching off the motor is the solution.

2510
02:18:49,625 --> 02:18:51,625
Hello, Sir, are you still connected?

2511
02:18:51,750 --> 02:18:55,000
Hey, I think he froze for the second time.
Clearly explain it to him.

2512
02:18:55,083 --> 02:18:57,375
Hello, Sir, this is Saravanan speaking.

2513
02:18:57,541 --> 02:18:58,875
<i>What happened?
Are you confused?</i>

2514
02:18:59,166 --> 02:19:00,125
Is your head spinning?

2515
02:19:03,791 --> 02:19:05,583
The toll scam is not
a quick get-in-and-out scam.

2516
02:19:05,708 --> 02:19:08,083
So, we'll have ample time
to find a way to save Jeeva.

2517
02:19:08,166 --> 02:19:10,791
Moreover, to divert Kalyana Sundaram

2518
02:19:10,958 --> 02:19:12,625
we would need another dummy idea.

2519
02:19:12,791 --> 02:19:14,958
As per our plan,
we need an electrical engineer.

2520
02:19:15,541 --> 02:19:16,416
Meet him.

2521
02:19:16,625 --> 02:19:18,500
<i>Could you please cover for me?
I'll be back soon.</i>

2522
02:19:19,083 --> 02:19:20,416
Will Kalyana Sundaram believe him?

2523
02:19:20,708 --> 02:19:21,750
What's his weakness?

2524
02:19:21,958 --> 02:19:23,708
<i>I started small-time betting.</i>

2525
02:19:24,041 --> 02:19:24,916
<i>I won!</i>

2526
02:19:25,333 --> 02:19:26,250
Gambling!

2527
02:19:26,375 --> 02:19:28,250
Quick Money and gambling are the same.

2528
02:19:28,375 --> 02:19:31,416
<i>Money earned through quick methods
always poses danger.</i>

2529
02:19:31,875 --> 02:19:33,083
It's easy to convince them.

2530
02:19:33,416 --> 02:19:34,416
You wait and watch.

2531
02:19:36,041 --> 02:19:39,500
This is a coffee tray, this is the motor,
heater, and this is the meter.

2532
02:19:39,583 --> 02:19:40,458
Heater?

2533
02:19:41,250 --> 02:19:43,208
It's junk art.
I'll give a fantastic presentation.

2534
02:19:43,291 --> 02:19:44,208
Hey, Baldie!

2535
02:19:44,583 --> 02:19:47,333
- Do you know who Kalyana Sundaram is?
- He did mention.

2536
02:19:47,416 --> 02:19:48,500
He's a marriage broker, right?

2537
02:19:49,458 --> 02:19:52,166
Dude, do you ever speak the truth?

2538
02:19:52,625 --> 02:19:54,750
Ji, shall I paint the heater pink?

2539
02:19:55,166 --> 02:19:56,041
Pink?

2540
02:19:57,250 --> 02:19:58,250
White is good enough.

2541
02:19:59,458 --> 02:20:00,916
We could bring major changes

2542
02:20:01,625 --> 02:20:03,333
in the Indian economy, sir.

2543
02:20:08,583 --> 02:20:12,416
You see, this wire travels all the way
and is connected to his machine.

2544
02:20:12,500 --> 02:20:13,666
That's why the three lights are on.

2545
02:20:13,916 --> 02:20:15,083
He's the best scientist, Sir.

2546
02:20:16,125 --> 02:20:18,375
<i>The water is enough to power it.</i>

2547
02:20:18,625 --> 02:20:20,583
My Boss is interested in your project.

2548
02:20:20,666 --> 02:20:22,541
- Five crores.
- We can push it till 20 crores.

2549
02:20:22,625 --> 02:20:24,625
- 40 crores.
- 50 crores.

2550
02:20:26,541 --> 02:20:29,416
Saravana, you may have cheated me on this.

2551
02:20:29,500 --> 02:20:31,708
Don't forget you committed a huge scam.

2552
02:20:31,791 --> 02:20:33,416
You can't easily escape from it.

2553
02:20:33,500 --> 02:20:36,250
This time you're messing with
the Central Government.

2554
02:20:36,333 --> 02:20:38,125
<i>They will be on to you wherever you go.</i>

2555
02:20:38,208 --> 02:20:41,041
Guys, for the third time, I got Joker.

2556
02:20:41,666 --> 02:20:44,500
We won!
Explain the same to the potty mouth.

2557
02:20:47,750 --> 02:20:48,875
Sir, let me explain something.

2558
02:20:49,875 --> 02:20:52,166
Actually, we were going to
spare you and leave.

2559
02:20:52,250 --> 02:20:54,791
But only after we arrived
we learnt something about you.

2560
02:20:55,250 --> 02:20:57,916
<i>In my service, I let many criminals,
like you, escape.</i>

2561
02:20:58,000 --> 02:21:01,916
<i>Only after hearing that did we
have a strong suspicion of you.</i>

2562
02:21:02,541 --> 02:21:06,958
<i>Later at reporter Arnaa's place,
I found a file named Sabari.</i>

2563
02:21:07,875 --> 02:21:10,625
<i>That file contained evidence
of how my friend Sabari died.</i>

2564
02:21:11,875 --> 02:21:15,500
<i>Only after I arrived here
did I learn that you killed Sabari.</i>

2565
02:21:16,916 --> 02:21:18,666
<i>During an illegal business deal,</i>

2566
02:21:18,750 --> 02:21:21,416
<i>he was shot dead in a crossfire
between two gangs.</i>

2567
02:21:23,000 --> 02:21:23,875
Bye, dude!

2568
02:21:25,916 --> 02:21:29,458
For safety, I always save a copy
of whatever I record.

2569
02:21:29,541 --> 02:21:31,541
Did you see?
Thank your stars I was here.

2570
02:21:31,625 --> 02:21:34,041
If it were someone else,
all of you would've been on <i>Flash news.</i>

2571
02:21:37,583 --> 02:21:38,916
This is Sabari's daughter.

2572
02:21:40,125 --> 02:21:41,000
Grandpa!

2573
02:21:42,166 --> 02:21:43,583
I'm telling the truth.

2574
02:21:44,208 --> 02:21:45,375
It's with Sabari.

2575
02:21:45,541 --> 02:21:47,916
Whenever I ask him about the money
he brings up Sabari.

2576
02:21:48,125 --> 02:21:50,041
- What do we do, Sir?
- Let them escape.

2577
02:21:51,750 --> 02:21:54,166
That means our money
is with Kalyana Sundaram.

2578
02:21:54,791 --> 02:21:56,916
I alone would've been trouble for him.

2579
02:21:57,500 --> 02:21:58,708
Imagine if we all come together.

2580
02:22:01,666 --> 02:22:03,166
Shall we show him our prowess?

2581
02:22:03,250 --> 02:22:05,208
We never wanted to return to Manglapuram.

2582
02:22:05,833 --> 02:22:07,333
But you brought us here.

2583
02:22:07,416 --> 02:22:08,791
But in a way, you did a good thing.

2584
02:22:09,166 --> 02:22:12,833
After learning that you're the reason
why our lives were ruined...

2585
02:22:13,083 --> 02:22:14,875
how could we let you go unscathed?

2586
02:22:14,958 --> 02:22:17,541
<i>Breaking news!
Retired Inspector Kalyana Sundaram,</i>

2587
02:22:17,625 --> 02:22:22,166
<i>installed a fake toll booth in Magalapuram
and swindled crores.</i>

2588
02:22:22,250 --> 02:22:23,333
We need to establish a paper trail

2589
02:22:23,416 --> 02:22:25,208
connecting Kalyana Sundaram
to the toll booth scam.

2590
02:22:25,291 --> 02:22:27,500
We're going to record everything
using this hidden cam.

2591
02:22:29,416 --> 02:22:31,916
<i>Fake toll? It's a fantastic plan!</i>

2592
02:22:32,000 --> 02:22:34,166
Oh, so Kalyana Sundaram is a fraud too.

2593
02:22:34,250 --> 02:22:35,708
Is Kalyana Sundaram a fraud too?

2594
02:22:35,791 --> 02:22:37,166
{\an8}Seems like he's a fraud.

2595
02:22:37,250 --> 02:22:38,166
I can't believe I trusted him.

2596
02:22:38,250 --> 02:22:40,958
So, the Pulp-cane Kalyana Sundaram
is a fraud too.

2597
02:22:41,833 --> 02:22:44,125
{\an8}<i>In addition,
we have information linking him</i>

2598
02:22:44,208 --> 02:22:46,625
<i>to a new scam involving hydro-generators.</i>

2599
02:22:46,708 --> 02:22:49,125
<i>Based on this information,
the police arrested him.</i>

2600
02:22:50,125 --> 02:22:51,208
I hear noise in the background.

2601
02:22:52,333 --> 02:22:53,250
I think they've arrived!

2602
02:22:54,041 --> 02:22:56,166
As you mentioned,
the Central Government

2603
02:22:56,791 --> 02:22:57,750
has arrived.

2604
02:22:59,833 --> 02:23:00,958
Hey, Wedding-Sundaram!

2605
02:23:01,333 --> 02:23:04,250
If we were the talk of the town,
you're the talk of the country.

2606
02:23:04,416 --> 02:23:05,875
You always quote one thing.

2607
02:23:06,083 --> 02:23:08,625
"Being cheated is a greater sin
than cheating."

2608
02:23:09,333 --> 02:23:10,416
Now, let me share a quote.

2609
02:23:11,208 --> 02:23:13,916
"It's wrong to cheat.
It's just as wrong to get cheated."

2610
02:23:14,000 --> 02:23:17,250
You guys made a mistake.
I won't let you off the hook.

2611
02:23:29,958 --> 02:23:30,875
Does this mean...

2612
02:23:31,791 --> 02:23:33,708
we have reformed?

2613
02:23:39,000 --> 02:23:40,083
Bad mother.

2614
02:23:50,791 --> 02:23:53,750
<i>Don't deceive, deceive no one</i>

2615
02:23:53,833 --> 02:23:54,708
<i>Brother!</i>

2616
02:23:54,791 --> 02:23:57,708
<i>But do not be deceived</i>

2617
02:23:57,791 --> 02:23:58,666
<i>By trusting!</i>

2618
02:23:58,750 --> 02:24:01,541
<i>Don't deceive, deceive no one</i>

2619
02:24:01,625 --> 02:24:02,500
<i>Brother!</i>

2620
02:24:02,583 --> 02:24:06,000
<i>But do not be deceived</i>

2621
02:24:06,833 --> 02:24:09,708
<i>Filled with lies of every hue</i>

2622
02:24:10,250 --> 02:24:14,125
<i>He crafted this earthen realm</i>

2623
02:24:14,500 --> 02:24:17,541
<i>Sowing countless little hopes</i>

2624
02:24:17,916 --> 02:24:21,250
<i>He let us run, only to block our way</i>

2625
02:24:21,333 --> 02:24:24,125
<i>And the tale ended there</i>

2626
02:24:28,916 --> 02:24:33,125
{\an8}<i>I sincerely apologize
for all the trouble I caused you.</i>

2627
02:24:33,208 --> 02:24:35,291
<i>I realized my mistake very late.</i>

2628
02:24:35,375 --> 02:24:36,791
<i>I hope you can forgive me.</i>

2629
02:24:36,875 --> 02:24:38,416
- Sorry.
- Saravanan.

2630
02:24:38,500 --> 02:24:40,375
- Mithra.
- Jacky and Janaki.

2631
02:24:43,875 --> 02:24:44,791
<i>Brother!</i>

2632
02:24:47,666 --> 02:24:48,625
<i>Brother!</i>

2633
02:24:49,791 --> 02:24:50,958
Hey, Satha!

2634
02:24:51,583 --> 02:24:52,583
<i>Brother!</i>

2635
02:24:55,083 --> 02:24:57,541
He thinks he is Paul Walker. Get lost!

2636
02:25:00,250 --> 02:25:03,166
<i>Filled with lies of every hue</i>

2637
02:25:03,625 --> 02:25:07,291
<i>He crafted this earthen realm</i>

2638
02:25:07,916 --> 02:25:10,875
<i>Sowing countless little hopes</i>

2639
02:25:11,291 --> 02:25:14,583
<i>He let us run, only to block our way</i>

2640
02:25:14,666 --> 02:25:17,583
<i>And the tale ended there</i>

2641
02:25:48,375 --> 02:25:50,291
{\an8}- Dude, I have some good news.
<i>- Tell me.</i>

2642
02:25:50,625 --> 02:25:52,583
{\an8}Sudha Illam is now Satha Illam.

2643
02:25:54,791 --> 02:25:57,833
{\an8}Hey, I'm trusting you
and taking a loan against this house.

2644
02:25:58,291 --> 02:26:00,875
{\an8}If I miss even one EMI,
they'll come after me.

2645
02:26:01,083 --> 02:26:03,208
{\an8}- Bear this in mind.
<i>- Hey, I won't miss it.</i>

2646
02:26:03,291 --> 02:26:04,416
{\an8}<i>I'll make the payments on time.</i>

2647
